WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.729
“This is impossible!”

00:00:01.729 --> 00:00:06.890
The SCP site director wasn’t normally a
calm or cheerful man, but the researcher had

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:10.970
rarely seen him as angry as he was right now.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:15.620
His face turned a deep beet red as he scanned
the documents on his desk before he asked

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:21.250
how months of valuable research on this subject
had suddenly gone blank, the data was completely

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.250
gone.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:27.490
The researcher gulped nervously, hoping a
demotion wasn’t in his future, and nodded.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.160
How could this be possible.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.870
This was an experienced researcher who should
have been taking all of the necessary precautions.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:38.660
Could the being they were studying somehow
have erased all these documents himself?

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.290
That’s just what the researcher had been
trying to find out for months, with hours

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.880
and hours spent trying to learn the extent
of its abilities.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.880
“Well?

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:48.880
Where are they?”

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.260
the site director asked.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.899
“I want everything you have!”

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:57.149
The researcher dropped a print-out of their
research on the mysterious subject’s abilities

00:00:57.149 --> 00:00:58.949
on the director’s desk.

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:01.840
Every relevant line read “Data Lost”.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.119
The director let out a deep sigh.

00:01:04.119 --> 00:01:09.520
He wanted to hear everything the researcher
knew, well everything he could remember at

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.240
least, from the beginning.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:17.470
The researcher sat town and began to relay
everything he could about SCP-343, which some

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:21.380
of the other researchers had started to refer
to by the nickname…

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.509
God.

00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:28.490
SCP-343 was first sighted in Prague, just
an unassuming older man wandering the streets.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:33.340
He seemed completely normal to everyone who
passed him by - until he decided he was tired

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.869
of staying on the ground.

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:39.970
An SCP agent stationed in the area noticed
the old man disappear from the streets as

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:44.479
if he was blinking out of existence - only
to appear on a rooftop nearby.

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:48.990
The local SCP teams were marshalled, and they
had soon tracked down what seemed to be a

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.040
very powerful specimen.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.200
But SCP-343 didn’t seem concerned.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.450
He reacted calmly when detained by the foundation
and went with them willingly.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:03.350
He was detained in a standard holding cell
for interrogation and examination, but he

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:06.180
seemed completely at ease with his sudden
confinement.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:11.840
It would soon become clear that this ordinary
old man was anything but.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.230
Doctors Beck and Ndlovu were brought in to
consult on the SCP’s classification, and

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:19.300
that’s when the first anomalies began.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:24.170
Their assessments matched initially, but when
it came time to describe him physically, things

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.340
took a strange turn.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.870
Older male, seemingly non-descript and with
no unusual physical features.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.770
Caucasian in appearance.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:36.870
Doctor Ndlovu was confused by what Doctor
Beck was describing in his report.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.800
This man was clearly black.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.510
The two doctors quarrelled, unable to square
their differing perceptions.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:47.440
They decided to bring in a third impartial
view to settle it - their fellow researcher,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.440
Dr. Wan.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.150
She didn’t take long before coming back
with her assessment.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.170
Older male, seemingly non-descript and with
no unusual physical features.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:58.560
Asian in appearance, possibly Chinese.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:04.390
Whatever SCP-343 was, he seemed to be perceived
by each staff member as close in appearance

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.880
to their own race.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.510
But that was only the start of the anomalies
surrounding the old man in the holding cell.

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:15.810
Dr. Beck started making regular visits to
the mysterious man, and in their first interview,

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:20.120
he asked the old man who he was and how he
came by his abilities.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.810
The old man had a simple response.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:24.630
“I created this universe.”

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:29.050
Dr. Beck stifled a laugh and decided to indulge
the old man’s delusion.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.879
It was a fascinating claim, but could he prove
it?

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:38.209
Without another word, SCP-343 got up from
his chair, laughed, and turned around and

00:03:38.209 --> 00:03:41.470
walked through the solid wall in the holding
cell and disappeared.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:45.430
Dr. Beck was about to hit the panic button
and marshall the facility’s security to

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:50.560
find him when the strange man reappeared,
walking through the solid wall.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.640
The only thing that was different?

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.599
He was holding a hamburger, which he sat down
and enjoyed.

00:03:55.599 --> 00:04:00.739
The facility quickly went on lockdown and
a full investigation was done into how SCP-343

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:02.610
breached containment.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:07.561
But there was no evidence of any security
breach, no failures in containment, and no

00:04:07.561 --> 00:04:10.439
evidence of any other cells failing.

00:04:10.439 --> 00:04:15.849
SCP-343 hadn’t broken through the security
- he had just ignored it, as if it wasn’t

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:17.110
there at all.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:21.449
When questioned about how he had gone on his
hamburger run, he simply repeated his belief

00:04:21.449 --> 00:04:25.310
that he was God - in between bites of his
fast food treat.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:30.000
This would be far from the only time strange
things happened around SCP-343.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.540
SCP containment cells are as secure as they
need to be, but even the least-strict containment

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.500
isn’t known for its decor.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:43.150
Which is why Dr. Beck was in for a surprise
the next time he paid a visit to SCP-343.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:48.790
The bare-bones cell now looked like a comfortable
home, decorated in Old English fashions.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:53.710
The scientists assumed that SCP-343 had been
making many more trips out of his cell to

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:59.160
get accessories to feel more at home - but
that didn’t explain all the changes to the

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.160
cell.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.640
No one could explain how he had installed
a roaring fireplace in the containment cell

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:08.199
- and everyone who entered could swear the
cell looked many times bigger than any other

00:05:08.199 --> 00:05:09.580
cell in the facility.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:15.199
SCP-343 wasn’t just breaking containment
- he now seemed to be breaking the laws of

00:05:15.199 --> 00:05:17.110
physics in the facility.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:22.889
The rules of the SCP containment facility
didn’t seem to be a concern to SCP-343,

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:26.910
but there was one thing he didn’t seem to
want to do - escape.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:32.400
After every sudden exit, he would always return
to his personal cell and treat it as his home.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:37.220
When interviewed by staff members, he was
polite but vague, and everyone seemed to enjoy

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.220
talking to him.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:43.780
It was decided to keep him on site, not attempt
to increase his security, but restrict access

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:48.711
and keep his room guarded at all times to
ensure only researchers with Level 3 access

00:05:48.711 --> 00:05:51.380
and above were allowed to meet with him.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.530
But God works in mysterious ways.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:06:00.410
Minimal Security Site 17 was one of the less-restrictive
SCP containment sites, hosting anomalies that

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:04.840
could be safely contained and weren’t likely
to mount violent escapes.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:10.490
But as in every SCP facility, security was
still taken seriously and only those with

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.380
proper clearance could interact with the subjects.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:17.300
So why did SCP-343 seem impossible to guard?

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:21.530
While only Level 3 clearance and above were
allowed in, the guards assigned to protect

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:25.090
the entrance all seemed to fall down on the
job.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:29.960
Security Officer James, who was supposed to
be keeping people out of SCP-343’s cell,

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:35.210
had instead let in multiple visitors in addition
to dropping in several times himself.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:39.310
When questioned on why he had gone against
orders and done so, he simply replied that

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:45.020
343 seemed lonely and was so happy every time
he got company that it just seemed like the

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.400
right thing to do.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:50.780
The security guard was reassigned and new
ones were brought in - but history repeated

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:51.990
itself.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:56.960
Guards were given stricter instructions to
minimize exposure - but SCP-343’s presence

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.710
always seemed to influence them anyway.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:04.150
His containment cell was a revolving door,
with staff members at the facility entering

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.480
regularly for friendly conversations.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:11.000
Dr. Beck decided it was time to take matters
into his own hands.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:17.210
He would meet with SCP-343 one-on-one and
express how dangerous these security breaches

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:18.210
were.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:21.930
He would try to convince the mysterious being
that he needed to stop influencing the minds

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:26.860
of the guards watching him, or the facility
would have to look into new measures to contain

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:27.860
him.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:33.300
Dr. Beck entered the containment cell and
had a long conversation with SCP-343, and

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:37.990
when he emerged...he had a big smile on his
face, like he had just finished a reunion

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.180
with an old friend.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.550
He gave the current guard a friendly clap
on the back, and told him not to worry so

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.190
much about security.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:49.080
After all, nothing bad was going to happen
from letting people at the facility visit

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.020
SCP-343, right?

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.930
He wasn’t dangerous in any way.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:57.060
He also said that security should bring him
anything he requests so he would feel less

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.069
need to leave his cell.

00:07:59.069 --> 00:08:04.780
Minimal Security Site 17 soon became a model
SCP facility, with morale being the highest

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:10.680
of any site - with most giving the credit
to the presence of SCP-343.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:14.720
Employees generally make daily visits to his
chambers, and he seems to have an encyclopedic

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:19.440
knowledge of anything they want to talk about
- including things he should have no way of

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.460
knowing.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:24.840
Guards no longer quit their posts or break
protocol, as their only real duty is to keep

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:30.699
track of who meets with SCP-343 so they can
be interviewed and debriefed after.

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:34.690
Everyone’s conversation is different, but
they all report being in a better mood after

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.900
leaving than when they came in.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:43.440
No further information is available on SCP-343’s
origins, the full extent of his powers, or

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:48.010
whether he is telling the truth about being
the God who created the universe.

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:51.560
The site director rubbed his temples after
hearing the researcher’s explanation.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:56.339
“So what you’re telling me is that we
have an uncontained, highly powerful SCP that

00:08:56.339 --> 00:09:01.020
has not only been breaking containment whenever
it wants, but has managed to destroy all the

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.440
files regarding the research on it?”

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.600
The researcher’s answer was yes.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:10.260
However, the situation at Site 17 seemed to
be stable, and they had come up with a plan

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:15.649
that should help to maximize the positive
effect SCP-343 has on the facility.

00:09:15.649 --> 00:09:20.040
They were even hypothesizing that staff from
other sites and even certain anomalies could

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.860
be pacified by 343’s presence.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:24.810
The site director wasn’t impressed though.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:28.900
He wanted the researcher to go back to the
drawing board and redo the research.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:33.029
After all, if all the files were blank, how
could they ever learn how to properly contain

00:09:33.029 --> 00:09:34.029
it?

00:09:34.029 --> 00:09:37.540
That’s what the C in SCP stood for after
all - containment.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:41.269
The researcher finally had to stand up to
the director though, and told them that it

00:09:41.269 --> 00:09:42.680
wasn’t a good idea.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:47.190
That they had already tried everything to
contain SCP-343, but that it wasn’t that

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:51.930
he broke containment, it was as if he didn’t
even acknowledge that an attempt had been

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.310
made to contain him.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:58.500
He was omnipotent, aware of things he shouldn’t,
and able to do things that broke the laws

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.210
of physics without breaking a sweat.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:06.220
There was no evidence that this was God, the
creator of the universe as he claimed to be,

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:10.720
but there also wasn’t any evidence yet to
conclusively prove he wasn’t.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:15.300
The researcher’s best guess was that this
was a powerful reality bender whose abilities

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:19.950
knew no limits, and that the only reason he
was staying in the facility was because he

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:26.050
wanted to, and doing anything to change that
might cause him to change his benevolent ways.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.240
The director sighed.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:31.480
As much as he hated to admit it, his researcher
was making good points.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.860
He wanted to meet SCP-343 personally.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.860
But did he need to know anything first?

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:40.490
“Well, sir…” the researcher replied,
“he likes hamburgers.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.820
But beyond that, he’ll take care of the
rest.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:47.010
He’s right where we left him, in his home
- waiting for his next guest.”

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:52.710
Over fifty men and women, clad in red robes,
kneel before an unholy altar.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:59.360
They chant and mutter indecipherable words
- words of cruelty and madness… of obsession

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.880
and sacrilege.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:03.970
Not long ago, these were regular people.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:10.510
Computer technicians, teachers, plumbers,
construction workers, accountants.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:14.950
This was before they fell under the ungodly
influence of a new ruler.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:19.920
The center of this makeshift place of worship
was once a normal school gymnasium, but it’s

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:22.620
now the home of a huge statue.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.220
A humanoid being, wreathed in tentacles.

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:31.950
Its head is more like a squid or cuttlefish
than anything resembling an actual human face.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:36.840
While he’s known to the cultists as the
Tentacled God, the beast they worship is known

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:43.500
to the SCP Foundation as SCP - 2662, and he
sits in the belly of one of their expansive

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:47.350
containment facilities, locked away from the
world.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:52.470
But not for long, if his devoted followers
have anything to say about it.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:58.970
This is their god, all-powerful and unchanging,
and when it comes to springing him from containment,

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:03.510
no tactic is too vile or underhanded to get
the job done.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:09.130
Their mortal leader and high-priest, a man
in a purple robe calling himself Brother Marsh,

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.320
walks among their crouched forms.

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:16.699
He whispers instructions for the great day
of liberation that’s soon to come, providing

00:12:16.699 --> 00:12:18.589
everyone plays their part.

00:12:18.589 --> 00:12:23.829
It’s a plan months in the making - and one
that, if it goes off without a hitch, could

00:12:23.829 --> 00:12:26.910
free their monstrous god into the world.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:32.779
They would strike at the very heart of their
enemy, The SCP Foundation, when they least

00:12:32.779 --> 00:12:36.579
expect it, and nothing shall stand in their
way.

00:12:36.579 --> 00:12:39.680
How could they lose when they have a god on
their side?

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:44.830
But why did all these normal people become
violent zealots for squid-faced deity?

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.870
It all began with a dream.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:52.240
To those who experienced these dreams, they
felt more like prophecies, premonitions of

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.100
the glorious horrors to come.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:58.639
A red sky, billions dead and billions more
enslaved.

00:12:58.639 --> 00:13:05.459
A dark silhouette on the horizon - Their Tentacled
God, holding dominion over all.

00:13:05.459 --> 00:13:08.420
At first, it just seemed like a strange nightmare.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:13.430
The ones who experienced it woke up shaken
and afraid, hoping to shake the images from

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:14.430
their mind.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:16.220
But they couldn’t.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:18.140
Every night, the nightmare would return.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:24.839
They’d see the images - the red sky, the
dead and enslaved, the Tentacled God.

00:13:24.839 --> 00:13:29.550
And after a while it would come to them even
when they weren’t asleep, eventually happening

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:31.940
whenever they closed their eyes.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:38.750
Little by little, this scene stopped looking
so hideous… and started to look glorious.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:43.930
They felt his presence in their minds, slowly
pushing them towards their inevitable future.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:49.110
They started to realize that they wanted him
to rule over the universe, and to experience

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:51.139
the honor of serving him.

00:13:51.139 --> 00:13:56.139
Many of them abandoned their homes and families
- leaving their friends and loved ones left

00:13:56.139 --> 00:13:59.490
to worry that they’d gone insane.

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:02.699
In their eyes, they were safer than they’d
ever been.

00:14:02.699 --> 00:14:04.880
They finally had purpose.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:09.310
They were working in service of something
far greater than themselves.

00:14:09.310 --> 00:14:13.399
The influence of the tentacled god drew them
closer to one another.

00:14:13.399 --> 00:14:18.540
They would meet in secret, exchanging information
from the prophecies their ruler sent them

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:19.839
in their dreams.

00:14:19.839 --> 00:14:23.779
They worshipped together, building altars
and idols to congregate around.

00:14:23.779 --> 00:14:28.589
They performed dark blood rituals, involving
human and animal sacrifice.

00:14:28.589 --> 00:14:33.680
It was when Brother Marsh, The Anointed One,
arrived to guide them towards their true mission

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.079
that things kicked into high gear.

00:14:37.079 --> 00:14:41.589
Just three months prior, Brother Marsh had
been an office drone working in data entry

00:14:41.589 --> 00:14:46.880
for a large insurance company, before the
Tentacled God invaded his thoughts with a

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:54.699
simple message: “FREE ME, AND THE NEW WORLD
I CREATE SHALL BE YOUR PLAYGROUND.”

00:14:54.699 --> 00:14:59.760
Since then, he’d devoted himself completely
to the cause, quitting his job and maxing

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:06.060
out his credit cards to help fund his new
life’s purpose - infiltrating the SCP Foundation,

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:10.180
and releasing his inhuman ruler from its imprisonment.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:15.720
That was the single goal he united the cultists
under: Freedom for the Tentacled God.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:19.680
And at long last, they had all the pieces
in place to strike.

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:24.500
They’d finally gathered the necessary intel
to subvert the will of the most powerful secret

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:26.579
organization on earth.

00:15:26.579 --> 00:15:32.009
Even the strongest institution is made of
people, and people are weak.

00:15:32.009 --> 00:15:36.399
Unlike the almighty Tentacled God, people
could be broken.

00:15:36.399 --> 00:15:42.649
The people in question were Kelly Thompson,
Sidney Levitt, Jordan Brosh, Dr. Juan Gutierrez,

00:15:42.649 --> 00:15:43.649
and Gillian Larson.

00:15:43.649 --> 00:15:48.511
Dr. Juan Gutierrez was a researcher with Level
3 clearance on the site where the Tentacled

00:15:48.511 --> 00:15:50.470
God was being contained.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:54.930
Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were both Security
Officers charged with verifying personnel

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.570
clearance on site.

00:15:56.570 --> 00:16:01.920
Kelly Thompson was a member of Site Administration
with research authorization powers, and Gillian

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:07.020
Larson was a research assistant who often
collaborated with Dr. Gutierrez.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:14.730
These five were the key to getting access
to SCP-2662 and bringing their plan to fruition.

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:19.290
Normally, personnel dossiers on people working
for the Foundation were highly confidential,

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.940
but the Devotees of the Tentacled God had
their ways.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:27.759
They had a number of computer experts in their
ranks more than capable of hacking in and

00:16:27.759 --> 00:16:32.460
pulling some basic information off of Foundation
servers without being detected.

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:37.399
For the other information they needed they
turned to some good, old-fashioned torture,

00:16:37.399 --> 00:16:41.940
which is often the most effective method when
you need some quick results.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:47.350
Of course, while the cult’s grip on sanity
may have been a little tenuous, they weren’t

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:48.350
stupid.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:52.170
While gathering their intel, they also made
sure to find out what exactly they were up

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:53.760
against.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:17:01.139
SCP-2662 was being held in a humanoid containment
cell, and guarded by on-site Task Force TAU-9,

00:17:01.139 --> 00:17:04.130
better known as the “Belligerent Bodyguards.”

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:09.360
These aren’t lazy, donut-chomping mall cops
- these are a heavily trained, heavily armed

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:10.800
fighting force.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:16.280
Though the cultists had one thing that these
Foundation soldiers didn’t: The element

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:17.870
of surprise.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:22.089
For everything to go off perfectly, Brother
Marsh’s plans would have to be executed

00:17:22.089 --> 00:17:26.120
within a single day, and they were already
on the clock.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:32.770
TAU-9 had been charged with tracking down
any new SCP - 2662 cults and dismantling them,

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:36.740
and Brother Marsh knew that it was only a
matter of time before the Foundation tracked

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.570
them down and did the same to them.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:44.620
If they wanted any chance of freeing the Tentacled
God, then they needed to strike quickly and

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:47.390
with overwhelming force.

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:53.660
The SCP-2662 worshippers were able to secure
the addresses of the five key Foundation personnel,

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:59.470
and station members outside each of them - including
one who could realistically imitate each.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:04.809
They waited for night to fall, and broke into
each of their homes as they slept.

00:18:04.809 --> 00:18:09.780
What followed was a sequence of ruthless and
efficient murders done in the cause of freeing

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:10.780
their god.

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:13.990
Dr. Gutierrez was shot in the head while he
slept.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:18.340
Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were both stabbed
to death before either even realized what

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:19.340
was happening.

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:24.630
Thompson, who’d gotten up to use the bathroom,
went down in a hail of machine gun fire.

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:28.620
Gillian Larson had seen that masked figures
were breaking into her home and attempted

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:32.510
to flee, but was caught and beaten to death
by cultists in her hallway.

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:37.320
It was a strange irony that people whose day
jobs entailed working with some of the most

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:42.960
dangerous and nightmarish anomalies imaginable
were murdered in their homes by nothing more

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:45.390
than regular humans.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:51.140
So far, Brother Marsh’s plan had gone perfectly,
with all five key personnel murdered within

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:52.690
a two minute period.

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:57.390
Next, the selected doppelgängers stole clothes
from their victims’ closets and were handed

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:59.890
the correct forged documentation.

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:04.409
The next morning, each replacement began their
journeys to the site where the Tentacled God

00:19:04.409 --> 00:19:09.170
was being contained, while the rest of the
cult armed themselves in preparation for their

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:11.720
own part in the plan.

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:16.370
Nobody at the Foundation seemed to notice
anything amiss when the five arrived on site.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:20.500
When you work for the SCP Foundation, more
mental energy is devoted to following the

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:26.020
rules that keep you alive than to memorizing
the faces of all your co-workers and each

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:32.160
one slipped neatly into position, disappearing
into the familiarity of office life.

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:37.130
But, infiltrating the site was one thing,
getting past the Belligerent Bodyguards and

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:41.120
into the cell of the Tentacled God would be
another thing entirely.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:45.360
That’s where the rest of the cult would
come into play.

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:49.260
Heavily armed with whatever firearms they
could get their hands on, the rest of the

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:54.210
Devotees of the Tentacled God - Brother Marsh
included - would attack the containment site

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:55.659
head-on.

00:19:55.659 --> 00:19:59.909
In the ensuing chaos, the five cultists who
had already infiltrated the site could take

00:19:59.909 --> 00:20:04.350
advantage of the distraction, and break into
the containment chamber.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:05.350
It was perfect.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:10.049
They’d launch their attack from the outside…
and from within.

00:20:10.049 --> 00:20:13.559
When Brother Marsh declared that the time
was right, the assault began.

00:20:13.559 --> 00:20:18.179
A legion of gun-wielding cultists seemed to
spring out of nowhere and started shooting

00:20:18.179 --> 00:20:21.480
up the warehouse that was a front for the
containment site.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:26.450
The site quickly mobilized guards and task
force members to take on the sudden threat,

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:31.070
and just as Brother Marsh had anticipated,
the Site Director called on the majority of

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:34.770
TAU-9 to help repel the violent cultists from
their perimeter.

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:41.300
TAU-9 obeyed, leaving three task force members
behind to guard SCP - 2662’s containment

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:42.300
chamber.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:46.780
They expected to be guarding the cell from
rampaging religious zealots seeking an audience

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:48.150
with their god.

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:52.950
What they didn’t expect was a group of five
Foundation employees walking right up to them

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:59.090
and opening fire, killing two TAU-9 members
and taking the third as a hostage.

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:04.020
While the war was being waged outside, the
infiltrators had found the Tentacled God’s

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:07.170
containment cell in the low-risk humanoid
ward.

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:11.640
Their hostage insisted that using him wouldn’t
give them any leverage - the rest of his team

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:16.670
would neutralize the whole group, him included,
if that’s what it took to stop them.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:21.230
The infiltrators explained that using him
as leverage was never their intention - he

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:23.160
wasn’t a hostage at all.

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:26.049
He was a sacrifice.

00:21:26.049 --> 00:21:30.789
The cultists of the Tentacled God detonated
explosives, creating a hole in the wall and

00:21:30.789 --> 00:21:33.490
finally giving them access to their deity.

00:21:33.490 --> 00:21:36.669
They climbed through and gazed upon him in
awe.

00:21:36.669 --> 00:21:44.549
There stood SCP-2662, twice as tall as a regular
man, with ten huge tentacles emerging from

00:21:44.549 --> 00:21:45.590
its back.

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:49.590
In their months of envisioning this creature,
they’d pictured it sitting on a throne made

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:55.580
of thousands of human bones, ready to dictate
its commands to the obedient liberators.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:01.310
What they certainly didn’t expect was to
see the Tentacled God hunched over a computer

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:02.310
screen.

00:22:02.310 --> 00:22:07.590
Still, gods work in mysterious ways, so they
stuck to the plan and began chanting.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:12.470
They pulled out a sacrificial dagger, and
began sacrificing their captured TAU-9 member.

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:18.279
It was at this point that SCP - 2662 turned
and saw what they were doing with a look of

00:22:18.279 --> 00:22:19.279
pure horror.

00:22:19.279 --> 00:22:23.669
He rose up from his computer, his headphones
getting caught as he did so.

00:22:23.669 --> 00:22:28.039
He told them to go away, that he didn’t
want them here, and that them murdering people

00:22:28.039 --> 00:22:31.789
in his bedroom like this was inconsiderate
and disgusting.

00:22:31.789 --> 00:22:37.179
The cultists became even more confused - why
wasn’t their god accepting their offerings?

00:22:37.179 --> 00:22:38.450
What were they doing wrong?

00:22:38.450 --> 00:22:43.610
They tried more chanting, and painting arcane
symbols on the floor in blood, but this just

00:22:43.610 --> 00:22:45.720
seemed to make the creature angrier.

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:50.909
He told them, in a tone more fitting for a
teenage boy than a Lovecraftian God, to just

00:22:50.909 --> 00:22:54.789
leave him alone so he could play his video
games.

00:22:54.789 --> 00:22:57.740
This was seriously not cool!

00:22:57.740 --> 00:22:59.480
The cultists were baffled.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:02.340
They told the Tentacled God they were there
to free him.

00:23:02.340 --> 00:23:05.120
He replied that he didn’t need saving.

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:09.470
That crazy stalkers like them were why he
turned himself in to the Foundation in the

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:11.170
first place!

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:15.059
Before the cultist infiltrators could get
another word in, the remaining members of

00:23:15.059 --> 00:23:19.990
TAU-9 stormed into the containment cell and
gunned them down with surgical precision.

00:23:19.990 --> 00:23:24.590
The war outside was already over - Brother
Marsh and the rest of the cultists were all

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:26.010
killed in the firefight.

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:32.360
TAU-9 didn’t look the least bit surprised
upon entering 2662’s cell, this was a common

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:34.500
occurrence unfortunately.

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:40.961
They had to deal with an attempted cult invasion
every few months, because SCP-2662’s main

00:23:40.961 --> 00:23:46.070
anomalous ability is inspiring violent cults
who relentlessly track down and worship it

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:48.750
with arcane and bloodthirsty rituals.

00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:55.450
The problem is, 2662 doesn’t do this consciously,
and definitely doesn’t like the results.

00:23:55.450 --> 00:24:00.380
That’s why he’s under the voluntary care
of the SCP Foundation who keeps him amused

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:04.990
with video games and reading material while
fending off the deranged cults who try to

00:24:04.990 --> 00:24:07.320
invade and abduct him.

00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:11.620
Following the termination of The Devotees
of the Tentacled God, just one of many cults

00:24:11.620 --> 00:24:17.040
who’d broken into 2662’s containment cell,
the remaining TAU-9 members apologized to

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:21.529
the tentacled creature for the disturbance,
allowing him to return to his gaming.

00:24:21.529 --> 00:24:25.860
They assured him that it’d probably be at
least a few more months before something like

00:24:25.860 --> 00:24:27.880
this happened again.

00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:33.620
SCP-2662’s cell was repaired, and the Foundation
returned to its task of seeking out would-be

00:24:33.620 --> 00:24:39.510
cultist emancipators, because for the SCP
Foundation, it’s not always about the anomaly

00:24:39.510 --> 00:24:43.399
that’s being kept in containment, but what’s
being kept out.

00:24:43.399 --> 00:24:48.810
A very strange anomaly sits in a humanoid
containment cell in the minimum security wing

00:24:48.810 --> 00:24:50.330
of Site 17.

00:24:50.330 --> 00:24:56.040
He walks, talks, and looks like a man, but
everything else is convoluted in a question

00:24:56.040 --> 00:24:57.040
mark.

00:24:57.040 --> 00:25:03.590
This is SCP-343 - Who, like his namesake,
God, is likely to cause arguments whenever

00:25:03.590 --> 00:25:04.590
he’s brought up.

00:25:04.590 --> 00:25:07.029
Is he the creator of all that exists?

00:25:07.029 --> 00:25:09.240
The basis for the Abrahamic Faiths?

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:15.880
Or is he a pretender - A reality warper with
immense power and a predilection towards delusion?

00:25:15.880 --> 00:25:18.490
A courtesan of the House of Malidraug?

00:25:18.490 --> 00:25:19.490
Matthew?

00:25:19.490 --> 00:25:20.490
Methuselah?

00:25:20.490 --> 00:25:21.490
Yahweh?

00:25:21.490 --> 00:25:22.490
Who knows?

00:25:22.490 --> 00:25:27.220
Really, it depends on who you ask, and which
stories you choose to believe.

00:25:27.220 --> 00:25:30.909
And few people enjoy a good story more than
SCP-343 himself.

00:25:30.909 --> 00:25:36.490
If, one day, you take the time to visit him
in his room, and ask him to reveal a page

00:25:36.490 --> 00:25:41.419
in the long book of his personal history,
he might be kind enough to tell you a story.

00:25:41.419 --> 00:25:48.440
A story like this - Of an encounter with something
monstrous, that few others could hope to survive

00:25:48.440 --> 00:25:50.360
meeting face to face…

00:25:50.360 --> 00:25:52.399
Rewind a few thousand years.

00:25:52.399 --> 00:25:55.029
Nobody knows how many, exactly.

00:25:55.029 --> 00:26:00.550
God - as he chooses to dub himself - walked
across the cracked ground on worn sandals.

00:26:00.550 --> 00:26:05.429
It’d been some time since he’d seen an
animal around here, and even longer since

00:26:05.429 --> 00:26:07.270
he’d seen a human being.

00:26:07.270 --> 00:26:08.440
Not that this bothered him.

00:26:08.440 --> 00:26:12.630
He’d never been bothered by his own company
on a long walk like this.

00:26:12.630 --> 00:26:17.419
Of course, he could have sped up time or teleported,
but where was the fun in that?

00:26:17.419 --> 00:26:20.080
He was a tourist in the world of sensation.

00:26:20.080 --> 00:26:21.690
Of experience.

00:26:21.690 --> 00:26:25.940
Of flesh, bone, dirt, blood, and sand.

00:26:25.940 --> 00:26:29.490
After all, where’s the fun in creating a
whole universe if you can’t drop in now

00:26:29.490 --> 00:26:32.110
and then to visit and do as the Romans do?

00:26:32.110 --> 00:26:36.370
Not that the Romans would be around for another
few thousand years.

00:26:36.370 --> 00:26:40.460
Even Atlas must occasionally shift the weight
of the globe from his shoulders for a jaunt

00:26:40.460 --> 00:26:46.340
around the cosmic neighborhood, and whatever
passes for “fresh air” in the vacuum.

00:26:46.340 --> 00:26:47.770
God whistled a tune to himself.

00:26:47.770 --> 00:26:51.470
It was a craggy, mountainous region he’d
found himself in.

00:26:51.470 --> 00:26:54.040
The distant peaks had frosted caps.

00:26:54.040 --> 00:26:58.590
A breathtaking place, where many truly had
their breaths taken away.

00:26:58.590 --> 00:27:02.770
How humans will so happily risk their lives
to do something extraordinary.

00:27:02.770 --> 00:27:05.049
It never ceased to amaze him.

00:27:05.049 --> 00:27:06.110
His stomach rumbled.

00:27:06.110 --> 00:27:08.789
Oh, how he enjoyed that sensation.

00:27:08.789 --> 00:27:12.990
One of the funny little quirks of this human
form that he’d weaved for himself.

00:27:12.990 --> 00:27:17.660
It was no reason to be concerned - If memory
served, from his last trip through the area

00:27:17.660 --> 00:27:21.850
a few decades before, there was a friendly
village not far from here.

00:27:21.850 --> 00:27:27.399
They had always accepted him as a genial stranger,
having no knowledge of his true power.

00:27:27.399 --> 00:27:31.860
God had always believed that a person’s
goodness is defined by how they treat those

00:27:31.860 --> 00:27:34.270
from whom they had nothing to gain.

00:27:34.270 --> 00:27:38.990
So it caused him great concern as he approached
the village, and saw great plumes of smoke

00:27:38.990 --> 00:27:41.000
rising into the sky.

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:45.470
He was so shocked by this that he decided
to break his rule about walking as a man,

00:27:45.470 --> 00:27:48.179
in case there was still some way he could
help.

00:27:48.179 --> 00:27:52.480
With a snap of his fingers, he disappeared
and reappeared in the center of the village’s

00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:53.700
town square.

00:27:53.700 --> 00:27:55.440
Total devastation.

00:27:55.440 --> 00:27:58.260
Huts and houses had been torn asunder.

00:27:58.260 --> 00:28:00.399
Broken weapons lay on the ground.

00:28:00.399 --> 00:28:05.789
Some places were on fire, others smeared with
streaks of blood, like some terrible battle

00:28:05.789 --> 00:28:07.110
had occurred here.

00:28:07.110 --> 00:28:09.340
But something was wrong.

00:28:09.340 --> 00:28:10.679
No bodies.

00:28:10.679 --> 00:28:14.620
Not one, from defender or assailant.

00:28:14.620 --> 00:28:20.200
How could a thriving village be so thoroughly
destroyed, and not leave a single corpse?

00:28:20.200 --> 00:28:25.760
It was an act so bizarre and depraved that
it even left God puzzling.

00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:30.299
That was another downside of his human form:
Here, on earth, he didn’t have access to

00:28:30.299 --> 00:28:32.040
true omniscience.

00:28:32.040 --> 00:28:37.490
How could a mere human mind, bound by the
constraints of linear time, ever truly comprehend

00:28:37.490 --> 00:28:39.390
the totality of existence?

00:28:39.390 --> 00:28:43.710
Even attempting to do that here would melt
the brain of his human body in its skull,

00:28:43.710 --> 00:28:46.750
and leave it dribbling out of his nose and
ears.

00:28:46.750 --> 00:28:51.860
Instead, he chose to walk around the ruins
of the village and investigate firsthand.

00:28:51.860 --> 00:28:55.860
Arrows and broken spears and swords littered
the ground.

00:28:55.860 --> 00:28:59.980
Some buildings were demolished, but there
were no tracks or stray projectiles that could

00:28:59.980 --> 00:29:02.500
suggest the presence of siege weapons.

00:29:02.500 --> 00:29:06.390
No, these buildings looked like they were
ripped apart.

00:29:06.390 --> 00:29:08.840
Some even still had claw marks…

00:29:08.840 --> 00:29:12.640
What terrible beast could have set upon this
town and done this?

00:29:12.640 --> 00:29:18.470
Then, he heard a voice, quiet and pleading
beneath some nearby rubble.

00:29:18.470 --> 00:29:19.539
A survivor!

00:29:19.539 --> 00:29:24.570
He rushed over to the pile and evaporated
it with a thought, Underneath, a feeble old

00:29:24.570 --> 00:29:28.000
man, covered in stone dust, was quivering.

00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:32.390
God helped him up and guided him into one
of the few remaining huts still standing in

00:29:32.390 --> 00:29:33.390
the village.

00:29:33.390 --> 00:29:38.000
They both took seats - God held up two hands,
cradling empty space.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:43.159
Two cups suddenly occupied that space, both
filled with warm, healing tea.

00:29:43.159 --> 00:29:47.070
He passed the old man one of the cups while
sipping from his own.

00:29:47.070 --> 00:29:49.870
He asked the old man if he’d seen what had
happened.

00:29:49.870 --> 00:29:53.650
The old man told him, no, he hadn’t seen
anything in decades.

00:29:53.650 --> 00:29:56.520
He’d been rendered blind in his youth.

00:29:56.520 --> 00:30:01.211
Little did either of them know, that very
blindness was the only reason he was the sole

00:30:01.211 --> 00:30:03.510
survivor of the massacre.

00:30:03.510 --> 00:30:07.590
The blind man told God that one of the village’s
scouts had gone up into the mountain with

00:30:07.590 --> 00:30:09.110
a small hunting party.

00:30:09.110 --> 00:30:14.500
The group was gone for days, until one of
the members - the youngest among them - returned,

00:30:14.500 --> 00:30:17.720
weeping, frostbitten, and covered in blood.

00:30:17.720 --> 00:30:21.890
He said that his friends had been killed by
a beast in the mountains.

00:30:21.890 --> 00:30:25.460
Something that looked almost like a man, but
terribly wrong.

00:30:25.460 --> 00:30:27.039
And its face.

00:30:27.039 --> 00:30:29.340
Its awful, awful face.

00:30:29.340 --> 00:30:31.399
He would never forget it.

00:30:31.399 --> 00:30:35.200
He was just lucky to escape with his life
when the others were torn apart.

00:30:35.200 --> 00:30:39.580
But when the young man returned, he’d brought
the shadow of death with him.

00:30:39.580 --> 00:30:45.950
It was a curse that doomed the entire village
- men, women, and children - to a terrible

00:30:45.950 --> 00:30:46.950
fate.

00:30:46.950 --> 00:30:51.870
And that fate was upon them a mere hour after
the survivor had returned.

00:30:51.870 --> 00:30:56.230
Of course, there were gaps in the blind man’s
understanding, given he was lacking one of

00:30:56.230 --> 00:30:57.800
his major senses.

00:30:57.800 --> 00:31:00.769
But the sounds he could describe with perfect
clarity.

00:31:00.769 --> 00:31:03.550
It was faint and distant at first.

00:31:03.550 --> 00:31:06.830
That awful wail, and the galloping.

00:31:06.830 --> 00:31:11.110
Hands and feet thundering against the ground,
faster than any horse could move.

00:31:11.110 --> 00:31:13.630
Getting closer and closer and closer.

00:31:13.630 --> 00:31:18.310
Another villager saw it approaching and screamed,
then it was upon them.

00:31:18.310 --> 00:31:21.700
The villagers screamed but it screamed louder.

00:31:21.700 --> 00:31:26.990
Always wailing and shrieking and sobbing like
a monster crawled straight up from hell.

00:31:26.990 --> 00:31:29.289
People tried to fight it, by the sounds of
it.

00:31:29.289 --> 00:31:35.740
The blind man, with teary, blank eyes, recalled
the sounds of arrows nocking and swords clashing

00:31:35.740 --> 00:31:36.840
against…

00:31:36.840 --> 00:31:37.950
Something.

00:31:37.950 --> 00:31:41.700
But even their greatest warriors had screamed
and died.

00:31:41.700 --> 00:31:46.389
Those who saw it and tried to flee and hide
were slaughtered all the same.

00:31:46.389 --> 00:31:49.600
Soon enough, there were only two sounds left
in the village.

00:31:49.600 --> 00:31:53.550
The monster and the blind man, both weeping.

00:31:53.550 --> 00:31:56.070
He didn’t understand why it never took him.

00:31:56.070 --> 00:31:57.370
It wasn’t fair.

00:31:57.370 --> 00:31:59.049
It took everything else.

00:31:59.049 --> 00:32:04.820
To leave him here, alive, when everyone and
everything he’d ever known was destroyed,

00:32:04.820 --> 00:32:07.679
was a greater punishment than even death.

00:32:07.679 --> 00:32:12.600
After killing all of these innocents, the
monster had simply wandered off to the mountains

00:32:12.600 --> 00:32:19.390
again, the sound of its quiet sobs getting
smaller and smaller until it was gone altogether.

00:32:19.390 --> 00:32:23.660
God comforted the blind man as he wept for
the loss of all his loved ones.

00:32:23.660 --> 00:32:27.430
He told the blind man that he would venture
up to the mountains himself and confront the

00:32:27.430 --> 00:32:32.970
creature on its own territory, and, at the
very least, find out why it had done this

00:32:32.970 --> 00:32:34.470
terrible thing.

00:32:34.470 --> 00:32:38.190
But first, he must relocate the blind man
to a safer place.

00:32:38.190 --> 00:32:41.750
He placed a hand on the blind man’s shoulder
and he vanished.

00:32:41.750 --> 00:32:45.779
He would appear in another friendly village,
miles away.

00:32:45.779 --> 00:32:52.289
God sent a silent message into the minds of
every villager: Take good care of this man.

00:32:52.289 --> 00:32:56.450
He has undergone horrors you can’t even
imagine.

00:32:56.450 --> 00:33:02.820
Your kindness will be rewarded later, for
that, you have my promise.

00:33:02.820 --> 00:33:06.620
God sighed and turned his tired eyes to the
distant mountains.

00:33:06.620 --> 00:33:12.520
A monster lurked up there - Perhaps one of
his own creations, or maybe a corruption of

00:33:12.520 --> 00:33:14.019
one of his creations.

00:33:14.019 --> 00:33:20.250
Either way, whatever existed without his knowledge
existed without his consent, and he intended

00:33:20.250 --> 00:33:22.710
to know of the beast in the mountains.

00:33:22.710 --> 00:33:26.890
Though given what he’d seen already, he
didn’t expect to receive a warm welcome

00:33:26.890 --> 00:33:29.110
from this murderous demon.

00:33:29.110 --> 00:33:32.750
Miles away, up in the mountains, the creature
licked the blood from its cracked lips.

00:33:32.750 --> 00:33:38.389
It looked like it might once have been a human
being or something that aspired to humanity,

00:33:38.389 --> 00:33:40.639
or mocked it with its very existence.

00:33:40.639 --> 00:33:48.299
It was a huge, gangling beast, skin alabaster,
eyes empty and soulless, dribbling rivulets

00:33:48.299 --> 00:33:51.529
of burning tears down a hideous, gaunt face.

00:33:51.529 --> 00:33:57.580
It crawled into the frozen mouth of a cave
with great icicle fangs, wheezing and weeping.

00:33:57.580 --> 00:34:00.919
All it ever wanted was to be alone.

00:34:00.919 --> 00:34:02.610
Why did they have to keep interfering?

00:34:02.610 --> 00:34:04.920
Didn’t they know what happened?

00:34:04.920 --> 00:34:07.389
All the terrible things they’d made it do…

00:34:07.389 --> 00:34:12.270
The creature curled its long, gangly body
into the fetal position, scratching great

00:34:12.270 --> 00:34:17.320
ruts into the sides of its bald cranium with
long, sharp fingers.

00:34:17.320 --> 00:34:18.560
Terrible things.

00:34:18.560 --> 00:34:21.000
Terrible, terrible things…

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:24.580
And then there was a brilliant flash, just
a few feet away.

00:34:24.580 --> 00:34:29.710
The monster was surprised, it turned to see
a figure silhouetted in the mouth of the cave.

00:34:29.710 --> 00:34:31.960
He wore sandals and thin robes.

00:34:31.960 --> 00:34:35.929
His eyes glowed with a kind of power that
the monster didn’t recognize.

00:34:35.929 --> 00:34:41.040
This stranger stared at the monster without
an ounce of fear in his heart: He stared right

00:34:41.040 --> 00:34:42.669
into its eyes, unwavering.

00:34:42.669 --> 00:34:43.669
No!

00:34:43.669 --> 00:34:45.600
No, no, no, no!

00:34:45.600 --> 00:34:47.520
It could feel it again.

00:34:47.520 --> 00:34:49.790
The rage bubbling up, deep down.

00:34:49.790 --> 00:34:52.020
A cauldron of seething anger.

00:34:52.020 --> 00:34:56.329
It hated the feeling, like being lowered into
a vat of molten metal.

00:34:56.329 --> 00:34:58.820
Unspeakable fire and pain coursing through
every vessel.

00:34:58.820 --> 00:35:04.010
It began to weep and scream while the stranger
in the cave mouth just watched, not moving

00:35:04.010 --> 00:35:05.010
a muscle.

00:35:05.010 --> 00:35:07.900
“Do you know who I am?”

00:35:07.900 --> 00:35:13.589
the stranger asked with a deep voice that
betrayed almost infinite power, knowledge,

00:35:13.589 --> 00:35:14.610
and wisdom.

00:35:14.610 --> 00:35:16.920
But it wouldn’t change the outcome here.

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:20.990
The monster bounded at him at speeds that
wouldn’t be seen again until jet planes

00:35:20.990 --> 00:35:24.470
and bullet trains are invented millennia into
the future.

00:35:24.470 --> 00:35:29.869
Its jaws were hanging impossibly wide, fangs
borne, its arms extended and deadly claws

00:35:29.869 --> 00:35:31.109
ready to strike.

00:35:31.109 --> 00:35:35.869
But before those terrible hands could close
around the stranger, he vanished.

00:35:35.869 --> 00:35:39.140
The monster stumbled and rolled across the
snow, confused.

00:35:39.140 --> 00:35:40.890
What trickery was being used here?

00:35:40.890 --> 00:35:45.640
“I’ll take that as a no,” said the voice
from behind him.

00:35:45.640 --> 00:35:49.220
“You ought to show your father some respect.

00:35:49.220 --> 00:35:53.990
More respect than you gave to those poor people
down in the village, at least.”

00:35:53.990 --> 00:35:58.230
Seething, the creature turned and saw the
stranger standing back in the darkness of

00:35:58.230 --> 00:35:59.910
the cave, staring at him.

00:35:59.910 --> 00:36:04.500
But the beast didn’t have the capacity for
awe or holy terror.

00:36:04.500 --> 00:36:05.700
Only violence.

00:36:05.700 --> 00:36:09.530
Boundless, limitless, unstoppable violence.

00:36:09.530 --> 00:36:13.470
It darted towards the stranger again, trying
to strike at him.

00:36:13.470 --> 00:36:15.920
Somehow, it was like fighting an empty robe.

00:36:15.920 --> 00:36:19.730
Not a single one of its deadly strikes seemed
to hit the stranger.

00:36:19.730 --> 00:36:24.390
The stranger leaped backwards, putting some
space between himself and the monster but

00:36:24.390 --> 00:36:26.300
still not breaking a sweat.

00:36:26.300 --> 00:36:28.930
He breathed in deeply, then exhaled.

00:36:28.930 --> 00:36:34.070
The breath came out like a mighty typhoon,
shocking even the monster with its sudden

00:36:34.070 --> 00:36:35.070
force.

00:36:35.070 --> 00:36:39.800
It was blown backwards, a leaf in the wind,
until its long claws dug into the ground and

00:36:39.800 --> 00:36:41.599
anchored it in place.

00:36:41.599 --> 00:36:44.260
The stranger gave a wry smile at this, impressed.

00:36:44.260 --> 00:36:49.760
“My, my, you’re certainly a tenacious
one, aren’t you?” he said.

00:36:49.760 --> 00:36:53.780
“Perhaps we can talk for a little while
instead of fighting.

00:36:53.780 --> 00:36:58.300
I want to know why you killed all those people.”

00:36:58.300 --> 00:36:59.340
No answer.

00:36:59.340 --> 00:37:04.340
The beast roared, its mighty limbs pounding
into the ground as it closed the gap between

00:37:04.340 --> 00:37:08.150
itself and the stranger in fractions of a
second.

00:37:08.150 --> 00:37:09.790
It would kill him.

00:37:09.790 --> 00:37:11.089
Rend him.

00:37:11.089 --> 00:37:13.589
Destroy him just like all the others.

00:37:13.589 --> 00:37:15.450
He’d left it no choice!

00:37:15.450 --> 00:37:18.500
Suddenly, the ground below it seemed to give
away.

00:37:18.500 --> 00:37:19.880
The creature was confused.

00:37:19.880 --> 00:37:24.560
It looked down to see that the ancient stone
below had somehow taken on the properties

00:37:24.560 --> 00:37:26.890
of a liquid, and it was sinking.

00:37:26.890 --> 00:37:29.030
The beast panicked and began to thrash.

00:37:29.030 --> 00:37:33.930
It was a strong swimmer, but it didn’t expect
to need to swim here.

00:37:33.930 --> 00:37:39.480
The shock was too much, and soon, the ground
submerged it entirely, muffling its terrible

00:37:39.480 --> 00:37:41.190
roars and shrieks.

00:37:41.190 --> 00:37:45.910
And just like that, the ground was solid again,
trapping the beast inside.

00:37:45.910 --> 00:37:47.920
The stranger stepped forward and looked at
the ground.

00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:49.820
“A much-needed time out,” he said.

00:37:49.820 --> 00:37:56.610
“You do yourself no good struggling like
this.”

00:37:56.610 --> 00:38:01.840
Despite its terrible capacity for evil, God
couldn’t help but admire the beast, at least

00:38:01.840 --> 00:38:03.740
on the level of construction.

00:38:03.740 --> 00:38:06.560
It was so pared down, so unburdened.

00:38:06.560 --> 00:38:10.330
A killer to the core, but seemingly unkillable.

00:38:10.330 --> 00:38:12.430
Had he made this creature?

00:38:12.430 --> 00:38:16.730
Billions of species and the species those,
in turn, had created through billions of years

00:38:16.730 --> 00:38:22.470
of breeding and evolution, and somewhere along
the line, this thing happened.

00:38:22.470 --> 00:38:27.790
It was easy even for the universe’s creator
to lose track of some of the tinier variables.

00:38:27.790 --> 00:38:32.380
And in the grand scheme of things, even this
monster was still a tiny variable.

00:38:32.380 --> 00:38:37.690
But right here, right now, it was still one
hell of a problem.

00:38:37.690 --> 00:38:40.000
The ground rumbled below God.

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:41.000
Cracks formed.

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:42.890
The mountain peak shook.

00:38:42.890 --> 00:38:48.180
God raised an eyebrow, genuinely impressed,
as the monster ripped free of its stone prison

00:38:48.180 --> 00:38:49.940
and re-entered the fray.

00:38:49.940 --> 00:38:54.520
It roared and screamed still, its blank eyes
fixed on him.

00:38:54.520 --> 00:38:57.900
Its skeletal body throbbed and heaved with
power.

00:38:57.900 --> 00:39:02.220
Unlike any other creature in nature, it was
almost like, the longer their conflict went

00:39:02.220 --> 00:39:05.700
on, the more energized the beast became.

00:39:05.700 --> 00:39:06.900
God sighed.

00:39:06.900 --> 00:39:08.819
All those poor villagers.

00:39:08.819 --> 00:39:10.930
They never stood a chance against this monster.

00:39:10.930 --> 00:39:14.849
It lunged for him, even faster and stronger
than before.

00:39:14.849 --> 00:39:19.050
He teleported out of the way in the nick of
time and the beast’s claws cleaved through

00:39:19.050 --> 00:39:21.960
a nearby cave wall, effortless.

00:39:21.960 --> 00:39:25.260
God materialized nearby, but he didn’t have
time to speak.

00:39:25.260 --> 00:39:29.010
The beast lunged again, and again, and again.

00:39:29.010 --> 00:39:34.030
Every time he reappeared, the beast went for
him with impossible speed.

00:39:34.030 --> 00:39:38.010
Deciding to widen the playing field, God teleported
to the top of the mountain.

00:39:38.010 --> 00:39:42.089
The creature, somehow sensing his presence,
vaulted upwards and tunneled through the roof

00:39:42.089 --> 00:39:47.130
of the cave, bursting out of the ground in
front of God, who was floating just slightly

00:39:47.130 --> 00:39:48.130
off the ground.

00:39:48.130 --> 00:39:52.590
“It would be wise of you to stop,” God
carefully intoned.

00:39:52.590 --> 00:39:55.690
“All this time, you know, I’ve been going
easy on you.

00:39:55.690 --> 00:40:01.390
You don’t want to find out what the wrath
of God looks like.”

00:40:01.390 --> 00:40:03.630
Storm clouds were gathering above.

00:40:03.630 --> 00:40:06.100
Mighty thunder roared across the sky.

00:40:06.100 --> 00:40:07.510
The beast was undeterred.

00:40:07.510 --> 00:40:10.099
It roared and galloped towards God.

00:40:10.099 --> 00:40:12.790
And God, in turn, called down a response.

00:40:12.790 --> 00:40:18.160
A volley of lightning the likes of which the
world has never seen before or since struck

00:40:18.160 --> 00:40:20.320
down on the charging monster.

00:40:20.320 --> 00:40:23.800
The sudden white flash could sting the eyes
from miles away.

00:40:23.800 --> 00:40:28.430
The monster shrieked from the blast, feeling
its flesh lift off its bones and atomize in

00:40:28.430 --> 00:40:31.030
the sheer heat of the electricity around it.

00:40:31.030 --> 00:40:32.740
It could smell itself cooking.

00:40:32.740 --> 00:40:37.910
The lightning blasts only lasted for a few
seconds, but for the beast, it felt like an

00:40:37.910 --> 00:40:38.910
eternity.

00:40:38.910 --> 00:40:42.970
When the onslaught stopped, the air was still
heavy with electrical potential.

00:40:42.970 --> 00:40:46.869
God stared down at the black scorch mark on
the side of the mountain where the creature

00:40:46.869 --> 00:40:48.270
had been standing.

00:40:48.270 --> 00:40:51.760
All the snow within the mile had been evaporated
by the blast.

00:40:51.760 --> 00:40:57.810
It was a raw display of the power of nature
that would make even Zeus tremble in his sandals.

00:40:57.810 --> 00:40:59.240
And yet…

00:40:59.240 --> 00:41:01.770
There was still movement.

00:41:01.770 --> 00:41:05.070
Something started to get up from the burnt
patch where nothing should be left alive.

00:41:05.070 --> 00:41:12.260
A blackened skeleton, rising shakily from
the ash but still very much alive.

00:41:12.260 --> 00:41:17.130
As it started to rise, new flesh began growing
over the bones, little by little.

00:41:17.130 --> 00:41:19.440
Even God was astonished by the sight of it.

00:41:19.440 --> 00:41:24.780
He’d never seen a creature cling so ardently
to life in spite of having truly unsurmountable

00:41:24.780 --> 00:41:26.950
power amassed against it.

00:41:26.950 --> 00:41:30.780
It was up against God, and still, it fought.

00:41:30.780 --> 00:41:36.190
The monster tottered on its freakishly long
limbs, still disoriented, unusually staggered

00:41:36.190 --> 00:41:39.580
for a creature driven by such single-minded,
violent purpose.

00:41:39.580 --> 00:41:45.480
When enough of its face grew back to do so,
it began to weep and sob again, tears streaking

00:41:45.480 --> 00:41:47.780
down its terrible face.

00:41:47.780 --> 00:41:52.550
Looking at this creature, after all this,
God couldn’t help but feel a new emotion:

00:41:52.550 --> 00:41:53.550
Pity.

00:41:53.550 --> 00:41:56.440
He lowered himself to the ground and approached
the creature.

00:41:56.440 --> 00:42:02.490
Like none had ever done before, he gathered
it up into his arms and held it, feeling its

00:42:02.490 --> 00:42:04.520
heaving, wretched sobs against him.

00:42:04.520 --> 00:42:07.089
This beast was in so much pain.

00:42:07.089 --> 00:42:09.820
He could feel it, radiating from within.

00:42:09.820 --> 00:42:14.900
“Speak, my son,” God said in a soft, fatherly
voice.

00:42:14.900 --> 00:42:20.900
And for the first and only time, the monster
spoke, “Can’t look.

00:42:20.900 --> 00:42:22.859
Can’t see.

00:42:22.859 --> 00:42:26.780
Make me hurt people.

00:42:26.780 --> 00:42:30.700
Don’t want hurt people.

00:42:30.700 --> 00:42:34.619
Can’t look, can’t look.

00:42:34.619 --> 00:42:35.619
Please.”

00:42:35.619 --> 00:42:41.349
That was all it managed to choke out before
devolving back into unintelligible babble.

00:42:41.349 --> 00:42:42.349
But it was enough.

00:42:42.349 --> 00:42:45.750
Enough for God to understand its pain.

00:42:45.750 --> 00:42:50.329
He did not know if it would be right to change
the monster’s nature - is it ever right

00:42:50.329 --> 00:42:52.780
to truly change anyone’s nature?

00:42:52.780 --> 00:42:57.960
- but it was within his almost limitless power
to grant it one reprieve from its pain.

00:42:57.960 --> 00:43:00.580
He settled the beast in the snow below him.

00:43:00.580 --> 00:43:02.869
It was quiet and still.

00:43:02.869 --> 00:43:06.369
And God said unto the beast, “Rest now,
child.

00:43:06.369 --> 00:43:10.290
Rest for thousands of years, if you must.

00:43:10.290 --> 00:43:16.800
I hope only that when you eventually awaken,
you feel differently…”

00:43:16.800 --> 00:43:20.670
And so another story from the catalog of SCP-343.

00:43:20.670 --> 00:43:26.339
Of course, it leaves us with certain questions,
chief among them being: Is it true?

00:43:26.339 --> 00:43:31.990
Did 343 and 096 have this chance encounter
long ago, or is this just another tall tale

00:43:31.990 --> 00:43:35.280
from an anomaly who fancies himself a deity?

00:43:35.280 --> 00:43:38.640
We have our truth, and you have yours.

00:43:38.640 --> 00:43:42.190
If you’ve ever read the Book of Genesis,
which is the part of the Old Testament that

00:43:42.190 --> 00:43:47.730
details God creating the world and humanity
during a particularly busy week, then you

00:43:47.730 --> 00:43:51.900
might just already be familiar with SCP-001.

00:43:51.900 --> 00:43:57.540
Or at least, one of the anomalies that’s
been proposed for the title of SCP-001.

00:43:57.540 --> 00:44:03.869
Because of course SCP-001 doesn’t refer
to a single creature, object or entity, but

00:44:03.869 --> 00:44:09.260
rather a collection of various anomalies contained
by the SCP Foundation.

00:44:09.260 --> 00:44:15.460
Anomalies sharing the name SCP-001 include
the infamous Scarlet King, a powerful eldritch

00:44:15.460 --> 00:44:19.920
being, intent on ending all of creation that
is thought by Foundation researchers to be

00:44:19.920 --> 00:44:24.700
one of the most dangerous beings in this,
and any other universe.

00:44:24.700 --> 00:44:30.619
But the Scarlet King isn’t the only incredibly
powerful being categorized as SCP-001.

00:44:30.619 --> 00:44:35.579
In fact, there are plenty of other anomalies
with similar levels of destructive power.

00:44:35.579 --> 00:44:40.540
And one such being is a creature code named
The Gate Guardian.

00:44:40.540 --> 00:44:44.620
Standing at well over a thousand feet tall,
The Gate Guardian is impossible to be fully

00:44:44.620 --> 00:44:48.190
contained by any means that the Foundation
possesses.

00:44:48.190 --> 00:44:53.480
The anomaly itself, despite its colossal size,
is humanoid in its shape, sporting wings that

00:44:53.480 --> 00:44:54.800
protrude from its back.

00:44:54.800 --> 00:45:00.830
While it usually has four of these, SCP-001
has historically been seen to have any number

00:45:00.830 --> 00:45:07.589
of wings between two and 108, sprouting from
various places over its body, including shoulders,

00:45:07.589 --> 00:45:11.260
ankles, wrists, and even its temples.

00:45:11.260 --> 00:45:17.660
This gigantic Guardian also carries its own
weapon, referred to as SCP-001-2.

00:45:17.660 --> 00:45:23.089
This weapon resembles an enormous knife or
sword, capable of emitting plumes of flame.

00:45:23.089 --> 00:45:27.000
According to tests conducted by the Foundation,
the temperature of the flames produced by

00:45:27.000 --> 00:45:30.800
SCP-001-2 rival that of our very own sun.

00:45:30.800 --> 00:45:36.610
For reference, the sun has a core temperature
of over twenty seven million degrees Fahrenheit,

00:45:36.610 --> 00:45:43.400
and 5,778 Kelvin at its surface, or almost
ten thousand degrees Fahrenheit.

00:45:43.400 --> 00:45:47.930
You would expect a flaming sword that burns
hotter than the sun to cause a considerable

00:45:47.930 --> 00:45:52.630
amount of damage, even if it wasn’t in use,
but the flames emitted by the weapon leave

00:45:52.630 --> 00:45:55.780
no lasting damage on the surrounding environment.

00:45:55.780 --> 00:46:02.400
It is capable though, of annihilating anything
that strays too close to SCP-001, burning

00:46:02.400 --> 00:46:07.680
them so intensely that their atoms literally
separate, breaking potential attackers apart

00:46:07.680 --> 00:46:09.470
on a molecular level.

00:46:09.470 --> 00:46:14.420
Much as its codename suggests, The Gate Guardian
stands solemnly at the threshold of some form

00:46:14.420 --> 00:46:20.200
of dimensional gateway which is equally as
tall as SCP-001 itself.

00:46:20.200 --> 00:46:25.660
Behind the Guardian, is a lush grove, abundant
with fruit trees of an astronomical size,

00:46:25.660 --> 00:46:31.000
as well as other beings that share a similar
appearance to SCP-001.

00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:36.050
This grove is thought to be the Garden of
Eden, the paradise that God created, and that

00:46:36.050 --> 00:46:41.060
was inhabited by Adam and Eve, the first two
humans in existence, according to the Book

00:46:41.060 --> 00:46:42.390
of Genesis.

00:46:42.390 --> 00:46:47.420
As the tale goes, the pair were created by
God himself, and permitted to live in the

00:46:47.420 --> 00:46:50.260
Garden of Eden as long as they followed a
single rule.

00:46:50.260 --> 00:46:55.319
Adam and Eve were instructed not to eat any
of the fruits that grew from certain trees

00:46:55.319 --> 00:46:57.530
that God had specified.

00:46:57.530 --> 00:47:02.240
Within view just behind the Gate Guardian
are two immense trees, one bearing apples

00:47:02.240 --> 00:47:05.120
and the other bearing different fruit of unknown
type.

00:47:05.120 --> 00:47:10.660
The one that looks like an apple tree is believed,
even by some in the Foundation, to be the

00:47:10.660 --> 00:47:16.480
biblical Tree of Knowledge that Eve was convinced
to pick a fateful apple from after an encounter

00:47:16.480 --> 00:47:17.609
with a snake.

00:47:17.609 --> 00:47:22.839
The other, the one with unidentifiable fruit,
is thought to be the Tree of Life.

00:47:22.839 --> 00:47:27.390
However, this is all speculation, since it
is currently impossible to venture through

00:47:27.390 --> 00:47:33.099
this gateway and verify if the realm beyond
is truly the Bible’s own Garden of Eden.

00:47:33.099 --> 00:47:38.619
This is largely because anything that breaches
a kilometer wide radius of SCP-001 is instantly

00:47:38.619 --> 00:47:39.910
vaporized.

00:47:39.910 --> 00:47:44.770
The Gate Guardian attacks with an imperceptible
speed, using its flaming sword to smite any

00:47:44.770 --> 00:47:47.220
person that gets too close.

00:47:47.220 --> 00:47:51.160
The Guardian actually moves so fast that it
can hardly be seen with the naked eye.

00:47:51.160 --> 00:47:56.200
It appears to always remain in its solemn,
dutiful stance with its weapon drawn and head

00:47:56.200 --> 00:48:01.069
bowed, only shifting for a fraction of a nanosecond
to attack.

00:48:01.069 --> 00:48:05.339
Ranged attacks against the Guardian are just
as ineffective, with all projectiles fired

00:48:05.339 --> 00:48:10.210
at SCP-001 reduced to atoms before they can
do any harm.

00:48:10.210 --> 00:48:14.569
Even if said projectile happens to be a nuclear
weapon, The Gate Guardian will be able to

00:48:14.569 --> 00:48:19.580
sub-atomically vaporize both the projectile
itself as well as the person who sent it,

00:48:19.580 --> 00:48:22.020
regardless of how far away they are.

00:48:22.020 --> 00:48:25.130
All while not appearing to lift a finger.

00:48:25.130 --> 00:48:32.820
During an experiment involving SCP-001on December
26th, 2004, an SCP Foundation nuclear submarine

00:48:32.820 --> 00:48:37.369
called ‘Nautilus’ launched a series of
multi-warhead intercontinental ballistic missiles

00:48:37.369 --> 00:48:38.369
at The Gate Guardian.

00:48:38.369 --> 00:48:44.380
The retaliation from the Guardian resulted
not only in the deaths of approximately 35,000

00:48:44.380 --> 00:48:49.630
innocent civilians, but the blast is also
believed, by some, to have inadvertently caused

00:48:49.630 --> 00:48:52.530
the 2004 Boxing Day tsunami.

00:48:52.530 --> 00:48:57.559
The severity of this incident came dangerously
close to revealing the Foundation’s existence

00:48:57.559 --> 00:49:02.670
to the world, resulting in them rapidly deploying
any means necessary to erase any trace of

00:49:02.670 --> 00:49:08.030
the thirty five thousand victims’ families,
friends and other related individuals.

00:49:08.030 --> 00:49:13.900
In order to avoid questioning, the SCP Foundation
administered amnestics on an almost worldwide

00:49:13.900 --> 00:49:21.730
scale, and the O5 council banned any further
tests on SCP-001 that involved nuclear weapons.

00:49:21.730 --> 00:49:26.540
In what was hoped by the Foundation to be
a test with lower stakes, they sent an expendable

00:49:26.540 --> 00:49:28.740
D-Class personnel towards SCP-001.

00:49:28.740 --> 00:49:33.810
The D-Class approached the area where the
Gate Guardian is located, and as soon as they

00:49:33.810 --> 00:49:39.559
saw it, they could hear a very clear command
in their mind - “Leave”

00:49:39.559 --> 00:49:43.470
The D-Class personnel reacted exactly the
same way you or I would.

00:49:43.470 --> 00:49:46.160
They promptly turned and started to walk away.

00:49:46.160 --> 00:49:51.000
They didn’t need a thousand foot tall entity
with a flaming sword to tell them twice.

00:49:51.000 --> 00:49:54.599
The researchers running the experiment were
not as swayed by the request, and ordered

00:49:54.599 --> 00:49:58.010
the D-Class to continue moving towards SCP-001.

00:49:58.010 --> 00:50:03.930
When the D-Class continued to ignore their
commands, they were terminated, as is standard

00:50:03.930 --> 00:50:07.809
policy when dealing with an insubordinate
member D-Class.

00:50:07.809 --> 00:50:13.240
SCP-001 appeared not to like this for some
reason though, and the researcher site as

00:50:13.240 --> 00:50:18.890
well as the researchers themselves were immediately
obliterated by an unknown force, though it’s

00:50:18.890 --> 00:50:23.750
a pretty safe guess that a certain flaming
weapon was responsible.

00:50:23.750 --> 00:50:30.290
This candidate for SCP-001 may be one of,
if not the most powerful being that the SCP

00:50:30.290 --> 00:50:36.391
Foundation has ever encountered, and according
to its entry in the SCP-001 file, the Guardian

00:50:36.391 --> 00:50:40.849
is even responsible for the creation of the
Foundation itself.

00:50:40.849 --> 00:50:46.700
If the file is to be believed, the Administrator
of the SCP Foundation one day heard a word

00:50:46.700 --> 00:50:49.290
echoing through his head.

00:50:49.290 --> 00:50:50.680
“Prepare.”

00:50:50.680 --> 00:50:56.450
This one word instruction led him to starting
the SCP Foundation, containing countless dangerous

00:50:56.450 --> 00:51:00.920
anomalies and entities in preparation for
an uncertain future.

00:51:00.920 --> 00:51:06.200
In all that time, since the very beginning
of the Foundation, The Gate Guardian has remained

00:51:06.200 --> 00:51:08.069
standing at its post.

00:51:08.069 --> 00:51:13.579
While it is not aggressive nor openly hostile
towards humanity, The Gate Guardian doesn’t

00:51:13.579 --> 00:51:16.191
seem to care much for us either, at least
as individuals.

00:51:16.191 --> 00:51:22.119
It rarely interacts with human beings when
left unprovoked, and venturing too close to

00:51:22.119 --> 00:51:25.809
the Guardian however, is not an automatic
death sentence.

00:51:25.809 --> 00:51:31.200
The Guardian first communicates with any living
being approaching it via a telepathic message,

00:51:31.200 --> 00:51:33.900
instructing them to either “Leave” or
“Forget”.

00:51:33.900 --> 00:51:39.530
If whomever has stepped too close to SCP-001
complies with the instructions, they’ll

00:51:39.530 --> 00:51:45.020
be able to freely leave the area, while simultaneously
forgetting every detail of The Gate Guardian’s

00:51:45.020 --> 00:51:46.020
existence.

00:51:46.020 --> 00:51:51.780
Ignore these warnings though, and SCP-001
has no qualms about completely eliminating

00:51:51.780 --> 00:51:53.520
you from reality.

00:51:53.520 --> 00:51:57.790
Given its enormous destructive potential,
it is no wonder that the Foundation has tried

00:51:57.790 --> 00:52:03.950
to use The Gate Guardian to eliminate other
dangerous SCPs, each with varying results.

00:52:03.950 --> 00:52:08.140
The Foundation at one time even attempted
to use The Gate Guardian to destroy the infamously

00:52:08.140 --> 00:52:13.980
indestructible SCP-682, better known by the
rather appropriate name of The Hard-to-Destroy

00:52:13.980 --> 00:52:15.330
Reptile.

00:52:15.330 --> 00:52:21.640
Due to the malicious contempt SCP-682 holds
for human beings and all other forms of life,

00:52:21.640 --> 00:52:27.790
it is perhaps one of the most dangerous anomalies
the SCP Foundation has in containment.

00:52:27.790 --> 00:52:33.460
SCP-682 is also one of the few creatures the
Foundation actively wants to terminate, a

00:52:33.460 --> 00:52:38.270
task made that much harder given that 682
can regenerate its entire form from as little

00:52:38.270 --> 00:52:40.190
as a single cell.

00:52:40.190 --> 00:52:44.520
The Gate Guardian had already shown time and
time again that it was capable of massive

00:52:44.520 --> 00:52:48.430
destruction, and researchers working for the
Foundation hoped to harness that power to

00:52:48.430 --> 00:52:52.299
rid the world of SCP-682 for good.

00:52:52.299 --> 00:52:56.991
682 was placed on an unmanned vehicle and
carried to within one kilometer of the Gate

00:52:56.991 --> 00:52:57.991
Guardian.

00:52:57.991 --> 00:53:02.220
The guardian attacked the vehicle, seriously
wounding but not killing 682.

00:53:02.220 --> 00:53:08.680
It seems even the mighty SCP-001 couldn’t
kill the Hard-to-Destroy Reptile.

00:53:08.680 --> 00:53:13.740
While the researchers were disappointed with
this result, it is worth noting that 682 made

00:53:13.740 --> 00:53:16.520
a very interesting comment to the Guardian.

00:53:16.520 --> 00:53:21.079
682 mentioned that the Gate Guardian is “not
Uriel” but a “pretender”.

00:53:21.079 --> 00:53:25.730
Uriel is the archangel that some religious
texts describe as the guardian standing at

00:53:25.730 --> 00:53:31.109
the Gate of Eden with a fiery sword, so does
this mean that 682 knows that the Gate Guardian

00:53:31.109 --> 00:53:32.920
is not actually an angel?

00:53:32.920 --> 00:53:37.319
Or that the location it is guarding isn’t
the Garden of Eden at all?

00:53:37.319 --> 00:53:41.891
Any truth or meaning behind these comments
has, as of yet, been undetermined by the SCP

00:53:41.891 --> 00:53:42.891
Foundation.

00:53:42.891 --> 00:53:51.869
A later experiment involved both SCP-001 and
SCP-073, the anomaly otherwise known as Cain.

00:53:51.869 --> 00:53:57.190
Cain is a male humanoid of possible Arabic
descent whose arms, legs, spine, and shoulders

00:53:57.190 --> 00:54:01.940
are replaced in an almost cyborg-like fashion
with beryllium bronze.

00:54:01.940 --> 00:54:07.970
Much like The Gate Guardian, SCP-073 may also
be the same as the one mentioned in the Bible’s

00:54:07.970 --> 00:54:13.200
Book of Genesis who, according to the biblical
story, murdered his own brother Abel out of

00:54:13.200 --> 00:54:14.200
spite.

00:54:14.200 --> 00:54:18.710
As punishment for his actions, Cain was cursed
to eternally suffer for his wrongdoing.

00:54:18.710 --> 00:54:24.910
In the case of SCP-073, any damage inflicted
on him is deflected back to the attacker,

00:54:24.910 --> 00:54:27.890
but Cain is made to feel the pain of the attack.

00:54:27.890 --> 00:54:32.390
Any plants or plant-based matter withers and
rots in his presence, and he is cursed with

00:54:32.390 --> 00:54:37.320
a perfect memory, keeping him forever haunted
by his murder of Abel.

00:54:37.320 --> 00:54:41.350
When Cain was brought before The Gate Guardian,
an unknown incident occurred.

00:54:41.350 --> 00:54:46.171
The Foundation’s records are heavily expunged,
but we do know that somehow, Cain’s usual

00:54:46.171 --> 00:54:52.950
ability to deflect incoming damage back at
his attacker had no effect on SCP-001.

00:54:52.950 --> 00:54:59.530
The encounter left SCP-073 unconscious, and
even permanently blinded nearby research personnel.

00:54:59.530 --> 00:55:04.460
It was as a direct result of this incident
that the O5 Council demanded that no further

00:55:04.460 --> 00:55:11.320
experiments of any kind were to be conducted
on SCP-001, with the Administrator even filing

00:55:11.320 --> 00:55:18.000
an executive order that no SCPs be exposed
to the Guardian, and that SCP-001 was to never

00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:22.690
again be used for the attempted termination
of other SCPs.

00:55:22.690 --> 00:55:26.880
Of course, perhaps it wasn’t just the mistakes
of the past that made the Council decide that

00:55:26.880 --> 00:55:29.970
SCP-001 was best left alone.

00:55:29.970 --> 00:55:35.770
At some point, an erratic transmission was
received from Site 0 by Foundation personnel,

00:55:35.770 --> 00:55:38.850
detailing an XK-class end of the world scenario.

00:55:38.850 --> 00:55:43.540
In the transmission, the sender, believed
to be another member of the SCP Foundation,

00:55:43.540 --> 00:55:48.869
described an event during which The Gate Guardian
finally left its post, stepping away from

00:55:48.869 --> 00:55:51.839
the entrance to the Garden of Eden.

00:55:51.839 --> 00:55:55.400
“SCP-001 has left its location,” the sender
wrote.

00:55:55.400 --> 00:55:56.550
“The Gate is Open.

00:55:56.550 --> 00:55:57.980
They are riding forth.

00:55:57.980 --> 00:55:59.760
Oh God, it's so beautiful…”

00:55:59.760 --> 00:56:04.270
The transmission then goes on to repeat various
phrases including “The Lord shall reign

00:56:04.270 --> 00:56:09.180
forever” and “Hear, O Israel, The Lord,
our God, The Lord is one”.

00:56:09.180 --> 00:56:14.760
What can be inferred from the rambling transmission
is that the event being described is the end

00:56:14.760 --> 00:56:15.950
of the world.

00:56:15.950 --> 00:56:20.491
Some believe that, once God deems it time,
his angelic armies will lay waste to the Earth

00:56:20.491 --> 00:56:22.720
in order to remake it as a paradise.

00:56:22.720 --> 00:56:29.490
When this occurs, SCP-001, The Gate Guardian,
will open the gate he stands in front of,

00:56:29.490 --> 00:56:35.299
allowing the other beings like it to emerge
into our world, ready to cleanse it.

00:56:35.299 --> 00:56:38.240
Perhaps most interesting is the source of
the message.

00:56:38.240 --> 00:56:42.829
The transmission was received from within
the SCP Foundation, from Site 0, however when

00:56:42.829 --> 00:56:49.240
questioned by personnel, O5-14 told them that
no such message had been sent, or even existed.

00:56:49.240 --> 00:56:54.039
While some initially disregarded the transmission
telling of the end of the world as a hoax,

00:56:54.039 --> 00:56:56.750
it was then that a timestamp was discovered.

00:56:56.750 --> 00:57:02.940
This warning had not been sent from Site 0,
at least not yet, and was dated several years

00:57:02.940 --> 00:57:04.359
in the future.

00:57:04.359 --> 00:57:09.559
Despite this ominous warning of things to
come, The Gate Guardian remains inactive,

00:57:09.559 --> 00:57:12.140
standing at the threshold to Eden, waiting.

00:57:12.140 --> 00:57:15.930
The smell of fire and oil fills the air.

00:57:15.930 --> 00:57:21.190
The sound of gears grinding can be heard between
the explosions and shrieks of terror.

00:57:21.190 --> 00:57:25.720
A man runs out of his house, only to have
his leg grabbed by a metal arm and dragged

00:57:25.720 --> 00:57:28.589
back through his front door.

00:57:28.589 --> 00:57:33.960
SCP-001 leaves a trail of metal fragments
and mechanical parts on the ground in the

00:57:33.960 --> 00:57:35.780
wake of its destruction.

00:57:35.780 --> 00:57:41.960
Iron chains swing from its form, cast iron
gears whirl within it, a glowing light throbs

00:57:41.960 --> 00:57:44.200
form the center of its body.

00:57:44.200 --> 00:57:48.789
SCP-001 is consuming everything in its path.

00:57:48.789 --> 00:57:54.809
After incorporating the truck chassis into
its being, SCP-001 rolls in a lumbering fashion

00:57:54.809 --> 00:57:56.130
to the next house.

00:57:56.130 --> 00:57:59.339
It rips the gutters from the side of the building.

00:57:59.339 --> 00:58:02.100
Residents who live in the area flee their
neighborhood.

00:58:02.100 --> 00:58:06.839
All the while hoping that the mechanical monstrosity
skips over their house so they have something

00:58:06.839 --> 00:58:09.460
to return to if they make it out alive.

00:58:09.460 --> 00:58:14.069
A section of SCP-001’s undercarriage drops
away from the main body.

00:58:14.069 --> 00:58:17.809
It rolls down the street consuming more and
more material.

00:58:17.809 --> 00:58:21.039
The new entity resembles a human spine and
rib cage.

00:58:21.039 --> 00:58:23.789
It topples over unable to support itself.

00:58:23.789 --> 00:58:28.619
The rib like formations extend out to grab
anything and everything within reach.

00:58:28.619 --> 00:58:33.289
The newly incorporated material forms what
can only be described as a head.

00:58:33.289 --> 00:58:37.079
Light from within the eye sockets fixate on
nearby civilians.

00:58:37.079 --> 00:58:41.530
The metallic creature picks up the people
and places them inside its exposed, steel,

00:58:41.530 --> 00:58:42.530
rib cage.

00:58:42.530 --> 00:58:46.220
Then it turns and spots a woman helplessly
trying to crawl away.

00:58:46.220 --> 00:58:50.700
The creature reaches out with a spiked tentacle
and wraps it around the woman’s body.

00:58:50.700 --> 00:58:53.680
She is placed inside of the chest cavity.

00:58:53.680 --> 00:58:58.280
Moments later a severed hand falls out of
the entity and onto the ground.

00:58:58.280 --> 00:59:03.420
The mechanical monster continues to gather
bodies and materials, incorporating them into

00:59:03.420 --> 00:59:04.420
its frame.

00:59:04.420 --> 00:59:07.369
A growth begins to slowly expand on its back.

00:59:07.369 --> 00:59:12.710
It becomes so massive that the creature falls
over and uses its limbs to scurry into a nearby

00:59:12.710 --> 00:59:13.710
house.

00:59:13.710 --> 00:59:16.599
There is a sickening crunching sound as the
growth bursts.

00:59:16.599 --> 00:59:21.910
From within emerge three humanoid creatures
resembling the civilians that the entity had

00:59:21.910 --> 00:59:23.190
consumed earlier.

00:59:23.190 --> 00:59:27.840
A female with chains extending from her scalp
like dreadlocks stumbles away.

00:59:27.840 --> 00:59:30.910
The second humanoid is a man with cogs for
limbs.

00:59:30.910 --> 00:59:35.599
He examines the clock-like components that
have been incorporated into his body, then

00:59:35.599 --> 00:59:37.750
stares blankly into the distance.

00:59:37.750 --> 00:59:40.579
The third humanoid lies motionless on the
ground.

00:59:40.579 --> 00:59:42.060
He did not make it.

00:59:42.060 --> 00:59:45.410
The two functioning humanoids look at their
creator intently.

00:59:45.410 --> 00:59:50.280
For a moment nothing moves, then as if they
have been given orders telepathically, the

00:59:50.280 --> 00:59:54.490
half human half machine humanoids turn and
run away from the mayhem.

00:59:54.490 --> 01:00:00.430
A few weeks before the massacre caused by
what would be designated as SCP-001, the Foundation

01:00:00.430 --> 01:00:02.549
had been in contact with the Allied Occult
Initiative.

01:00:02.549 --> 01:00:07.420
There were rumors of an anomalous object in
Mexico being worshipped by a group of people

01:00:07.420 --> 01:00:11.170
who identified themselves as The Church of
the Broken God.

01:00:11.170 --> 01:00:15.559
Intel about the Church claimed their deity
was a small mechanical box filled with cogs

01:00:15.559 --> 01:00:16.750
and pistons.

01:00:16.750 --> 01:00:21.380
The box supposedly had supernatural abilities,
it was said to be able to communicate with

01:00:21.380 --> 01:00:24.700
congregants of The Church of the Broken God
telepathically.

01:00:24.700 --> 01:00:29.819
The devout worshiped the box, following any
order it gave, and in return they were filled

01:00:29.819 --> 01:00:33.630
with an emotion that could only be described
as divine.

01:00:33.630 --> 01:00:38.770
As World War II rages on in Europe, the Foundation
sends agents to recover anomalies in Mexico

01:00:38.770 --> 01:00:40.569
that might help with the war effort.

01:00:40.569 --> 01:00:44.230
While there, the Foundation force is tasked
with learning more about The Church of the

01:00:44.230 --> 01:00:45.420
Broken God.

01:00:45.420 --> 01:00:49.390
They are also ordered to investigate a town
near La Paz where there are troubling accounts

01:00:49.390 --> 01:00:52.500
of a mechanical anomalous creatures causing
mayhem.

01:00:52.500 --> 01:00:57.130
The agents make their way through Mexico gathering
various objects to bring back to Foundation

01:00:57.130 --> 01:00:59.240
sites in the United States.

01:00:59.240 --> 01:01:03.349
The unit loads all of the anomalies they’ve
recovered onto a train with the plan to check

01:01:03.349 --> 01:01:07.640
out the stories of the mechanical anomaly
they’ve heard about as they make their way

01:01:07.640 --> 01:01:08.640
to the U.S. border.

01:01:08.640 --> 01:01:11.840
The train heads north along rusted rails.

01:01:11.840 --> 01:01:16.170
Just outside of La Paz they come across a
broken down train filled with what looks to

01:01:16.170 --> 01:01:17.539
be refugees.

01:01:17.539 --> 01:01:21.460
When the Foundation unit goes to investigate
they find all of the refugees repeating the

01:01:21.460 --> 01:01:25.869
same words over and over again but they don’t
understand.

01:01:25.869 --> 01:01:30.070
The Foundation agents look at one another
confused, until one of them translates the

01:01:30.070 --> 01:01:31.770
words into English.

01:01:31.770 --> 01:01:36.490
The words the refugees are saying over and
over again are “la máquina, la máquina…

01:01:36.490 --> 01:01:37.961
the machine, the machine,”

01:01:37.961 --> 01:01:42.829
The commanding officer orders a squad of Foundation
agents to proceed up the tracks, to see if

01:01:42.829 --> 01:01:45.849
they can figure out what has the refugees
so scared.

01:01:45.849 --> 01:01:49.810
They make their way towards La Paz, disappearing
over the horizon.

01:01:49.810 --> 01:01:54.000
As the sun sets the remaining Foundation agents
hear gunshots in the distance.

01:01:54.000 --> 01:01:59.490
They stay awake all night remaining vigilant,
waiting for the exploratory squad, but morning

01:01:59.490 --> 01:02:01.980
comes without anyone returning.

01:02:01.980 --> 01:02:06.039
Three days later, the Foundation force still
has not seen anything since the exploratory

01:02:06.039 --> 01:02:07.539
squad left.

01:02:07.539 --> 01:02:12.309
Then as the sun sits lazily in the morning
sky, a lone figure is spotted walking down

01:02:12.309 --> 01:02:14.470
the tracks towards the trains.

01:02:14.470 --> 01:02:17.870
One of the agents on watch blows his whistle
and points to the figure.

01:02:17.870 --> 01:02:20.640
A squad of agents rushes towards the shadow
of a man.

01:02:20.640 --> 01:02:23.309
Their guns are raised, ready for anything.

01:02:23.309 --> 01:02:27.170
The figure drops to the ground and begins
to crawl along the tracks.

01:02:27.170 --> 01:02:31.570
The agents reach the fallen man, only to find
that he is one of their squadmates who had

01:02:31.570 --> 01:02:35.690
been sent up the tracks to investigate La
Paz several days before.

01:02:35.690 --> 01:02:37.010
The agent’s name is DeMarco.

01:02:37.010 --> 01:02:38.740
He is covered in blood.

01:02:38.740 --> 01:02:41.530
His clothes are in tatters and he has lost
a boot.

01:02:41.530 --> 01:02:46.680
DeMarco lies on his back with Foundation agents
standing around him, his eyes are wide and

01:02:46.680 --> 01:02:47.680
wild.

01:02:47.680 --> 01:02:51.970
He keeps babbling on about a “world eater,”
how the rest of his squad had been mulched,

01:02:51.970 --> 01:02:54.529
and he is the only one who made it out alive.

01:02:54.529 --> 01:02:59.079
The Foundation agents carry DeMarco back to
the makeshift base they created by the trains.

01:02:59.079 --> 01:03:04.210
They need to figure out a way to get the convoy
moving again, but whatever is up ahead has

01:03:04.210 --> 01:03:06.720
taken out an entire Foundation squad.

01:03:06.720 --> 01:03:10.359
It had to be something anomalous, but what
could it possibly be?

01:03:10.359 --> 01:03:13.710
The unit of Foundation agents prepare to move
towards La Paz.

01:03:13.710 --> 01:03:17.900
They start loading their rifles and check
the amount of ammunition and explosives available

01:03:17.900 --> 01:03:21.050
in case the containment process gets out of
hand.

01:03:21.050 --> 01:03:25.089
Just as they are about to leave the base,
a convoy appears on the horizon.

01:03:25.089 --> 01:03:29.420
It is an Allied Occult Initiative force preparing
to attack whatever it is that is devastating

01:03:29.420 --> 01:03:30.580
La Paz.

01:03:30.580 --> 01:03:35.750
This organization’s mission is not to secure,
contain, or protect, but to destroy.

01:03:35.750 --> 01:03:39.800
The Foundation may be in over their heads
on this one, and the joint force with the

01:03:39.800 --> 01:03:45.950
Allied Occult Initiative may be the only way
to stop what is now known as SCP-001.

01:03:45.950 --> 01:03:48.990
The AOI and Foundation force gears up for
battle.

01:03:48.990 --> 01:03:54.109
They set out for La Paz, and what they find
causes them to quake with fear.

01:03:54.109 --> 01:03:59.359
SCP-001 has consumed so much material it is
the size of a mountain.

01:03:59.359 --> 01:04:04.880
It moves like a tidal wave of mechanical destruction,
washing over the buildings and landscape under

01:04:04.880 --> 01:04:05.880
it.

01:04:05.880 --> 01:04:11.829
Whatever SCP-001 passes over is consumed and
added to its massive body.

01:04:11.829 --> 01:04:17.809
SCP-001 started as a small mechanical box
with cogs, but now has morphed into a gigantic

01:04:17.809 --> 01:04:19.619
metal death machine.

01:04:19.619 --> 01:04:25.059
The Church of the Broken God has finally met
their maker, as the small entity they once

01:04:25.059 --> 01:04:28.270
worshiped has now consumed all of its members.

01:04:28.270 --> 01:04:31.560
Their god is an all consuming monster.

01:04:31.560 --> 01:04:37.400
The AOI and Foundation forces do everything
they can to stop SCP-001 from continuing its

01:04:37.400 --> 01:04:38.779
reign of destruction.

01:04:38.779 --> 01:04:43.270
They fire barrage after barrage of bullets
and explosives into the mechanical anomaly.

01:04:43.270 --> 01:04:48.230
They bring in air support to try and damage
it from the skies, but nothing works.

01:04:48.230 --> 01:04:53.800
The AOI uses an artifact in their possession
to lure SCP-001 to the coast of the Pacific

01:04:53.800 --> 01:04:57.549
Ocean where a trap has been set for the so-called
god.

01:04:57.549 --> 01:05:01.069
The monstrous mechanical creature moves slowly
towards the water.

01:05:01.069 --> 01:05:05.349
It consumes abandoned cars, buildings, and
boats as it approaches the coastline.

01:05:05.349 --> 01:05:10.119
It even shovels large amounts of the earth
into its form, causing flames to spurt out

01:05:10.119 --> 01:05:12.170
from its inner workings.

01:05:12.170 --> 01:05:16.950
Smoke bellows from openings between different
mechanical components, like a volcano before

01:05:16.950 --> 01:05:18.700
it is about to erupt.

01:05:18.700 --> 01:05:24.380
Suddenly, seemingly from nowhere, a massive
cloud with a reddish tint appears in the sky.

01:05:24.380 --> 01:05:27.330
Air raid sirens can be heard in the distance.

01:05:27.330 --> 01:05:29.680
The enormous cloud begins to pulsate.

01:05:29.680 --> 01:05:32.049
Streaks of lightning shoot through the red
mist in the sky.

01:05:32.049 --> 01:05:35.680
It now sits directly over SCP-001.

01:05:35.680 --> 01:05:38.150
From within the cloud part of a ship can be
seen.

01:05:38.150 --> 01:05:42.569
It appears to be slightly damaged, electricity
flows over its hull.

01:05:42.569 --> 01:05:45.510
The vessel in the giant red cloud is classified
as SCP-2399.

01:05:45.510 --> 01:05:50.540
The underside of the vessel begins to glow
aqua blue.

01:05:50.540 --> 01:05:58.220
A blinding beam of light is ejected from SCP-2399,
which penetrates straight down and through

01:05:58.220 --> 01:05:59.320
SCP-001.

01:05:59.320 --> 01:06:02.099
For a moment everything is still.

01:06:02.099 --> 01:06:03.640
There is complete silence.

01:06:03.640 --> 01:06:09.880
Then as if SCP-001 is trying to reach up and
grab the vessel above it, a mechanical bulge

01:06:09.880 --> 01:06:10.940
reaches out.

01:06:10.940 --> 01:06:17.109
Before SCP-001 can grab the vessel above,
there is another bright flash of light.

01:06:17.109 --> 01:06:19.750
SCP-2399 blinks out of existence.

01:06:19.750 --> 01:06:23.690
The sound of grinding gears can be heard coming
from within SCP-001.

01:06:23.690 --> 01:06:27.420
It begins to shed its outer layers of metal.

01:06:27.420 --> 01:06:33.329
Then the entire structure that was SCP-001
collapses into the water and onto the beach.

01:06:33.329 --> 01:06:35.740
Giant cogs fall from the sky.

01:06:35.740 --> 01:06:38.109
Parts of vehicles embed themselves in the
sand.

01:06:38.109 --> 01:06:43.180
As the Foundation and AOI agents approach
the piles of scrap metal and mechanical components

01:06:43.180 --> 01:06:45.700
they see that some of them are still moving.

01:06:45.700 --> 01:06:50.490
It is as if an invisible powersource is still
pulsating through some of the machinery.

01:06:50.490 --> 01:06:54.520
The agents of the Foundation celebrate the
destruction of the giant mechanical beast,

01:06:54.520 --> 01:06:59.780
but little do they know this was only a piece
of the entity worshipped as the Broken God.

01:06:59.780 --> 01:07:03.210
The Foundation agents collect as many of the
still moving parts as they can.

01:07:03.210 --> 01:07:07.369
They find spinning gears, twitching pulleys,
and firing pistons.

01:07:07.369 --> 01:07:10.799
As the parts are separated from one another
and carried away from the main wreckage of

01:07:10.799 --> 01:07:15.859
SCP-001, they slowly stop moving and become
inactive.

01:07:15.859 --> 01:07:19.750
Some of the artifacts recovered were identified
as being connected to the Church of the Broken

01:07:19.750 --> 01:07:20.750
God.

01:07:20.750 --> 01:07:26.920
These artifacts are found closer to the middle
of what was once a mountain sized SCP-001.

01:07:26.920 --> 01:07:32.040
Hundreds of anomalous artifacts are collected
and transported to SCP Foundation sites.

01:07:32.040 --> 01:07:35.890
Collecting the broken parts of SCP-001 is
relatively safe.

01:07:35.890 --> 01:07:40.130
However, some agents get too close to the
larger moving parts, getting caught in them

01:07:40.130 --> 01:07:41.780
and losing a body part or two.

01:07:41.780 --> 01:07:46.400
But most agents proceed with caution and survive
the collection ordeal with their arms and

01:07:46.400 --> 01:07:48.900
legs still attached to their bodies.

01:07:48.900 --> 01:07:52.829
Dive teams are sent into the water to recover
parts that have sunk to the bottom of the

01:07:52.829 --> 01:07:53.829
sea.

01:07:53.829 --> 01:07:55.590
One of the divers is a local from the area.

01:07:55.590 --> 01:08:00.089
He is hired to bring up the heart of the machine,
since he is an experienced diver used to free

01:08:00.089 --> 01:08:04.130
diving to great depths to collect oysters
from the bottom of the bay.

01:08:04.130 --> 01:08:07.470
The diver enters the water and swims down
into the murky depths.

01:08:07.470 --> 01:08:13.150
He secures straps around the heart of SCP-001
and pulls hard on the rope, as an indication

01:08:13.150 --> 01:08:15.819
to the surface that it is ready to be hauled
up.

01:08:15.819 --> 01:08:18.330
The salvage team on the surface begins to
pull.

01:08:18.330 --> 01:08:21.630
There is a second slight tug on the rope,
then it goes slack.

01:08:21.630 --> 01:08:23.370
The team continues to pull.

01:08:23.370 --> 01:08:28.450
When they get the heart to the surface they
are horrified at what else comes up with it.

01:08:28.450 --> 01:08:31.949
Tangled in the ropes is the lifeless body
of the diver.

01:08:31.949 --> 01:08:35.739
His head is smashed between two moving pieces
of the heart.

01:08:35.739 --> 01:08:40.480
It looks as if he shoved his head between
the slabs of metal himself.

01:08:40.480 --> 01:08:45.679
The salvage team untangles the body, rolls
it off the deck, and back into the ocean.

01:08:45.679 --> 01:08:50.960
The mechanical box which was the heart of
SCP-001 is offloaded onto the shore, but as

01:08:50.960 --> 01:08:55.730
the Foundation prepares to move it to a containment
facility, the weather starts to deteriorate.

01:08:55.730 --> 01:08:59.370
Hurricane force winds sweep across the water
and batter the coast.

01:08:59.370 --> 01:09:02.860
The heart is kept in a secured storage warehouse
until it can be moved.

01:09:02.860 --> 01:09:07.230
The people living in the village nearby complain
of hearing voices and rashes so itchy that

01:09:07.230 --> 01:09:09.790
they practically tear their skin off.

01:09:09.790 --> 01:09:13.720
Once the storm passes, the Foundation agents
load the heart onto a ship.

01:09:13.720 --> 01:09:17.299
It is to be transported to a Foundation site
just across the border.

01:09:17.299 --> 01:09:19.650
The ocean seems calm and serene.

01:09:19.650 --> 01:09:23.190
The Foundation ship undocks and begins its
journey up the coast.

01:09:23.190 --> 01:09:27.239
Not too long after beginning its journey the
ship slowly drifts off course.

01:09:27.239 --> 01:09:31.839
It is as if the crew has stopped manning their
posts, and the ship is being controlled by

01:09:31.839 --> 01:09:33.380
a mind of its own.

01:09:33.380 --> 01:09:38.460
The Foundation ship crashes and sinks somewhere
in the Pacific Ocean, never to be found, and

01:09:38.460 --> 01:09:44.740
more importantly, the heart of SCP-001 doesn’t
make it to the Foundation site.

01:09:44.740 --> 01:09:47.330
Years later a man is walking along the beach.

01:09:47.330 --> 01:09:48.330
He hears something.

01:09:48.330 --> 01:09:52.540
It sounds like someone pounding on a large
drum to the rhythm of a heartbeat.

01:09:52.540 --> 01:09:54.800
The man walks towards the sound.

01:09:54.800 --> 01:09:58.680
Something is drawing him forward, closer and
closer to the heartbeat.

01:09:58.680 --> 01:10:01.690
He walks and walks until the beating stops.

01:10:01.690 --> 01:10:04.290
He bends down and moves the sand aside.

01:10:04.290 --> 01:10:08.170
He spots the corner of a mechanical box sticking
out of the white sand.

01:10:08.170 --> 01:10:11.760
The man digs deeper and pulls out the small
box.

01:10:11.760 --> 01:10:15.030
Inside he can see gears whirling and pistons
firing.

01:10:15.030 --> 01:10:17.540
He holds the box close to his own heart.

01:10:17.540 --> 01:10:19.840
It seems to speak to him.

01:10:19.840 --> 01:10:21.960
The man brings the box back to town.

01:10:21.960 --> 01:10:26.990
He starts to worship the box and soon more
and more people in the area join the new religion.

01:10:26.990 --> 01:10:31.460
They cast aside their old beliefs and focus
on the powerful entity contained within the

01:10:31.460 --> 01:10:32.460
box.

01:10:32.460 --> 01:10:38.730
God is not dead… at least not yet, but the
prophecies of The Church of the Broken God

01:10:38.730 --> 01:10:44.650
say that when the heart is found, the God
will reassemble itself once again.

01:10:44.650 --> 01:10:52.489
Then the Unbroken God will destroy all other
false deities, until only he remains.

01:10:52.489 --> 01:10:55.739
Corpses littered the facility, around twenty
in total.

01:10:55.739 --> 01:11:00.650
Their massacre had unfolded in a matter of
seconds despite their advanced armor and heavy

01:11:00.650 --> 01:11:01.650
weaponry.

01:11:01.650 --> 01:11:06.410
Their killer, wielding an ancient sword he’d
somehow pulled from thin air, looked upon

01:11:06.410 --> 01:11:08.230
them with disdain.

01:11:08.230 --> 01:11:10.460
Weak, unworthy opponents.

01:11:10.460 --> 01:11:15.210
He breathed heavily - His torso was covered
with bullet wounds and many had punctured

01:11:15.210 --> 01:11:16.210
his lungs.

01:11:16.210 --> 01:11:20.380
It was enough to kill a normal man ten times
over, but not him.

01:11:20.380 --> 01:11:22.260
He was the ultimate warrior.

01:11:22.260 --> 01:11:24.060
The perfect killing machine.

01:11:24.060 --> 01:11:28.440
He would need to seek out an enemy more fitting
for his legendary combat skills.

01:11:28.440 --> 01:11:32.960
He fled from the chamber into a connecting
hallway - where a giant, metal door slammed

01:11:32.960 --> 01:11:34.110
shut behind him.

01:11:34.110 --> 01:11:37.010
At the other end of the hall another door
did the same.

01:11:37.010 --> 01:11:41.490
He laughed at the thought of someone thinking
he could be trapped so easily and charged

01:11:41.490 --> 01:11:42.490
towards it.

01:11:42.490 --> 01:11:46.010
But then, large valves began to open all around
him.

01:11:46.010 --> 01:11:50.350
Torrents of freezing seawater began pouring
in, filling up the chamber and submerging

01:11:50.350 --> 01:11:52.680
him before he could reach the door.

01:11:52.680 --> 01:11:58.150
The warrior fought for breath, and he held
it far longer than any mortal man could - especially

01:11:58.150 --> 01:12:02.500
considering the state of his lungs, but water
always wins.

01:12:02.500 --> 01:12:07.400
He soon gave his last gasp, and floated, lifeless,
in the hallway.

01:12:07.400 --> 01:12:12.219
And soon after his body turned to dust and
disappeared in the briny water.

01:12:12.219 --> 01:12:13.530
But he would be back.

01:12:13.530 --> 01:12:15.550
He’d always be back.

01:12:15.550 --> 01:12:17.270
His brother was a different story.

01:12:17.270 --> 01:12:22.860
Tall and handsome, with a strange Sumerian
rune tattooed on his forehead, he was practically

01:12:22.860 --> 01:12:27.610
a pacifist and spent most of his days reading,
conversing with the staff, and wandering the

01:12:27.610 --> 01:12:29.870
facility of his own accord.

01:12:29.870 --> 01:12:33.429
Upon hearing of the latest incident at the
facility, he gave a sigh.

01:12:33.429 --> 01:12:36.750
He knew, on some level, that all of this was
his fault.

01:12:36.750 --> 01:12:39.420
It’d been centuries, millennia even.

01:12:39.420 --> 01:12:42.520
But was it too late to make things right?

01:12:42.520 --> 01:12:45.790
Six days later, the two are standing face
to face.

01:12:45.790 --> 01:12:50.310
This meeting had been a long time coming,
but it was always destined to end in blood

01:12:50.310 --> 01:12:51.310
and pain.

01:12:51.310 --> 01:12:56.590
The man with the runic tattoo was unarmed
- the only thing he carried was his regrets.

01:12:56.590 --> 01:13:00.870
The warrior, eyes full of burning fury, drew
his sword.

01:13:00.870 --> 01:13:04.130
And not long after, a head hit the floor.

01:13:04.130 --> 01:13:05.929
Who are these two strange men?

01:13:05.929 --> 01:13:08.830
And what is the significance of this fatal
meeting?

01:13:08.830 --> 01:13:12.139
In our own universe, these two may never meet
again.

01:13:12.139 --> 01:13:15.720
But that doesn’t mean there isn’t a universe
out there where they will.

01:13:15.720 --> 01:13:19.360
And it is that universe where today’s tale
springs from.

01:13:19.360 --> 01:13:24.340
The story between these two began a long,
long time ago, when they were both set on

01:13:24.340 --> 01:13:25.430
a course of destruction.

01:13:25.430 --> 01:13:30.949
But to learn how these two finally met once
again, we only need to go back a few days.

01:13:30.949 --> 01:13:35.520
While they seem more human than a lot of the
beings under the SCP Foundation’s watchful

01:13:35.520 --> 01:13:42.280
eyes, there’s no doubt that these two are
anomalous - they’re known as SCP - 073 and

01:13:42.280 --> 01:13:46.910
SCP - 076, but better known as Cain and Able.

01:13:46.910 --> 01:13:51.100
From the name alone, most people with a basic
knowledge of the bible could tell that these

01:13:51.100 --> 01:13:55.060
two have a connection, but the particulars
were largely a mystery to the Foundation.

01:13:55.060 --> 01:13:59.100
They wanted to know how much of the story
was actually true.

01:13:59.100 --> 01:14:05.300
SCP Researchers approached SCP - 073 - aka,
Cain - and asked if he’d be interested in

01:14:05.300 --> 01:14:08.090
reuniting with his brother one last time.

01:14:08.090 --> 01:14:14.600
It took Cain three days to answer: Yes, but
on one condition - that he was the only person

01:14:14.600 --> 01:14:16.370
who could abort the mission.

01:14:16.370 --> 01:14:20.690
The Foundation mulled over this requirement
for three days before the O5 Council finally

01:14:20.690 --> 01:14:23.880
made a decision - Cross-testing approved.

01:14:23.880 --> 01:14:30.050
These two brothers, separated by millennia,
would finally meet again - and the SCP Foundation

01:14:30.050 --> 01:14:32.860
would get to watch what happened when they
did.

01:14:32.860 --> 01:14:37.351
Of course, for safety reasons, the cross-test
would have to take place in 076’s containment

01:14:37.351 --> 01:14:41.330
facility - a bedrock chamber two hundred meters
beneath the sea.

01:14:41.330 --> 01:14:45.780
That would be the closest thing to “safe”
this fateful meeting could ever be.

01:14:45.780 --> 01:14:50.929
Though safe was really a relative term when
it came to SCP - 076.

01:14:50.929 --> 01:14:56.020
His escape attempts were as frequent and unpredictable
as they were deadly, and everyone who’d

01:14:56.020 --> 01:14:58.639
ever worked with him knew exactly why.

01:14:58.639 --> 01:15:03.840
To the untrained eye, it would seem strange
to create such a complex facility for a three-meter-squared

01:15:03.840 --> 01:15:08.210
stone cube, known as SCP - 076 - 01.

01:15:08.210 --> 01:15:10.620
But the cube isn’t what’s being locked
up here.

01:15:10.620 --> 01:15:17.739
The real danger comes from the corpse stored
inside - known as SCP - 076 - 02, but better

01:15:17.739 --> 01:15:19.210
known as Able.

01:15:19.210 --> 01:15:24.389
He’s a lean, olive-skinned man who appears
to be in his late twenties, but his most distinctive

01:15:24.389 --> 01:15:29.060
physical feature is the fact he’s covered
in an elaborate network of arcane and occult

01:15:29.060 --> 01:15:34.460
tattoos, largely of scowling, demonic faces
- similar to those found on members of the

01:15:34.460 --> 01:15:35.460
Yakuza.

01:15:35.460 --> 01:15:39.640
Whenever Able’s corpse reanimates, as it
does at random intervals, everyone in his

01:15:39.640 --> 01:15:41.719
vicinity is in terrible danger.

01:15:41.719 --> 01:15:46.130
He’s capable of pulling bladed weapons out
of miniature dimensional rifts that appear

01:15:46.130 --> 01:15:50.179
around him, though he does this so quickly
that it seems as though the weapons are simply

01:15:50.179 --> 01:15:52.560
materializing in his hands.

01:15:52.560 --> 01:15:56.500
Despite the increasingly complex efforts to
contain him, Able has been able to breach

01:15:56.500 --> 01:16:02.070
containment and go on brutal rampages multiple
times, killing scores of Foundation personnel

01:16:02.070 --> 01:16:03.730
in the process.

01:16:03.730 --> 01:16:07.360
Able possesses superhuman strength, speed,
and durability.

01:16:07.360 --> 01:16:11.640
During prior containment breaches, he was
able to shrug off rounds from .50 caliber

01:16:11.640 --> 01:16:12.640
machine guns.

01:16:12.640 --> 01:16:14.950
He’s torn through reinforced steel doors.

01:16:14.950 --> 01:16:19.750
He’s even swatted bullets from both handguns
and assault rifles out of the air with a length

01:16:19.750 --> 01:16:21.310
of steel rebar.

01:16:21.310 --> 01:16:26.170
Only killing him can truly end one of these
rampages - and the Foundation has had to go

01:16:26.170 --> 01:16:30.060
to terrifying lengths in order to achieve
this during past containment breaches.

01:16:30.060 --> 01:16:35.139
He’s been drowned, asphyxiated, crushed,
burned to death with a thermite grenade directly

01:16:35.139 --> 01:16:40.720
inserted into his chest cavity, and even disintegrated
by the activation of the facility’s on-site

01:16:40.720 --> 01:16:42.270
nuclear warhead.

01:16:42.270 --> 01:16:48.290
This may seem like overkill, but if Able ever
made his way into a major population center,

01:16:48.290 --> 01:16:53.620
the fatalities would be… well, of biblical
proportions.

01:16:53.620 --> 01:16:58.611
Even death can’t keep him down for long
- his body will rapidly decompose, and reappear

01:16:58.611 --> 01:17:02.239
intact within SCP - 076 - 01.

01:17:02.239 --> 01:17:07.060
There’s no telling when he’ll reawaken,
and his periods of inactivity can range from

01:17:07.060 --> 01:17:09.130
hours to years.

01:17:09.130 --> 01:17:14.239
Because of this, he must be constantly observed
by guards highly proficient in close combat,

01:17:14.239 --> 01:17:18.909
always ready to go toe to toe with perhaps
the most dangerous melee combatant in history.

01:17:18.909 --> 01:17:23.550
He’s such a proficient killer that there
was once a project aimed at weaponizing Able,

01:17:23.550 --> 01:17:27.120
but this turned out to be a disastrous failure
for the Foundation.

01:17:27.120 --> 01:17:30.840
When they ran out of missions to give him,
Able’s thirst for blood caused him to turn

01:17:30.840 --> 01:17:35.810
his blade on his allies with no remorse, hacking
them up with the same ruthless abandon he

01:17:35.810 --> 01:17:38.140
gave his assigned enemies.

01:17:38.140 --> 01:17:41.560
Interestingly, Able does seem to have a twisted
sense of honour.

01:17:41.560 --> 01:17:45.820
He has a respect for combatants capable of
providing him with a real challenge - and

01:17:45.820 --> 01:17:50.330
has even expressed concern for guards he considers
to be respectable adversaries.

01:17:50.330 --> 01:17:52.310
But don’t be fooled.

01:17:52.310 --> 01:17:59.290
There is no reasoning with Able - either you
kill him, or he kills you, and trust us, he’s

01:17:59.290 --> 01:18:00.940
much better at it than you are.

01:18:00.940 --> 01:18:05.570
While he’s often overshadowed by world-ending
anomalies or more talkative mass killers like

01:18:05.570 --> 01:18:10.890
SCP - 682, Able is one of the most deadly
creatures known to the Foundation.

01:18:10.890 --> 01:18:15.440
Able’s counterpart, 073, is an entirely
different story.

01:18:15.440 --> 01:18:20.489
Despite his namesake being the first biblical
murderer, this Cain is a far more enigmatic

01:18:20.489 --> 01:18:21.489
figure.

01:18:21.489 --> 01:18:25.570
A tall man in his early thirties appearing
to be of Middle Eastern descent, he has two

01:18:25.570 --> 01:18:30.340
very notable physical characteristics - The
untranslated Sumerian symbol tattooed onto

01:18:30.340 --> 01:18:35.489
his forehead, and the fact that several of
his body parts - namely, his arms, legs, spinal

01:18:35.489 --> 01:18:40.840
cord, and shoulder blades - have been replaced
by mysterious prosthetics of unknown origin.

01:18:40.840 --> 01:18:46.780
Unlike Able, Cain is polite, non-confrontational,
articulate, and communicative.

01:18:46.780 --> 01:18:51.460
He’s even allowed to wander the facility
he’s housed in freely, though with certain

01:18:51.460 --> 01:18:52.570
regulations.

01:18:52.570 --> 01:18:56.969
Namely that Cain is never permitted to come
into contact with plant life or uncovered

01:18:56.969 --> 01:18:57.969
ground.

01:18:57.969 --> 01:19:02.659
This is because, in spite of the fact Cain
doesn’t appear to harbor any malicious intent,

01:19:02.659 --> 01:19:08.330
direct contact with him causes plants to wither
and die, and the ground to become infertile.

01:19:08.330 --> 01:19:12.640
If Cain was ever introduced into a natural
environment again, he could unwittingly cause

01:19:12.640 --> 01:19:15.830
an ecological catastrophe with his mere presence.

01:19:15.830 --> 01:19:20.880
In that sense, he can be almost as dangerous
to large populations as Able.

01:19:20.880 --> 01:19:25.880
However, Cain’s danger to flora is only
one of his several anomalous qualities.

01:19:25.880 --> 01:19:30.280
Another is extraordinary mental capabilities,
and a near-perfect memory.

01:19:30.280 --> 01:19:35.300
His memory and ability to recall is so good,
that some Foundation personnel have suggested

01:19:35.300 --> 01:19:40.320
using Cain’s mind as a kind of backup server
for the Foundation’s collective knowledge.

01:19:40.320 --> 01:19:45.100
But perhaps his most well-known anomalous
trait is his ability to act as a kind of immortal

01:19:45.100 --> 01:19:46.630
human voodoo doll.

01:19:46.630 --> 01:19:52.140
That’s right: Any damage inflicted on Cain
causes no permanent injury to him, and is

01:19:52.140 --> 01:19:54.520
reflected back on the perpetrator.

01:19:54.520 --> 01:19:59.070
While Cain has remarked on still being able
to feel the pain of these assaults, he’s

01:19:59.070 --> 01:20:00.560
functionally immortal.

01:20:00.560 --> 01:20:05.310
This damage-reflecting ability has even made
performing certain kinds of tests impossible

01:20:05.310 --> 01:20:09.690
- as doctors attempting to draw blood from
Cain have found that their sample was actually

01:20:09.690 --> 01:20:13.860
their own blood, and their skin exhibited
the telltale bruising and puncture marks of

01:20:13.860 --> 01:20:14.950
blood testing.

01:20:14.950 --> 01:20:19.929
But, of most interest to the Foundation right
now was the fact that Cain has shown prior

01:20:19.929 --> 01:20:21.350
knowledge of Able.

01:20:21.350 --> 01:20:23.530
However, he was cagey when questioned.

01:20:23.530 --> 01:20:28.370
He refused to add any additional information,
and commented that it would be best if he

01:20:28.370 --> 01:20:30.420
and Able were never brought into contact.

01:20:30.420 --> 01:20:34.120
But what does “never” really mean when
you live forever?

01:20:34.120 --> 01:20:38.870
Cain finally did agree to the test, and while
nobody knows what caused Cain’s change of

01:20:38.870 --> 01:20:43.350
heart, the Foundation knew better than to
push him and potentially get the entire mission

01:20:43.350 --> 01:20:44.350
scrapped.

01:20:44.350 --> 01:20:48.480
Cain was taken from his facility, and transported
to the access point of Able’s underwater

01:20:48.480 --> 01:20:49.480
prison.

01:20:49.480 --> 01:20:54.190
The experiment’s design was simple: Cain
would occupy a temporary residence in Able’s

01:20:54.190 --> 01:20:58.540
containment facility until he next reanimated,
at which point, the interaction between them

01:20:58.540 --> 01:21:00.520
would be closely observed.

01:21:00.520 --> 01:21:05.020
Perhaps it would take weeks, months, or even
years before Able once again awoke and left

01:21:05.020 --> 01:21:08.659
his cube, but when he did, Cain would be there.

01:21:08.659 --> 01:21:13.530
Thankfully, as Cain whispered soothing words
into Able’s tomb, the resurrection took

01:21:13.530 --> 01:21:14.929
only minutes.

01:21:14.929 --> 01:21:18.650
If you were expecting a heartwarming reunion,
think again.

01:21:18.650 --> 01:21:23.320
Cain tried to apologize, but Able immediately
struck him with a decapitating blow which

01:21:23.320 --> 01:21:28.950
- due to Cain's damage reflecting properties
- caused him to sever his own head instead.

01:21:28.950 --> 01:21:33.719
Cain remained at Able’s side as he regenerated,
and as soon as Able did he immediately tried

01:21:33.719 --> 01:21:35.080
killing Cain again.

01:21:35.080 --> 01:21:38.600
It went on like this again and again and again.

01:21:38.600 --> 01:21:45.239
It was an arduous process, and eventually,
even Able began to tire of it.

01:21:45.239 --> 01:21:47.989
The duo fell into a tearful embrace.

01:21:47.989 --> 01:21:51.250
Able asked his brother why he killed him,
so long ago.

01:21:51.250 --> 01:21:56.020
And Cain apologized, saying it was the actions
of a younger and more foolish man.

01:21:56.020 --> 01:22:01.260
In that moment, the two finally reconciled,
and having fulfilled their bargain with their

01:22:01.260 --> 01:22:04.220
creator, both finally crumbled into dust.

01:22:04.220 --> 01:22:06.260
Peace at last.

01:22:06.260 --> 01:22:11.360
As we said, this didn’t happen to the Cain
and Able of our universe, but when universes

01:22:11.360 --> 01:22:16.770
are more numerous than grains of sand in an
endless desert, such a thing has indeed happened

01:22:16.770 --> 01:22:20.750
somewhere out there - perhaps in a kinder
universe than our own.

01:22:20.750 --> 01:22:26.120
We can only hope that our Cain and Able may
someday get to meet and find the same resolution,

01:22:26.120 --> 01:22:30.590
but until then, these brothers will remain
one of the most dangerous and fascinating

01:22:30.590 --> 01:22:33.000
duos in the Foundation’s catalogue.

01:22:33.000 --> 01:22:36.920
“Every time a bell rings, an angel gets
its wings.”

01:22:36.920 --> 01:22:41.270
It’s an iconic line from “It’s a Wonderful
Life” and even if you don’t believe in

01:22:41.270 --> 01:22:44.160
angels, it’s a pleasant image.

01:22:44.160 --> 01:22:49.070
After all, angels are the embodiment of goodness
and light, so an angel getting its wings has

01:22:49.070 --> 01:22:50.870
to be a good thing, right?

01:22:50.870 --> 01:22:56.720
Well, as anyone who’s ever eaten one too
many Christmas cookies can tell you, it’s

01:22:56.720 --> 01:22:59.650
possible to have too much of a good thing.

01:22:59.650 --> 01:23:05.270
Even something that sounds like the embodiment
of all things good, in theory, can become

01:23:05.270 --> 01:23:08.390
deadly when taken to the extreme.

01:23:08.390 --> 01:23:13.790
That is where SCP-469, also known as the Many-Winged
Angel, comes in.

01:23:13.790 --> 01:23:19.680
This angel-like creature is anything but innocent
and in fact it has been responsible for multiple

01:23:19.680 --> 01:23:24.480
deaths of SCP Foundation personnel during
its captivity.

01:23:24.480 --> 01:23:31.600
SCP-469 may be deadly, but it is also undeniably
beautiful in a mysterious, ethereal way.

01:23:31.600 --> 01:23:36.520
When first seen, it appears to be nothing
more than a massive pile of pristine white

01:23:36.520 --> 01:23:39.350
feathers, like something out of a pillow commercial.

01:23:39.350 --> 01:23:44.090
The pile measures 24 feet in diameter and
weighs at least two tons.

01:23:44.090 --> 01:23:49.320
However, like many of the entities contained
within the walls of the Foundation’s countless

01:23:49.320 --> 01:23:53.770
containment sites, all is not as it seems
with 469.

01:23:53.770 --> 01:23:58.489
What looks at first glance to be a pile of
feathers is in fact a dense, curled mass of

01:23:58.489 --> 01:24:00.070
giant wings.

01:24:00.070 --> 01:24:06.639
The wings vary in size, from the tiny wingspan
of a sparrow to the staggering 3.6-meter wingspan

01:24:06.639 --> 01:24:08.820
of the wandering albatross.

01:24:08.820 --> 01:24:13.590
The one thing they have in common is their
plumage, with each wing being covered with

01:24:13.590 --> 01:24:16.190
the same glossy white feathers.

01:24:16.190 --> 01:24:21.080
The Foundation was able to perform a series
of X-rays on the mass of wings, revealing

01:24:21.080 --> 01:24:23.719
a skeletal structure beneath the feathers.

01:24:23.719 --> 01:24:26.630
Like those of a bird, the wings’ bones are
hollow.

01:24:26.630 --> 01:24:32.250
However, they are unnaturally soft and flexible,
allowing for a range of motion that no known

01:24:32.250 --> 01:24:34.200
birds possess.

01:24:34.200 --> 01:24:38.620
This accounts for the curvature of the wings,
and their ability to coil tightly into each

01:24:38.620 --> 01:24:39.620
other.

01:24:39.620 --> 01:24:44.770
The X-Ray also provided the first, and only
recorded glimpse at the creature hiding underneath

01:24:44.770 --> 01:24:46.179
all of the feathers.

01:24:46.179 --> 01:24:50.619
At the center of the layers upon layers of
wings, is a humanoid creature, curled into

01:24:50.619 --> 01:24:51.869
a fetal position.

01:24:51.869 --> 01:24:57.989
In defiance of the laws of natural anatomy,
every single wing appears to be fused to this

01:24:57.989 --> 01:24:58.989
creature’s spine.

01:24:58.989 --> 01:25:03.550
How it would be able to move under the weight
of these wings, or if it even could, is as

01:25:03.550 --> 01:25:05.340
of yet unknown.

01:25:05.340 --> 01:25:13.290
The first Foundation personnel lost to SCP-469
were D-class personnel, D-112 and D-624, who

01:25:13.290 --> 01:25:17.540
were sent in to investigate the nature of
the creature and attempt to contact the humanoid

01:25:17.540 --> 01:25:20.270
entity identified on the X-rays.

01:25:20.270 --> 01:25:26.179
112 and 624 entered the room, equipped with
gloves and protective eye gear, as scientists

01:25:26.179 --> 01:25:29.920
watched the situation unfold on a monitor
on a video feed.

01:25:29.920 --> 01:25:34.400
No one expected much to come of the encounter,
the working hypothesis was that the layers

01:25:34.400 --> 01:25:39.670
of feathers would simply be too thick to get
through without seriously damaging the bones.

01:25:39.670 --> 01:25:45.180
It would be a fairly uneventful experiment,
or so they thought.

01:25:45.180 --> 01:25:50.430
112 approached SCP-469 first, and attempted
to part a section of its feathers with his

01:25:50.430 --> 01:25:53.290
hands as 624 stood back and observed.

01:25:53.290 --> 01:25:58.199
The moment his fingertips touched the feathers,
a rustling sound filled the room.

01:25:58.199 --> 01:26:03.610
The feathers began to quiver, shaking as if
all waking up at once from a deep slumber.

01:26:03.610 --> 01:26:08.340
Suddenly, in the blink of an eye, the hundreds
and hundreds of wings unfurled and pulled

01:26:08.340 --> 01:26:10.640
112 into their depths.

01:26:10.640 --> 01:26:15.300
He was swept into a swirl of feathers and,
within seconds, he had disappeared from view

01:26:15.300 --> 01:26:16.300
completely.

01:26:16.300 --> 01:26:20.960
Though 624 and the scientists watching on
their monitor could no longer see him…they

01:26:20.960 --> 01:26:22.659
could certainly hear him.

01:26:22.659 --> 01:26:27.150
From the moment the wings pulled him into
the sea of feathers, 112 had begun to scream

01:26:27.150 --> 01:26:28.350
in agony.

01:26:28.350 --> 01:26:33.150
His screams persisted, growing louder and
more desperate even as his voice cracked and

01:26:33.150 --> 01:26:34.210
grew weak.

01:26:34.210 --> 01:26:38.409
624 stood, frozen in place with fear and shock.

01:26:38.409 --> 01:26:43.490
624 was ordered to attempt to retrieve 112
from the feathers, but made no move to do

01:26:43.490 --> 01:26:44.490
so.

01:26:44.490 --> 01:26:49.970
He simply stared at the feathers, eyes wide,
face pale, as the pained shrieks of his colleague

01:26:49.970 --> 01:26:53.409
bounced off the sterile white walls of the
containment room.

01:26:53.409 --> 01:26:58.010
A guard called over the intercom, threatening
to terminate 624 if he did not attempt to

01:26:58.010 --> 01:27:01.980
remove 112 from SCP-469’s grasp.

01:27:01.980 --> 01:27:07.280
This warning seemed to shock 624 back into
action, and he made a run for the center feathers,

01:27:07.280 --> 01:27:09.340
arms up to protect his face.

01:27:09.340 --> 01:27:13.360
Again, the sound of rustling as the feathers
began to quake.

01:27:13.360 --> 01:27:18.600
The wings unfurled once more, and 624 did
not even have a chance to turn back before

01:27:18.600 --> 01:27:22.650
he was pulled in to meet the same dismal fate
as the other D Class.

01:27:22.650 --> 01:27:26.610
His screams of pain joined 112’s as the
scientists watching over the monitor could

01:27:26.610 --> 01:27:28.540
do nothing to help them.

01:27:28.540 --> 01:27:32.840
As the two men cried out in pain and horror
from within their winged prison, something

01:27:32.840 --> 01:27:36.580
began to happen that the scientists had never
seen before.

01:27:36.580 --> 01:27:41.350
The feathers started to shake again, faster
than before, and at first the wings appeared

01:27:41.350 --> 01:27:43.070
to be unfolding again.

01:27:43.070 --> 01:27:46.010
Upon a second look though, it was clear they
hadn’t moved.

01:27:46.010 --> 01:27:48.800
There were simply more of them now.

01:27:48.800 --> 01:27:53.330
As the men continued to scream, more feathers
appeared, the wings stretching out and elongating,

01:27:53.330 --> 01:27:56.449
and new wings sprouting as if from nowhere.

01:27:56.449 --> 01:28:03.300
SCP-469 appeared to be feeding on the sound
of the screams, and using that energy to expand.

01:28:03.300 --> 01:28:07.780
It was only after several long minutes when
the screaming finally stopped that the growth

01:28:07.780 --> 01:28:09.739
of the wings did too.

01:28:09.739 --> 01:28:15.920
At this point, the wings shifted again, expelling
the bodies of 112 and 624 from within its

01:28:15.920 --> 01:28:18.840
folds, dropping them limply on the ground.

01:28:18.840 --> 01:28:24.710
Though their deaths were unfortunate, the
loss of 112 and 624 did reveal some new information

01:28:24.710 --> 01:28:26.300
about SCP-469.

01:28:26.300 --> 01:28:32.270
First, that it could grow, and apparently
needed to feed on sounds in order to do so.

01:28:32.270 --> 01:28:37.580
Second, that it was deadly to humans, and
most likely to other living things as well.

01:28:37.580 --> 01:28:43.550
Autopsies of 112 and 624’s corpses would
later reveal exactly what happened to them,

01:28:43.550 --> 01:28:47.160
and how SCP-469 kills its prey.

01:28:47.160 --> 01:28:51.900
Though 469’s feathers may look as though
they would be soft to the touch, each feather

01:28:51.900 --> 01:28:56.450
is actually made up of sharp barbs that are
capable of piercing clothing and skin.

01:28:56.450 --> 01:29:00.860
These barbs release a neurotoxin into the
system that activates every pain receptor

01:29:00.860 --> 01:29:02.670
in the body of the victim.

01:29:02.670 --> 01:29:07.310
The neurotoxin present in these feathers has
not been identified anywhere else in nature,

01:29:07.310 --> 01:29:12.389
but is somewhat similar in structure and function
to the neurotoxins excreted by the cone snail

01:29:12.389 --> 01:29:15.420
and in the bite of the blue-ringed octopus.

01:29:15.420 --> 01:29:20.140
In addition to the pain-inducing neurotoxin,
the feathers also carry several unidentified

01:29:20.140 --> 01:29:22.020
stimulant compounds, which seem to be intended
to keep the victim awake for as long as possible.

01:29:22.020 --> 01:29:25.909
Where the neurotoxin on its own would induce
enough pain for the affected party to pass

01:29:25.909 --> 01:29:30.620
out almost immediately, the stimulants serve
to keep the victim conscious.

01:29:30.620 --> 01:29:36.900
SCP Foundation scientists posit that this
is so that 469 can get as much noise, in this

01:29:36.900 --> 01:29:41.929
case in the form of screams, out of its prey
as possible and achieve maximum growth before

01:29:41.929 --> 01:29:45.179
the captive creature dies or goes into shock.

01:29:45.179 --> 01:29:50.440
Further experiments confirmed this theory,
and showed that SCP 469 will react similarly

01:29:50.440 --> 01:29:56.161
when exposed to any living creature capable
of making a sound and experiencing pain, not

01:29:56.161 --> 01:29:57.850
just humans.

01:29:57.850 --> 01:30:03.110
Nonliving matter though, including dead animals,
elicit no response from 469.

01:30:03.110 --> 01:30:07.760
Additional experiments were then undertaken
that involved applying various different sounds

01:30:07.760 --> 01:30:12.010
in order to test their effect on SCP 469’s
growth.

01:30:12.010 --> 01:30:16.929
Though it feeds on any sounds produced in
its presence, it seems to respond most strongly

01:30:16.929 --> 01:30:22.620
to musical sounds, exhibiting a particularly
strong response to classical music.

01:30:22.620 --> 01:30:27.290
No sound elicits a stronger reaction from
this creature, however, than the sound of

01:30:27.290 --> 01:30:28.290
ringing bells.

01:30:28.290 --> 01:30:33.150
It is rumored that when a bell was rung in
the presence of the 469, the humanoid at the

01:30:33.150 --> 01:30:37.650
center of the feathers is said to have moved
for the first time on record.

01:30:37.650 --> 01:30:42.389
Apparently whatever is at the center appeared
to “wake up” and unfurl its wings, revealing

01:30:42.389 --> 01:30:43.389
itself.

01:30:43.389 --> 01:30:47.550
But unfortunately, all security footage of
this incident has been wiped, and the data

01:30:47.550 --> 01:30:52.130
has been expunged from the record leaving
the creature’s true form a mystery.

01:30:52.130 --> 01:30:56.620
You may be remembering that four members of
Foundation personnel on record were lost to

01:30:56.620 --> 01:31:00.969
SCP-469, and that only two have been mentioned
so far.

01:31:00.969 --> 01:31:06.360
The second pair of casualties resulted when
the Foundation attempted to terminate SCP

01:31:06.360 --> 01:31:07.719
469.

01:31:07.719 --> 01:31:11.820
Believing that there was no more scientific
benefit to keeping it alive, or at least that

01:31:11.820 --> 01:31:17.530
the possible benefits did not outweigh the
risks, it was ordered that SCP-469 be terminated

01:31:17.530 --> 01:31:19.090
by any means necessary.

01:31:19.090 --> 01:31:25.070
Two skilled personnel, Dr. Jones and Dr. Smith,
were sent into the containment facility in

01:31:25.070 --> 01:31:28.350
hazmat gear, armed with several sharp instruments.

01:31:28.350 --> 01:31:32.830
They were to attempt to use these to cut through
the forest of feathers and soft bones until

01:31:32.830 --> 01:31:34.910
they could reach the humanoid at the center.

01:31:34.910 --> 01:31:39.480
It was presumed that once they did and the
creature no longer had the protection of its

01:31:39.480 --> 01:31:43.489
poisonous feathers, that it would be relatively
easy to kill.

01:31:43.489 --> 01:31:46.030
They could not have been more wrong.

01:31:46.030 --> 01:31:50.680
Dr. Jones approached the dense cover of feathers
with a pair of sharpened gardening shears,

01:31:50.680 --> 01:31:53.340
while Dr. Smith opted for a machete.

01:31:53.340 --> 01:31:55.300
At first, the strategy appeared to be working.

01:31:55.300 --> 01:32:00.200
Dr. Jones made several quick cuts, with feathers
fluttering to the floor and sticking to the

01:32:00.200 --> 01:32:05.370
Hazmat suit as Dr. Smith slashed into the
feathers with his machete, making similarly

01:32:05.370 --> 01:32:06.780
promising progress.

01:32:06.780 --> 01:32:12.010
However, the situation quickly took a turn
for the worse when Dr. Jones dropped her shears

01:32:12.010 --> 01:32:13.989
and let out a bloodcurdling scream.

01:32:13.989 --> 01:32:18.650
The feathers had taken a little longer to
get through the suit to her skin, but somehow

01:32:18.650 --> 01:32:21.850
they had managed to find a way just the same.

01:32:21.850 --> 01:32:26.331
Smith grabbed Jones and attempted to make
a break for it, but he was too slow, and far

01:32:26.331 --> 01:32:28.540
too close to the feathers already.

01:32:28.540 --> 01:32:33.460
The wings wrapped around them and swallowed
them both up, leaving the researchers outside

01:32:33.460 --> 01:32:38.890
helpless to do anything but listen to their
screams and wait for them to go quiet.

01:32:38.890 --> 01:32:44.880
After several minutes they finally did, and
the now larger SCP-469 had officially claimed

01:32:44.880 --> 01:32:47.440
another two Foundation personnel.

01:32:47.440 --> 01:32:52.230
Obviously, 469 could not be terminated using
any methods that would place the responsible

01:32:52.230 --> 01:32:54.530
personnel within its grasp.

01:32:54.530 --> 01:32:56.180
That was simply too risky.

01:32:56.180 --> 01:33:00.840
So, the Foundation selected a team of D-class
personnel to attempt to burn the feathers

01:33:00.840 --> 01:33:03.040
with an array of flamethrowers.

01:33:03.040 --> 01:33:07.980
Though the feathers were vulnerable to fire
and began to blacken and disintegrate on contact,

01:33:07.980 --> 01:33:13.890
the sound of the flames being expelled was
loud enough to feed SCP 469.

01:33:13.890 --> 01:33:17.820
Its growth was so quick in response to the
noise that the fire could not keep up with

01:33:17.820 --> 01:33:21.130
the amount of new feathers and wings being
produced.

01:33:21.130 --> 01:33:26.659
By the time the flamethrowers ran out of propellant,
469 was the same size as it had been when

01:33:26.659 --> 01:33:27.679
they started.

01:33:27.679 --> 01:33:31.570
Other termination methods have been discussed,
including the possibility of submerging the

01:33:31.570 --> 01:33:37.150
entire creature in a highly corrosive acid,
but so far this has not yet been attempted.

01:33:37.150 --> 01:33:41.380
Whatever they end up trying, it is clear that
nothing that produces a significant amount

01:33:41.380 --> 01:33:44.119
of noise will be able to kill 469.

01:33:44.119 --> 01:33:46.210
So, where is it now?

01:33:46.210 --> 01:33:50.010
What’s become of this perverse angel with
the never-ending wings?

01:33:50.010 --> 01:33:53.920
Currently, it is kept isolated in an airtight,
soundproof chamber where nothing can trigger

01:33:53.920 --> 01:33:56.310
the growth of any more wings.

01:33:56.310 --> 01:33:57.790
So, what is it?

01:33:57.790 --> 01:33:58.790
An angel?

01:33:58.790 --> 01:33:59.790
A demon?

01:33:59.790 --> 01:34:02.310
A twisted, mutated bird of some kind?

01:34:02.310 --> 01:34:05.030
It is entirely possible we will never know.

01:34:05.030 --> 01:34:09.580
But It’s a Wonderful Life had something
right, even if by accident.

01:34:09.580 --> 01:34:16.210
Every time a bell rings, something, twisted
and deadly though it may be, gets its wings.

01:34:16.210 --> 01:34:18.580
Man, it’s even better on the fifteenth read...

01:34:18.580 --> 01:34:19.580
Oh, hello!

01:34:19.580 --> 01:34:22.040
I didn’t see you there, dear viewers of
SCP Explained.

01:34:22.040 --> 01:34:27.610
I’m on break between supervising SCP-682
termination attempts and inspecting the mops

01:34:27.610 --> 01:34:33.420
we use on SCP-173’s leavings, so I decided
to do what all the cool people are doing in

01:34:33.420 --> 01:34:39.119
their spare time right now: Rereading Chainsaw
Man, the hit manga by Japanese author and

01:34:39.119 --> 01:34:41.810
artist Tatsuki Fujimoto.

01:34:41.810 --> 01:34:46.550
For the uninitiated, it’s the story of Denji,
a poor young man from Japan who makes his

01:34:46.550 --> 01:34:51.720
living hunting devils - dangerous creatures
that are embodiments of mankind’s greatest

01:34:51.720 --> 01:34:52.810
fears.

01:34:52.810 --> 01:34:57.790
But when that living leads to him dying at
the hands of a gang of zombie yakuza - believe

01:34:57.790 --> 01:35:03.619
me, it makes sense in context - he bonds with
the legendary Chainsaw devil and is reborn

01:35:03.619 --> 01:35:10.930
as Chainsaw Man, an unconventional superhero
who chainsaws first and asks questions later.

01:35:10.930 --> 01:35:15.659
Naturally, I was eager to see how one of our
own bloodthirsty killers would fare against

01:35:15.659 --> 01:35:21.120
Denji’s chainsaws of fury, so I selected
the most violent, battle-hardened, and carnage-hungry

01:35:21.120 --> 01:35:28.550
anomaly out there: SCP-076-2, the immortal
warrior known as Able.

01:35:28.550 --> 01:35:31.790
The two of them have a surprising amount in
common.

01:35:31.790 --> 01:35:36.969
Both are effectively immortal and can revive
after sustaining massive physical injuries.

01:35:36.969 --> 01:35:42.030
Both absolutely love to fight with their array
of deadly weapons and anomalous strength.

01:35:42.030 --> 01:35:46.630
Both have been part of experimental operations
groups - with Denji being a member of Japan’s

01:35:46.630 --> 01:35:52.710
Public Safety Devil Hunter’s Division 4,
and Able being an ex-member of the SCP Foundation’s

01:35:52.710 --> 01:35:58.790
disastrous Pandora’s Box Mobile Task Force,
most of which he later massacred out of boredom.

01:35:58.790 --> 01:36:03.580
You can probably see why these two really
did feel like the perfect match-up.

01:36:03.580 --> 01:36:08.440
So after forcing the trusty Anon-O-Tron 6000
to read every currently available volume of

01:36:08.440 --> 01:36:13.830
Chainsaw Man, and compute years of Able’s
gruesome battle data, I’ve set up the perfect

01:36:13.830 --> 01:36:16.650
simulation for your viewing pleasure.

01:36:16.650 --> 01:36:21.600
And hey, fellow fans of the manga, isn’t
it horrifying that even we beat MAPPA to the

01:36:21.600 --> 01:36:24.690
punch of animating this thing?

01:36:24.690 --> 01:36:29.190
God, that joke will age poorly if that anime
comes out before this.

01:36:29.190 --> 01:36:34.409
Anyway, let’s crank this machine into action
and let her rip!

01:36:34.409 --> 01:36:36.219
Japan, 1997.

01:36:36.219 --> 01:36:38.050
Everything is roasting in the July Heat.

01:36:38.050 --> 01:36:43.070
Men In Black, Harrison Ford’s Air Force
One, and Air Bud are hitting theaters for

01:36:43.070 --> 01:36:44.800
the first time.

01:36:44.800 --> 01:36:46.320
Everything is right with the world.

01:36:46.320 --> 01:36:50.489
That’s why, over in the headquarters of
the Public Safety Devil Hunting Department,

01:36:50.489 --> 01:36:55.900
Denji - our Chainsaw-loving hero - is being
praised by his kind boss and mentor figure,

01:36:55.900 --> 01:36:56.900
Makima.

01:36:56.900 --> 01:37:01.310
A lovable, supportive woman who will never
do anything wrong.

01:37:01.310 --> 01:37:05.960
She even loves dogs - how could a person who
loves dogs ever be evil?

01:37:05.960 --> 01:37:11.100
That very morning, Denji, in his Chainsaw
Man form, managed to defeat the Accidentally

01:37:11.100 --> 01:37:15.030
Making A Mistake On Your Tax Forms And Now
You’re Going To Prison Devil, who had been

01:37:15.030 --> 01:37:17.190
terrorizing downtown Tokyo.

01:37:17.190 --> 01:37:21.840
It was a challenging battle, but in the end,
he’d managed to turn the tables and defeat

01:37:21.840 --> 01:37:24.110
the creature by setting it on fire.

01:37:24.110 --> 01:37:30.000
Needless to say, Makima was extremely pleased
with Denji’s work here, but now, she had

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:32.330
considerable graver news to impart.

01:37:32.330 --> 01:37:37.040
She’d gotten word from an envoy of another
organization that hunts down dangerous and

01:37:37.040 --> 01:37:43.080
anomalous creatures - the SCP Foundation - that
an extremely lethal entity had breached their

01:37:43.080 --> 01:37:46.270
containment and was now somewhere in Japan.

01:37:46.270 --> 01:37:51.489
The entity in question was not a devil, and
thereby would be working on a different rule

01:37:51.489 --> 01:37:52.489
set.

01:37:52.489 --> 01:37:58.910
Makima opened a file faxed to her by the Foundation
- yes, remember, this is set in 1997 - and

01:37:58.910 --> 01:38:01.670
gave Denji the crucial lowdown.

01:38:01.670 --> 01:38:06.840
Several hours ago, the entity known as Able
had resurrected from his huge, black sarcophagus

01:38:06.840 --> 01:38:12.369
in the underwater chamber of the classified
facility, Containment Area 25b.

01:38:12.369 --> 01:38:16.909
After waking up, Able had slaughtered his
way through the entire base, killing every

01:38:16.909 --> 01:38:23.159
SCP Foundation operative in his path and then
swimming out into the Pacific Ocean.

01:38:23.159 --> 01:38:28.239
Sometime after that, he infiltrated a Japanese
cargo ship and murdered all the workers on

01:38:28.239 --> 01:38:32.630
board, before steering the ship back towards
the land of the rising sun, where he hoped

01:38:32.630 --> 01:38:34.840
to claim even more victims.

01:38:34.840 --> 01:38:40.420
Makima told Denji that it would fall to him
and his associates to stop this Able, with

01:38:40.420 --> 01:38:44.160
a little help from the SCP Foundation’s
intelligence.

01:38:44.160 --> 01:38:50.290
But be warned: Able is an incredible combatant
with extreme physical strength and durability,

01:38:50.290 --> 01:38:53.500
as well as surprising tactical intelligence.

01:38:53.500 --> 01:38:58.630
It wouldn’t be an easy fight, but Makima
promised that if Denji won, she’d hug him

01:38:58.630 --> 01:39:01.280
and go to a nearby karaoke bar with him.

01:39:01.280 --> 01:39:05.440
Denji replied, “Consider him dead already,
Miss Makima.”

01:39:05.440 --> 01:39:10.340
Meanwhile, Able was walking through the slums
of Tokyo, marveling at the neon signs for

01:39:10.340 --> 01:39:12.210
bars and clubs.

01:39:12.210 --> 01:39:14.860
His journey to Japan hadn’t been an accident.

01:39:14.860 --> 01:39:18.860
Able had been to Japan once before, in the
year 1605.

01:39:18.860 --> 01:39:25.000
He’d faced the legendary Japanese philosopher
and Swordsman Miyamoto Musashi, considered

01:39:25.000 --> 01:39:28.679
by many to be one of the greatest warriors
in human history.

01:39:28.679 --> 01:39:33.750
Able had dueled Musashi - who famously wielded
two Katanas at once - in the hills of the

01:39:33.750 --> 01:39:38.349
Harima Province, where, after a tense battle,
Musashi cut him down.

01:39:38.349 --> 01:39:42.909
Able would not resurrect again during Musashi’s
lifetime, but the battle gave him a deep and

01:39:42.909 --> 01:39:46.060
abiding respect for the legendary warrior.

01:39:46.060 --> 01:39:50.890
Able knew that if the opportunity ever rose
again, he would return to Japan, in hopes

01:39:50.890 --> 01:39:54.260
of experiencing such a brilliant battle yet
again.

01:39:54.260 --> 01:39:58.140
But the industrial and technological boom
had changed so much.

01:39:58.140 --> 01:40:03.060
It was no longer the quiet and pastoral Japan
he’d experienced, but a booming epicenter

01:40:03.060 --> 01:40:05.100
of trade and commerce.

01:40:05.100 --> 01:40:07.810
He found it all strange and perplexing.

01:40:07.810 --> 01:40:12.150
Suddenly, he found himself surrounded by a
group of Japanese street toughs, many of them

01:40:12.150 --> 01:40:13.420
wielding switchblades.

01:40:13.420 --> 01:40:18.540
They laughed at his strange outfit, which
to them looked like an old, worn bedsheet.

01:40:18.540 --> 01:40:22.170
One of the smarter members of the group had
already decided to go home when the others

01:40:22.170 --> 01:40:28.670
made up their mind to mug Able - the warrior’s
extensive tattoos made him look like a Middle-Eastern

01:40:28.670 --> 01:40:29.670
yakuza don.

01:40:29.670 --> 01:40:32.389
The rest, however, were happy to take their
chances with him.

01:40:32.389 --> 01:40:37.200
“Empty your pockets, if that goofy toga
even has pockets,” the leader said, holding

01:40:37.200 --> 01:40:38.239
up his switchblade.

01:40:38.239 --> 01:40:39.969
“Unless you wanna get cut.”

01:40:39.969 --> 01:40:43.760
Able just smirked and drew a pair of long,
obsidian daggers.

01:40:43.760 --> 01:40:49.139
In the following moment, the alley was filled
with screams, then was silent yet again.

01:40:49.139 --> 01:40:54.290
Able walked on, breathing a sigh of disappointment
at how incredibly mediocre this first fight

01:40:54.290 --> 01:40:57.599
had been, his blades dripping with fresh blood.

01:40:57.599 --> 01:41:01.000
Musashi is rolling in his grave, Able thought
to himself.

01:41:01.000 --> 01:41:06.190
Meanwhile, across town, Denji and the rest
of Division 4 were mobilizing.

01:41:06.190 --> 01:41:11.580
It was him, the serious, sword-wielding Aki,
and the adorable, pathologically-lying Blood

01:41:11.580 --> 01:41:12.739
Fiend, Power.

01:41:12.739 --> 01:41:17.340
They’d been told over the phone by a man
named Dr. Bright that Able would be relatively

01:41:17.340 --> 01:41:22.219
easy to track down - He’s not known for
his subtlety; all you need to do is follow

01:41:22.219 --> 01:41:25.790
the trail of carnage he causes wherever he
goes.

01:41:25.790 --> 01:41:30.550
From the way he talks about him, it seems
almost as though Dr. Bright bears a personal

01:41:30.550 --> 01:41:32.480
grudge against Able.

01:41:32.480 --> 01:41:33.880
How strange.

01:41:33.880 --> 01:41:36.219
Power didn’t seem intimidated.

01:41:36.219 --> 01:41:40.900
She proudly proclaimed, “I don’t think
this battle will be difficult at all.

01:41:40.900 --> 01:41:47.239
In fact, I’ve faced this Able before and
defeated him handily.”

01:41:47.239 --> 01:41:48.500
Aki sighed and asked.

01:41:48.500 --> 01:41:50.540
“When did this happen?”

01:41:50.540 --> 01:41:53.989
“Last Tuesday, of course!”

01:41:53.989 --> 01:41:55.230
she replied.

01:41:55.230 --> 01:41:59.940
Power had only heard about Able this morning,
but Denji and Aki had learned better than

01:41:59.940 --> 01:42:01.820
to dispute her at this point.

01:42:01.820 --> 01:42:06.389
Suddenly, a large television screen that had
been previously relaying an ad for a cutting-edge

01:42:06.389 --> 01:42:09.969
stereo system cut to an emergency news report.

01:42:09.969 --> 01:42:15.219
There’d been a horrific incident in downtown
Tokyo, where a bar had been attacked and most

01:42:15.219 --> 01:42:20.210
of its patrons murdered by a deranged, tattooed
man carrying a pair of huge swords.

01:42:20.210 --> 01:42:24.710
Aki immediately recognized the place - The
bar was yakuza-owned.

01:42:24.710 --> 01:42:29.810
If this Able was on the hunt for worthy opponents,
it makes all the sense in the world that Japan’s

01:42:29.810 --> 01:42:33.050
iconic crime syndicates would be his first
target.

01:42:33.050 --> 01:42:38.210
Denji, Aki, and Power knew exactly where they
needed to go.

01:42:38.210 --> 01:42:41.300
Over at the bar, Able was having a whale of
a time.

01:42:41.300 --> 01:42:45.730
Innocent patrons were running and screaming,
while the Yakuza engaged in an all-out war

01:42:45.730 --> 01:42:48.680
with the terrifying, inhuman warrior.

01:42:48.680 --> 01:42:50.820
Several of them had already been cut down.

01:42:50.820 --> 01:42:56.820
Two Yakuza soldiers behind the bar were reloading
illegal Uzis and preparing to return fire.

01:42:56.820 --> 01:43:00.199
Both were sweating, terrified by the sudden,
random attack.

01:43:00.199 --> 01:43:05.290
When they’d shot him before, he’d managed
to dodge most of the bullets, and expertly

01:43:05.290 --> 01:43:07.349
block the rest with his swords.

01:43:07.349 --> 01:43:09.570
Who the hell had sent this monster?

01:43:09.570 --> 01:43:11.060
Was he with the Triads?

01:43:11.060 --> 01:43:12.060
The Russian mob?

01:43:12.060 --> 01:43:15.940
Or some devil summoned by the Japanese government
to crack down on them?

01:43:15.940 --> 01:43:19.620
Whatever the case, he seemed almost impossible
to kill.

01:43:19.620 --> 01:43:22.210
The two men stood back up and opened fire.

01:43:22.210 --> 01:43:26.340
Able held his two swords and spun them like
a propeller, blocking all the bullets almost

01:43:26.340 --> 01:43:27.340
effortlessly.

01:43:27.340 --> 01:43:32.179
He then produced another dagger, seemingly
from thin air, and threw it directly into

01:43:32.179 --> 01:43:35.599
the heart of one of the two remaining Yakuza
behind the bar.

01:43:35.599 --> 01:43:40.369
He dropped to the ground, dead instantly,
leaving only his friend alive in a bar full

01:43:40.369 --> 01:43:41.650
of corpses.

01:43:41.650 --> 01:43:45.250
That’s when Able noticed a decorative katana
behind the bar.

01:43:45.250 --> 01:43:49.429
He smiled and ordered the surviving Yakuza
soldier to pick up the sword and give him

01:43:49.429 --> 01:43:50.980
a real fight.

01:43:50.980 --> 01:43:56.650
The hapless mobster realized in that moment
that this guy was truly crazy, whoever he

01:43:56.650 --> 01:43:57.650
was.

01:43:57.650 --> 01:43:59.030
But what choice did he have now?

01:43:59.030 --> 01:44:04.570
With terror in his heart, the last surviving
Yakuza grabbed the katana and unsheathed it.

01:44:04.570 --> 01:44:07.760
“Good,” Able said, his voice deep and
menacing.

01:44:07.760 --> 01:44:09.780
“Now come fight me.

01:44:09.780 --> 01:44:15.180
Let’s see if you last a few seconds longer
than your worthless friends, shall we?”

01:44:15.180 --> 01:44:16.849
He did not.

01:44:16.849 --> 01:44:21.030
The second the Yakuza ran towards Able, and
the ancient Swordsman swiped at him with one

01:44:21.030 --> 01:44:25.090
of his blades, cutting through the katana
and then the opponent holding it.

01:44:25.090 --> 01:44:31.560
A puny gangster never stood a chance against
a deadly immortal warrior, and Able was furious.

01:44:31.560 --> 01:44:34.980
The last time he was here, he faced a truly
expert killer,

01:44:34.980 --> 01:44:38.869
who’d even managed to end Able’s life
in single combat.

01:44:38.869 --> 01:44:42.280
And now he was slaying insects in a karaoke
bar.

01:44:42.280 --> 01:44:43.280
Pathetic…

01:44:43.280 --> 01:44:45.369
Suddenly, his ears pricked up.

01:44:45.369 --> 01:44:49.130
He turned to see a red axe flying at his head
at incredible speeds.

01:44:49.130 --> 01:44:53.960
With his superhuman reflexes, he managed to
dodge just in time, but the axe still cleaved

01:44:53.960 --> 01:44:56.500
off a chunk of his hair as it passed.

01:44:56.500 --> 01:45:00.280
Able could see the one who threw it standing
at the entrance to the bar: It was the Blood

01:45:00.280 --> 01:45:04.510
Fiend, Power, who’d made the axe out of
her own blood.

01:45:04.510 --> 01:45:09.860
Standing next to her were Denji and Aki, Denji
wielding an axe and Aki stoically observing.

01:45:09.860 --> 01:45:14.409
“Damn, Miss Makima promised we’d do karaoke
at this bar if I beat you,” Denji said.

01:45:14.409 --> 01:45:16.190
“You’re going down for this.”

01:45:16.190 --> 01:45:19.250
Able smiled and pulled out another pair of
blades.

01:45:19.250 --> 01:45:21.489
“Finally!” he roared.

01:45:21.489 --> 01:45:24.920
“Warriors who fight the old-fashioned way.

01:45:24.920 --> 01:45:28.510
I feared the years had stolen you all from
me.”

01:45:28.510 --> 01:45:30.969
Power stepped forward, producing another blood
axe from nowhere.

01:45:30.969 --> 01:45:31.969
She yelled, “Tremble in fear, Able.

01:45:31.969 --> 01:45:41.389
‘Tis I, your archnemesis, the mighty Power!”

01:45:41.389 --> 01:45:46.540
Able had literally never seen her before in
his thousands of years of life, but he appreciated

01:45:46.540 --> 01:45:49.690
that these warriors were at least able to
match his level of drama.

01:45:49.690 --> 01:45:52.730
As far as he was concerned, the fight was
on.

01:45:52.730 --> 01:45:56.420
But even Able didn’t know the level of fighting
he was getting in for here.

01:45:56.420 --> 01:45:59.840
As he charged forward, the trio split, immediately
surrounding him.

01:45:59.840 --> 01:46:02.370
Good tactics, Able thought to himself.

01:46:02.370 --> 01:46:04.310
Already, this was promising.

01:46:04.310 --> 01:46:08.190
Aki, who had remained quiet up to this point,
attacked first.

01:46:08.190 --> 01:46:12.440
He drew a tanto knife from his suit jacket
and slashed at Able with impressive speed.

01:46:12.440 --> 01:46:17.411
But unlike three of the other combatants in
this situation, Aki was only human, which

01:46:17.411 --> 01:46:19.900
gave him a serious disadvantage.

01:46:19.900 --> 01:46:23.040
Able decided it would be best to put him out
of commission first.

01:46:23.040 --> 01:46:26.790
With a quick and brutal kick to the chest,
Aki was thrown against the wall with the majority

01:46:26.790 --> 01:46:28.500
of his ribs broken.

01:46:28.500 --> 01:46:33.750
Revved up by his own bloodlust, Able turned
to Denji and Power and grinned like a maniac.

01:46:33.750 --> 01:46:36.849
This was already the most fun he’d had in
a long time.

01:46:36.849 --> 01:46:38.210
Who are these people?

01:46:38.210 --> 01:46:40.060
Doesn’t matter, he thought.

01:46:40.060 --> 01:46:42.380
They’ll be dead soon anyway.

01:46:42.380 --> 01:46:46.500
While Able was still locked in thought, Power
pulled out a comically large hammer made out

01:46:46.500 --> 01:46:49.370
of her own blood, and brought it down towards
Able.

01:46:49.370 --> 01:46:53.960
He was surprised by the sudden attack - Did
this girl have the same weapon-producing powers

01:46:53.960 --> 01:46:54.960
as him!?

01:46:54.960 --> 01:46:57.250
This just keeps getting more interesting!

01:46:57.250 --> 01:46:59.710
“‘Tis the end, Able!”

01:46:59.710 --> 01:47:01.460
Power screamed as the hammer came down.

01:47:01.460 --> 01:47:07.080
“You have once again been defeated by the
mighty Power!”

01:47:07.080 --> 01:47:10.750
Again, just to clarify, these two had never
met each other.

01:47:10.750 --> 01:47:12.849
But it was already too late.

01:47:12.849 --> 01:47:16.139
Able punched upwards, his clenched fist colliding
with the hammer.

01:47:16.139 --> 01:47:20.650
He hit it with such terrifying force that
Power’s blood hammer shattered against his

01:47:20.650 --> 01:47:21.650
knuckles.

01:47:21.650 --> 01:47:25.750
In that same instant, Able noticed Denji running
at him with an axe from behind.

01:47:25.750 --> 01:47:29.790
Able produced another obsidian dagger and
threw it into Denji’s forehead, dropping

01:47:29.790 --> 01:47:31.740
him to the ground immediately.

01:47:31.740 --> 01:47:32.900
Pathetic.

01:47:32.900 --> 01:47:36.860
Power tried to produce another weapon, but
she’d used up too much blood already.

01:47:36.860 --> 01:47:41.880
Before she had a chance to make anything substantial,
Able sprung forwards with terrifying speed,

01:47:41.880 --> 01:47:43.680
trying to land a killing blow.

01:47:43.680 --> 01:47:46.980
But even weakened, Power was freakishly fast.

01:47:46.980 --> 01:47:50.860
She was able to dodge his blow and kick him
in the ribs, momentarily stunning him.

01:47:50.860 --> 01:47:55.150
Of course, she took the time to gloat, putting
her hands on her hips and laughing victoriously.

01:47:55.150 --> 01:47:59.070
“Need a second to catch your breath, Able?

01:47:59.070 --> 01:48:01.760
It is to be expected.

01:48:01.760 --> 01:48:04.250
None can keep up with me!”

01:48:04.250 --> 01:48:05.889
She grandiosely announced.

01:48:05.889 --> 01:48:11.199
“Perhaps you should just give up and agree
to become my servant.

01:48:11.199 --> 01:48:15.870
I might even teach you a thing or two about
fighting—“

01:48:15.870 --> 01:48:19.960
Suddenly, Able was standing right in front
of her, squeezing her throat with his iron

01:48:19.960 --> 01:48:20.960
grip.

01:48:20.960 --> 01:48:25.440
He smiled, flashing teeth, and said, “If
you want to kill, kill.

01:48:25.440 --> 01:48:26.440
Don’t talk.”

01:48:26.440 --> 01:48:31.210
With a surprisingly minimal amount of strength,
he squeezed and heard a crunch from Power’s

01:48:31.210 --> 01:48:32.210
neck.

01:48:32.210 --> 01:48:33.460
He dropped her limp body to the ground.

01:48:33.460 --> 01:48:38.190
Lucky for Power, Able wasn’t aware that
a Fiend like Power can survive an injury like

01:48:38.190 --> 01:48:40.680
this as long as she’s fed some more blood.

01:48:40.680 --> 01:48:42.980
Instead, he just sighed in disappointment.

01:48:42.980 --> 01:48:46.490
“Is that all you weaklings have to offer?”

01:48:46.490 --> 01:48:47.490
He bellowed.

01:48:47.490 --> 01:48:51.740
Aki, barely conscious after being kicked against
the wall, remained just conscious enough to

01:48:51.740 --> 01:48:56.290
activate his contract with a powerful beast
known as the Fox Devil.

01:48:56.290 --> 01:49:01.469
He twists his hands into a strange gesture
and whispers the word, “Kon”, before falling

01:49:01.469 --> 01:49:02.469
unconscious.

01:49:02.469 --> 01:49:03.760
But that’s still enough.

01:49:03.760 --> 01:49:09.510
Suddenly, a giant demonic fox claw burst through
the wall of the bar, spraying dust and rubble

01:49:09.510 --> 01:49:10.710
everywhere.

01:49:10.710 --> 01:49:13.469
Able was definitely not expecting that.

01:49:13.469 --> 01:49:17.580
He dodged several times as the claw swiped
for him, often barely missing him.

01:49:17.580 --> 01:49:22.920
For its last strike, it lunged forward and
raked four claw marks across his chest.

01:49:22.920 --> 01:49:25.020
Able was shocked by the sudden pain.

01:49:25.020 --> 01:49:26.030
It felt fantastic.

01:49:26.030 --> 01:49:31.920
He pulled a long, obsidian spear out of one
of his pocket dimensions, and forced it down

01:49:31.920 --> 01:49:36.790
through the Fox Devil’s paw and into the
ground, pinning it in place.

01:49:36.790 --> 01:49:42.030
After a moment of thrashing, the claw dissipated
into smoke, lending Able another victory - though

01:49:42.030 --> 01:49:47.010
even he would admit this was a more exciting
fight than the other ones had been.

01:49:47.010 --> 01:49:48.010
Was that it?

01:49:48.010 --> 01:49:52.190
Had he gained total victory once more, just
like he so often did these days?

01:49:52.190 --> 01:49:56.090
He was about to take pity on himself when
Denji rose up behind him.

01:49:56.090 --> 01:49:58.060
“How about a rematch?”

01:49:58.060 --> 01:49:59.199
Denji asked.

01:49:59.199 --> 01:50:00.199
Able grinned.

01:50:00.199 --> 01:50:01.340
He liked this kid.

01:50:01.340 --> 01:50:04.270
“Challenge me, child,” Able said.

01:50:04.270 --> 01:50:06.239
“Well, since you asked...”

01:50:06.239 --> 01:50:07.360
Denji smirked.

01:50:07.360 --> 01:50:10.900
Denji reached into his shirt and grabbed the
rip cord emerging from his chest.

01:50:10.900 --> 01:50:13.610
It was time to go into overdrive on this thing.

01:50:13.610 --> 01:50:19.040
He gave it a mighty yank, and like the rev
of a chainsaw, the madness began.

01:50:19.040 --> 01:50:23.610
Denji transformed - Giant blades emerging
from his arms, and his head transforming into

01:50:23.610 --> 01:50:25.929
a toothy, saw-blade nightmare.

01:50:25.929 --> 01:50:28.770
He gave a mechanical roar that spewed smoke.

01:50:28.770 --> 01:50:31.110
This wasn’t just Denji anymore.

01:50:31.110 --> 01:50:33.580
This was Chainsaw Man.

01:50:33.580 --> 01:50:40.360
Now this, Able thought, feeling his adrenaline
spike, is more like it!

01:50:40.360 --> 01:50:43.650
Following Denji’s lead, Able reached into
one of his pocket dimensions and pulled out

01:50:43.650 --> 01:50:48.150
one of his favorite weapons - one he’d only
previously used against the mighty Hard to

01:50:48.150 --> 01:50:55.550
Destroy Reptile, SCP-682: The Chainsaw Claymore,
a huge, two-handed sword with the eternally

01:50:55.550 --> 01:50:59.820
twisting, shredding teeth of a chainsaw ever
circulating around it.

01:50:59.820 --> 01:51:02.190
It was time for Chainsaw Vs Chainsaw.

01:51:02.190 --> 01:51:04.849
“What the hell are you waiting for?”

01:51:04.849 --> 01:51:05.870
Chainsaw Man roared.

01:51:05.870 --> 01:51:09.179
“Are we gonna stand around all day, or are
we gonna fight?”

01:51:09.179 --> 01:51:11.810
Able couldn’t have said it better himself.

01:51:11.810 --> 01:51:16.889
The two charged at one another at lightning
speeds, chainsaw clashing against chainsword.

01:51:16.889 --> 01:51:20.969
The sheer force of contact was enough to send
a shockwave blasting through the bar.

01:51:20.969 --> 01:51:25.489
It rapidly became a power struggle, each one
of them trying hard to force their chainsaws

01:51:25.489 --> 01:51:27.260
out of the stalemate.

01:51:27.260 --> 01:51:31.869
Realizing that this time he perhaps couldn’t
win with raw strength, Able backflipped away

01:51:31.869 --> 01:51:33.849
to reassess his options.

01:51:33.849 --> 01:51:38.040
But Chainsaw Man had no intention of giving
Able time to think about it.

01:51:38.040 --> 01:51:41.800
He darted towards Able with the weight and
momentum of a runaway freight train.

01:51:41.800 --> 01:51:46.260
If Able hadn’t raised his claymore to parry,
he would have been shredded to pieces by the

01:51:46.260 --> 01:51:47.980
devil’s saws in an instant.

01:51:47.980 --> 01:51:53.060
Instead, the two of them rocketed out of the
nearby wall in a cascade of debris, causing

01:51:53.060 --> 01:51:56.050
everyone on the outside street to run for
their lives.

01:51:56.050 --> 01:52:01.340
The two quickly stood from the stumble, catching
their breath.

01:52:01.340 --> 01:52:02.650
“Impressive,” Able said.

01:52:02.650 --> 01:52:05.170
“You’re much better than the others.”

01:52:05.170 --> 01:52:09.820
Instead of replying, Denji briefly retracted
his arm chainsaws and grabbed a nearby parked

01:52:09.820 --> 01:52:12.619
car, throwing it directly at Able.

01:52:12.619 --> 01:52:16.820
Able reacted quickly, cleaving the car in
half with his claymore and charging for Chainsaw

01:52:16.820 --> 01:52:18.179
Man again.

01:52:18.179 --> 01:52:23.099
Just before Able could land a lethal strike,
Chainsaw Man deployed his chainsaws again,

01:52:23.099 --> 01:52:24.610
blocking the blow.

01:52:24.610 --> 01:52:28.730
Able sped around him, trying to strike again
and again, but Chainsaw Man blocked every

01:52:28.730 --> 01:52:30.679
strike with stunning efficacy.

01:52:30.679 --> 01:52:35.489
Able was astonished - few had ever been able
to go toe to toe with him like this before.

01:52:35.489 --> 01:52:38.500
He could feel his heart pounding gloriously
in his chest.

01:52:38.500 --> 01:52:40.810
He would give Denji a warrior’s death.

01:52:40.810 --> 01:52:45.640
With a furious yell, Able brought down the
Chainsaw Claymore for a devastating vertical

01:52:45.640 --> 01:52:47.510
strike, but Chainsaw Man was ready.

01:52:47.510 --> 01:52:52.989
He arranged his arm chainsaws in a cross formation,
like a giant pair of scissors, and caught

01:52:52.989 --> 01:52:55.060
Able’s chainsword between them.

01:52:55.060 --> 01:53:00.429
Chainsaw Man pulled his arms in opposite directions,
slicing Able’s mighty sword in half.

01:53:00.429 --> 01:53:05.230
The immortal Swordsman skidded backwards to
avoid the fallout, producing two smaller blades

01:53:05.230 --> 01:53:06.300
immediately.

01:53:06.300 --> 01:53:10.780
This Chainsaw Man just kept exceeding expectations,
didn’t he?

01:53:10.780 --> 01:53:14.380
Able would need to change tactics if he wanted
to win this one...

01:53:14.380 --> 01:53:17.610
Chainsaw Man was impressed by the speed and
tenacity of his foe.

01:53:17.610 --> 01:53:22.230
For someone who apparently wasn’t even a
devil, Able sure packed a hell of a punch.

01:53:22.230 --> 01:53:24.750
Did he ever run out of those damn weapons?

01:53:24.750 --> 01:53:29.170
As though attempting to answer Chainsaw Man’s
question for him, Able began running around

01:53:29.170 --> 01:53:34.210
his flank, rapidly producing and throwing
blades and axes in a startling volley.

01:53:34.210 --> 01:53:38.840
Chainsaw Man was able to use his Chainsaw
arms and face to block most of them, but not

01:53:38.840 --> 01:53:39.960
all of them.

01:53:39.960 --> 01:53:44.630
Several daggers and small throwing axes splattered
into the tender flesh of Chainsaw Man’s

01:53:44.630 --> 01:53:45.630
chest.

01:53:45.630 --> 01:53:49.080
Able had successfully wounded him, and he
wasn’t done.

01:53:49.080 --> 01:53:53.610
Feeling a little more confident now, Able
decided to take a different tactic: He produced

01:53:53.610 --> 01:53:58.159
a large, spiked mace from thin air, and ran
at Chainsaw Man while the devil was still

01:53:58.159 --> 01:54:00.679
recovering from his projectile attack.

01:54:00.679 --> 01:54:06.730
With one brutal whack, he sent Denji flying
down the street, carving a rut into the concrete

01:54:06.730 --> 01:54:07.860
beneath him.

01:54:07.860 --> 01:54:09.020
But Able wasn’t done.

01:54:09.020 --> 01:54:13.670
While Chainsaw Man was still trying to recover,
Able leaped onto him and began beating him

01:54:13.670 --> 01:54:15.880
into the ground with his mace.

01:54:15.880 --> 01:54:20.400
The strikes were so brutal they shook the
earth and sent cracks across the surrounding

01:54:20.400 --> 01:54:21.400
ground.

01:54:21.400 --> 01:54:23.030
Then Able stopped.

01:54:23.030 --> 01:54:27.440
He realized, for a moment, that he was letting
his blood lust get the better of him.

01:54:27.440 --> 01:54:29.470
This was dishonorable.

01:54:29.470 --> 01:54:33.040
Where would be the fun in beating this boy
to death while he lay on the ground, and depriving

01:54:33.040 --> 01:54:36.710
himself of one of the greatest opponents he’s
had in quite some time?

01:54:36.710 --> 01:54:38.980
No, that wouldn’t do at all.

01:54:38.980 --> 01:54:41.139
He’d give him one more chance.

01:54:41.139 --> 01:54:43.940
“On your feet, boy,” Able said.

01:54:43.940 --> 01:54:45.190
“You fight well.

01:54:45.190 --> 01:54:46.190
Get up and carry on.

01:54:46.190 --> 01:54:49.910
I won’t let a beast as rare as you die like
a common dog.

01:54:49.910 --> 01:54:51.340
Rise and fight me!”

01:54:51.340 --> 01:54:54.190
And Chainsaw Man did as he was told.

01:54:54.190 --> 01:54:58.540
Able was shocked to see the very ground shatter
underneath him as Chainsaw Man burst up through

01:54:58.540 --> 01:55:00.440
it, all his swords at the ready.

01:55:00.440 --> 01:55:05.099
The mace was thrown from Able’s hands as
Chainsaw Man launched up towards him, all

01:55:05.099 --> 01:55:06.720
metal teeth and fury.

01:55:06.720 --> 01:55:11.639
Luckily for Able, he pulled out a battle axe
just in time to block the flurry of brutal

01:55:11.639 --> 01:55:14.329
strikes from the patron saint of chainsaws.

01:55:14.329 --> 01:55:18.940
Now this was a fight even Musashi would be
proud of.

01:55:18.940 --> 01:55:20.480
“Yes, boy, yes!”

01:55:20.480 --> 01:55:21.480
Able yelled.

01:55:21.480 --> 01:55:23.820
“This is true combat!”

01:55:23.820 --> 01:55:28.409
Chainsaw Man replied with the swing of his
blades, which Able was narrowly able to dodge.

01:55:28.409 --> 01:55:32.710
The two finally landed back down on the ground,
and Able was fast enough to bury his battle

01:55:32.710 --> 01:55:35.090
axe in Chainsaw Man’s shoulder.

01:55:35.090 --> 01:55:38.869
Before the devil could return a blow to Able,
the anomalous Swordsman pulled out a pair

01:55:38.869 --> 01:55:43.550
of his favorite swords and locked Chainsaw
Man’s arms in place.

01:55:43.550 --> 01:55:49.060
Chainsaw Man was undeniably incredibly powerful,
but it looked like Able’s superior experience

01:55:49.060 --> 01:55:51.909
and tactics might save him this time.

01:55:51.909 --> 01:55:54.400
“What the hell are you?”

01:55:54.400 --> 01:55:55.400
Chainsaw Man roared.

01:55:55.400 --> 01:56:00.260
“You’ve been a worthy opponent, boy, those
are few and far between,” Able said.

01:56:00.260 --> 01:56:02.090
“I’ll remember you for this...”

01:56:02.090 --> 01:56:07.090
But before Able could execute a killing blow,
he felt a blood red throwing axe stick into

01:56:07.090 --> 01:56:08.099
his back.

01:56:08.099 --> 01:56:12.530
Able winced in pain and turned to see Power
and Aki about thirty feet behind him.

01:56:12.530 --> 01:56:17.389
Power was propping Aki up - he’d donated
some of his blood to bring her back to life.

01:56:17.389 --> 01:56:20.119
And she was just as delusionally cocky as
ever.

01:56:20.119 --> 01:56:21.119
“Tis I once again, my arch-nemesis!”

01:56:21.119 --> 01:56:22.119
Power yelled.

01:56:22.119 --> 01:56:23.119
“Did you really believe you could beat me
so easily?”

01:56:23.119 --> 01:56:24.929
Able was about to say something, but he’d
already made a fatal mistake: Letting his

01:56:24.929 --> 01:56:25.960
guard down.

01:56:25.960 --> 01:56:29.710
Before another word could pass the cursed
warrior’s lips, one of Chainsaw Man’s

01:56:29.710 --> 01:56:34.320
arm chainsaws passed directly through his
heart, tearing it apart within Able’s chest.

01:56:34.320 --> 01:56:37.580
It was a sudden and decisive killing blow.

01:56:37.580 --> 01:56:42.070
Chainsaw Man pulled his saw back out of Able’s
chest, stained with the deadly anomaly’s

01:56:42.070 --> 01:56:43.070
blood.

01:56:43.070 --> 01:56:46.840
Able collapsed to the ground, wheezing and
bleeding profusely from the hole in his chest.

01:56:46.840 --> 01:56:52.850
But strangely, as Power, Aki, and Chainsaw
Man converged around him, they realized he

01:56:52.850 --> 01:56:53.949
was smiling.

01:56:53.949 --> 01:56:55.329
“Thank you...”

01:56:55.329 --> 01:56:57.940
Able said, and died yet again.

01:56:57.940 --> 01:57:02.960
With the battle won, like an extremely metal
Incredible Hulk, Chainsaw Man transformed

01:57:02.960 --> 01:57:04.460
back into Denji.

01:57:04.460 --> 01:57:08.610
The trio stood around Able’s corpse, deeply
confused as to what had just happened.

01:57:08.610 --> 01:57:13.380
If this was the kind of thing the SCP Foundation
normally dealt with, they all silently agreed

01:57:13.380 --> 01:57:17.750
that perhaps it would be better not to get
involved with them in future.

01:57:17.750 --> 01:57:24.139
Except Power, of course, who said, “You
two should be thanking me for defeating him.

01:57:24.139 --> 01:57:26.360
You both owe me drinks for this!”

01:57:26.360 --> 01:57:30.829
Hundreds of miles away, in a black sarcophagus
deep underwater, surrounded by professional

01:57:30.829 --> 01:57:34.680
SCP Foundation divers, Able’s body once
again returned.

01:57:34.680 --> 01:57:37.670
Who knows how long he’d remain sleeping
in there?

01:57:37.670 --> 01:57:43.181
But what we do know is that his deathless
sleep was suffused with sweet dreams, knowing

01:57:43.181 --> 01:57:46.330
that this world still held worthy opponents.

01:57:46.330 --> 01:57:48.849
And for Able, that was everything.

01:57:48.849 --> 01:57:55.301
We’d been so cautious, keeping quiet, covering
up, only moving at night, but sometimes, despite

01:57:55.301 --> 01:57:58.219
all your best efforts, you just get unlucky.

01:57:58.219 --> 01:58:03.110
We made our way through what we thought was
an abandoned street, littered with broken-down

01:58:03.110 --> 01:58:04.290
cars, when those...

01:58:04.290 --> 01:58:07.030
Things had slithered out and ambushed us.

01:58:07.030 --> 01:58:10.929
Kaspar, who was always the most trigger happy
of us, panicked and opened fire with his scavenged

01:58:10.929 --> 01:58:13.570
submachine gun on the largest of the creatures.

01:58:13.570 --> 01:58:14.570
Big mistake.

01:58:14.570 --> 01:58:18.610
It didn’t slow the monster down, and only
seemed to attract more.

01:58:18.610 --> 01:58:21.270
It’d be blob city before sunrise now.

01:58:21.270 --> 01:58:24.370
But poor Kaspar wouldn’t make it that long.

01:58:24.370 --> 01:58:28.949
Fleshy tendrils wrapped around his limbs and
pulled him into the terrible mass of one of

01:58:28.949 --> 01:58:29.949
the creatures.

01:58:29.949 --> 01:58:35.690
It started reshaping around him, enveloping
him as he screamed, until the tide of flesh

01:58:35.690 --> 01:58:38.380
coursing down his throat silenced him.

01:58:38.380 --> 01:58:43.370
The whole time, the monster just kept gibbering
madness in a warped voice.

01:58:43.370 --> 01:58:50.210
“Become one, yes, let our cells bond and
our minds coagulate in the glorious shimmering

01:58:50.210 --> 01:58:51.210
light.

01:58:51.210 --> 01:59:02.110
We will all be one in daylight, pretty flower,
yes, yes, yes...”

01:59:02.110 --> 01:59:04.230
And then there were four.

01:59:04.230 --> 01:59:06.310
Me, Ellen, Darcy, and Jones.

01:59:06.310 --> 01:59:10.980
There had been more of us once, but in this
war of attrition, we always seemed to be the

01:59:10.980 --> 01:59:12.820
ones who had to lose.

01:59:12.820 --> 01:59:16.310
And if we didn’t get away from these monsters
quickly, then there wouldn’t be any of us

01:59:16.310 --> 01:59:17.760
left soon enough.

01:59:17.760 --> 01:59:21.889
We ran, ducking and weaving around the cars
as the blobs got closer.

01:59:21.889 --> 01:59:27.110
There were so many of them, all howling and
ranting, zealots for the only cause their

01:59:27.110 --> 01:59:30.700
melted excuses for minds could understand
anymore.

01:59:30.700 --> 01:59:32.780
Occasionally, we fired back, hoping to slow
them down a little - But it never worked.

01:59:32.780 --> 01:59:39.020
The guns, if anything, were a psychological
support mechanism, and something to scare

01:59:39.020 --> 01:59:42.320
off other survivors who were even more desperate
than us.

01:59:42.320 --> 01:59:46.690
When it came to the blobs, especially the
big ones, the only things you could do were

01:59:46.690 --> 01:59:48.190
run and hope.

01:59:48.190 --> 01:59:50.300
And hope’s in short supply these days.

01:59:50.300 --> 01:59:55.320
No matter how fast we ran, the blobs kept
catching up, and they didn’t seem to get

01:59:55.320 --> 01:59:56.320
tired.

01:59:56.320 --> 01:59:59.780
Knowing we couldn’t outrun them, we ran
up to one of the abandoned cars and crouched

01:59:59.780 --> 02:00:01.730
behind them, breathing raggedly.

02:00:01.730 --> 02:00:07.070
This whole stupid mission, in hopes of eventually
reaching safety, a good night’s sleep behind

02:00:07.070 --> 02:00:10.640
solid walls, and some people who actually
know what the Hell is going on.

02:00:10.640 --> 02:00:13.050
I drew my sidearm out of my pocket.

02:00:13.050 --> 02:00:16.380
Even if I didn’t make it out of here, I
wouldn’t turn into one of those monsters.

02:00:16.380 --> 02:00:19.280
Pulling back the hammer, I muttered a quiet
prayer.

02:00:19.280 --> 02:00:23.440
If there’s a God out there, he had a hell
of a lot to answer for right now.

02:00:23.440 --> 02:00:28.290
I looked to Ellen, Darcy, and Jones, and they
all had the same idea.

02:00:28.290 --> 02:00:31.270
It was a pleasure to know them all, after
everything that’d happened.

02:00:31.270 --> 02:00:36.449
We heard the blobs getting closer, their lunatic
whispers growing in volume and intensity,

02:00:36.449 --> 02:00:39.370
as they always did before they claimed one
of us.

02:00:39.370 --> 02:00:44.199
I breathed a sigh, ready to accept my fate,
knowing what I needed to do.

02:00:44.199 --> 02:00:45.920
It all seemed to be over.

02:00:45.920 --> 02:00:47.300
Until He appeared.

02:00:47.300 --> 02:00:50.380
I looked up and spotted a strange man approaching.

02:00:50.380 --> 02:00:55.860
He was dressed in an old-fashioned hessian
toga, His hair and beard frosty white.

02:00:55.860 --> 02:01:00.470
I couldn’t identify His age or race, but
those factors seemed secondary to the fact

02:01:00.470 --> 02:01:04.880
His eyes were glowing brilliant white, as
if exuding pure energy.

02:01:04.880 --> 02:01:09.969
He raised a hand, the same glowing aura of
pure white energy emanating off of it.

02:01:09.969 --> 02:01:14.020
I’d seen so many things that terrified me
in the past six months.

02:01:14.020 --> 02:01:15.020
But this...

02:01:15.020 --> 02:01:18.860
This was the first time I’d experienced
something I could call “Awe.”

02:01:18.860 --> 02:01:24.060
He walked towards us with a stillness and
confidence and said “You look like you could

02:01:24.060 --> 02:01:25.380
use a hand.”

02:01:25.380 --> 02:01:27.080
Where were you when day broke?

02:01:27.080 --> 02:01:28.849
Whoever’s left, they remember.

02:01:28.849 --> 02:01:33.210
I was in a supermarket with my wife and two
kids, just another normal day.

02:01:33.210 --> 02:01:37.929
I was worrying about bills, taxes, and whatever
we were going to have for dinner that night.

02:01:37.929 --> 02:01:43.460
If the Devil exists, I’d sell my soul to
the nasty red creep to get those worries back.

02:01:43.460 --> 02:01:47.570
Lucky for us, we were in the back half of
the store, lit entirely by artificial light.

02:01:47.570 --> 02:01:51.060
The people checking out their groceries down
front, right in front of the building’s

02:01:51.060 --> 02:01:54.110
huge, glass facade, they were the first to
go down.

02:01:54.110 --> 02:01:55.989
All these terrible drowned screams.

02:01:55.989 --> 02:01:59.950
First, the exact kind of shrieks you’d expect
from somebody starting to melt.

02:01:59.950 --> 02:02:05.820
Then, the gurgling, like a backed-up drain,
as their mouth and throat melted around the

02:02:05.820 --> 02:02:07.409
sound, choking it.

02:02:07.409 --> 02:02:10.179
Those were the first minutes of Hell on Earth.

02:02:10.179 --> 02:02:12.099
I’ve never been the smartest man.

02:02:12.099 --> 02:02:15.050
I was a roofer, back when things made sense.

02:02:15.050 --> 02:02:19.300
Never went to college, never been much for
reading, but I had intuition, and I credit

02:02:19.300 --> 02:02:20.800
that with surviving this long.

02:02:20.800 --> 02:02:22.699
My dad was in the service.

02:02:22.699 --> 02:02:24.130
Two tours in ‘Nam.

02:02:24.130 --> 02:02:28.010
He always told me when I was a kid, the guys
who didn’t make it back, they panicked.

02:02:28.010 --> 02:02:30.400
Because that’s what the enemy wants you
to do.

02:02:30.400 --> 02:02:35.020
They hope, when everything hits the fan, you’ll
break formation, forget the plan, and all

02:02:35.020 --> 02:02:38.750
start scurrying in different directions like
rats, just hoping you’ll be the one who

02:02:38.750 --> 02:02:40.500
finds a crack and gets out.

02:02:40.500 --> 02:02:42.150
That’s when they get you.

02:02:42.150 --> 02:02:48.060
When you panic, you’re giving up the birth
rite of reason and letting the animal take

02:02:48.060 --> 02:02:49.060
over.

02:02:49.060 --> 02:02:50.060
“And animals, son, are easier to kill.”

02:02:50.060 --> 02:02:55.250
When the sun went bad that day, plenty of
people in that store started running.

02:02:55.250 --> 02:02:57.200
They didn’t know what they were running
from, or where they were running to.

02:02:57.200 --> 02:03:01.190
They just wanted to put some distance between
themselves and the screaming.

02:03:01.190 --> 02:03:02.380
Every man for himself.

02:03:02.380 --> 02:03:07.239
I’d love to tell you all those people are
dead now, but in actuality, they were in for

02:03:07.239 --> 02:03:09.000
a far worse fate.

02:03:09.000 --> 02:03:12.900
They ran out of the safety and cover of the
store, putting themselves at the mercy of

02:03:12.900 --> 02:03:14.060
the light.

02:03:14.060 --> 02:03:16.590
Even as they melted, they kept running.

02:03:16.590 --> 02:03:20.960
They were blobs, slithering away, not even
knowing that the thing they were running from

02:03:20.960 --> 02:03:22.450
had already gotten them.

02:03:22.450 --> 02:03:26.830
It all happened so fast, but I can remember
every single detail.

02:03:26.830 --> 02:03:28.140
You can judge me if you like.

02:03:28.140 --> 02:03:29.140
I don’t care anymore.

02:03:29.140 --> 02:03:33.070
If I could have spoken reason to those terrified
people that day, hand on my heart, I would

02:03:33.070 --> 02:03:34.070
have.

02:03:34.070 --> 02:03:38.860
But one of man’s greatest design flaws is
that God made fear the master of reason.

02:03:38.860 --> 02:03:41.650
Nothing I could’ve said that day would’ve
changed anything.

02:03:41.650 --> 02:03:45.639
The only ones I could hope to save were my
family, so that’s exactly what I did.

02:03:45.639 --> 02:03:50.130
We grabbed what we could, stayed away from
windows, and made our way to the nearest supply

02:03:50.130 --> 02:03:51.130
closet.

02:03:51.130 --> 02:03:54.700
We were in there for hours, and we didn’t
come out until things were actually quiet.

02:03:54.700 --> 02:03:57.099
Which, coincidentally, happened to be at night.

02:03:57.099 --> 02:04:01.320
When we stepped outside of the store, we saw
the carnage that must’ve unfolded over the

02:04:01.320 --> 02:04:02.790
past few hours.

02:04:02.790 --> 02:04:04.010
Windows smashed.

02:04:04.010 --> 02:04:06.880
Cars driven into storefronts and abandoned.

02:04:06.880 --> 02:04:09.239
Slithering blobs of former-people on the ground.

02:04:09.239 --> 02:04:14.420
In the space of a few hours, the world had
truly and irrevocably changed.

02:04:14.420 --> 02:04:19.290
No matter what happened, even if we survived,
we knew there would never be a “normal”

02:04:19.290 --> 02:04:21.389
as we’d known it before ever again.

02:04:21.389 --> 02:04:25.059
The same message was playing on every TV,
radio, and computer.

02:04:25.059 --> 02:04:30.469
A logo I didn’t quite recognize, along with
an overlay that read, “An Important Message

02:04:30.469 --> 02:04:32.460
from the SCP Foundation.”

02:04:32.460 --> 02:04:38.170
It explained, in an eternally looping, robotic
voice, that they were superseding the control

02:04:38.170 --> 02:04:42.559
of all world governments to protect humanity
from this new and terrifying threat.

02:04:42.559 --> 02:04:45.309
In short, the sun had turned against us.

02:04:45.309 --> 02:04:48.130
In some scenarios, survival is a curse.

02:04:48.130 --> 02:04:52.531
In those early days and weeks, you wouldn’t
believe the number of times I started to envy

02:04:52.531 --> 02:04:53.531
the dead.

02:04:53.531 --> 02:04:57.329
People who’d been wiped off the mortal coil
by diseases and car crashes and random acts

02:04:57.329 --> 02:05:02.420
of violence in the days before Day Broke,
they had no idea how good they had it.

02:05:02.420 --> 02:05:07.030
Little by little, in this terrible new world,
death became a kind of luxury.

02:05:07.030 --> 02:05:10.290
Because melting under the fiery gaze of the
sun?

02:05:10.290 --> 02:05:11.460
That wasn’t death.

02:05:11.460 --> 02:05:12.469
Not even close.

02:05:12.469 --> 02:05:14.159
They seemed harmless at first.

02:05:14.159 --> 02:05:15.730
Tragic, pitiful, really.

02:05:15.730 --> 02:05:20.400
The voices on the TV even told us that, to
avoid starvation, we could eat small parts

02:05:20.400 --> 02:05:21.400
of the melted.

02:05:21.400 --> 02:05:23.429
But, over time, the situation evolved.

02:05:23.429 --> 02:05:27.940
I don’t know when it started, or why, but
the blobs that had once been people started

02:05:27.940 --> 02:05:28.940
coagulating.

02:05:28.940 --> 02:05:35.080
They joined up, started turning into bigger
creatures, all with one mind, always screaming

02:05:35.080 --> 02:05:38.900
and talking madness in a collage of stolen
voices.

02:05:38.900 --> 02:05:44.960
These monsters existed for one purpose, and
one purpose only: Finding the people who were

02:05:44.960 --> 02:05:48.199
still normal and dragging them out into the
light to join them.

02:05:48.199 --> 02:05:51.920
They roamed the world during the night, hunting,
seeking.

02:05:51.920 --> 02:05:56.630
And given night was the only time we could
ever safely move, this created problems for

02:05:56.630 --> 02:05:57.630
all of us.

02:05:57.630 --> 02:06:00.520
We lost so many to those terrible monsters.

02:06:00.520 --> 02:06:01.909
Including my wife and both my kids.

02:06:01.909 --> 02:06:05.639
See what I mean about survival sometimes being
a curse?

02:06:05.639 --> 02:06:06.820
Especially when you’ve got people to miss.

02:06:06.820 --> 02:06:11.730
I wish they were dead, all three of them,
but I still hear them - their voices added

02:06:11.730 --> 02:06:14.210
to the chorus of a house-sized flesh monster.

02:06:14.210 --> 02:06:17.350
But I lived on, if you can call this living.

02:06:17.350 --> 02:06:21.480
I met with others, like Kaspar, Ellen, Darcy,
and Jones.

02:06:21.480 --> 02:06:23.179
All of them had lost people.

02:06:23.179 --> 02:06:25.849
You hadn’t lived this long if you hadn’t
lost people.

02:06:25.849 --> 02:06:28.900
We did all we could to keep surviving against
the odds.

02:06:28.900 --> 02:06:34.079
We spent our days in basements and abandoned
stores, and our nights dodging the flesh creatures

02:06:34.079 --> 02:06:35.690
and foraging for food.

02:06:35.690 --> 02:06:39.150
We eked out each day, taking every breath
as it came.

02:06:39.150 --> 02:06:41.070
We didn’t hope for anything.

02:06:41.070 --> 02:06:44.920
Until one day, we heard that the people at
the SCP Foundation might know how to reverse

02:06:44.920 --> 02:06:45.920
all this.

02:06:45.920 --> 02:06:49.579
They needed all the people and help they could
get at one of their bases, around twenty miles

02:06:49.579 --> 02:06:50.579
away from us.

02:06:50.579 --> 02:06:54.230
It’d only be a couple nights walk to get
there, we figured, so why not help out the

02:06:54.230 --> 02:06:55.230
cause?

02:06:55.230 --> 02:06:59.530
Safety in numbers, after all - And, truth
be told, we’d missed people.

02:06:59.530 --> 02:07:04.159
After days of hiding and nights of traveling,
we were ambushed, but you already know about

02:07:04.159 --> 02:07:05.159
that part.

02:07:05.159 --> 02:07:09.170
We lost Kaspar to one of those monsters and
got cornered behind an abandoned car.

02:07:09.170 --> 02:07:13.639
However, as the blobs got closer and closer,
that mysterious stranger with the glowing

02:07:13.639 --> 02:07:14.670
eyes appeared.

02:07:14.670 --> 02:07:16.960
He didn’t walk like the rest of us.

02:07:16.960 --> 02:07:21.040
He was bold, confident, His back straight
as a dancer’s.

02:07:21.040 --> 02:07:22.570
Like He feared nothing.

02:07:22.570 --> 02:07:24.180
Like nothing here could hurt Him.

02:07:24.180 --> 02:07:26.449
Suddenly, I felt a rumbling behind me.

02:07:26.449 --> 02:07:28.250
The car was rattling.

02:07:28.250 --> 02:07:32.450
I feared for a second that the blobs were
crawling over it to get us, but when I turned,

02:07:32.450 --> 02:07:34.160
I saw the opposite was happening.

02:07:34.160 --> 02:07:36.969
The car was rising off of the ground, free-floating.

02:07:36.969 --> 02:07:42.580
Myself and the other survivors stared in astonishment
as the stranger simply flicked His wrist.

02:07:42.580 --> 02:07:47.830
The floating car was thrown with tremendous
force at the largest of the advancing blobs.

02:07:47.830 --> 02:07:52.179
It hit the beast so hard that the top of it
simply splattered off, freezing what was left

02:07:52.179 --> 02:07:53.360
in place.

02:07:53.360 --> 02:07:56.210
Even the other blobs paused, seemingly astonished.

02:07:56.210 --> 02:07:59.290
We all turned to the stranger, still standing
firm.

02:07:59.290 --> 02:08:03.469
“Stand behind me if you wish to live,”
He said.

02:08:03.469 --> 02:08:07.070
There was something both passionate and commanding
about His voice.

02:08:07.070 --> 02:08:10.790
It was impossible to hear Him and not heed
His words.

02:08:10.790 --> 02:08:14.889
All of us stood up and ran behind the stranger,
as He lifted both hands.

02:08:14.889 --> 02:08:16.920
Debris climbed into the air.

02:08:16.920 --> 02:08:19.270
Cars, rocks, broken glass.

02:08:19.270 --> 02:08:22.969
The blobs were beginning to coagulate again,
but this time, the stranger wasn’t going

02:08:22.969 --> 02:08:24.900
to let them get the upper hand again.

02:08:24.900 --> 02:08:29.330
With a slight nod, everything He’d raised
flew at the blobs with the force of a machine

02:08:29.330 --> 02:08:30.330
gun.

02:08:30.330 --> 02:08:31.940
They were decimated.

02:08:31.940 --> 02:08:33.510
The bigger ones, cut apart.

02:08:33.510 --> 02:08:36.270
The smaller one fleeing to avoid the onslaught.

02:08:36.270 --> 02:08:39.860
After months of running from these monsters,
I don’t think any sight could have been

02:08:39.860 --> 02:08:40.860
more satisfying.

02:08:40.860 --> 02:08:44.090
When the creatures were gone, the stranger
just gave a quiet sigh.

02:08:44.090 --> 02:08:46.710
He turned to us and asked if we were okay.

02:08:46.710 --> 02:08:49.540
The answer was, essentially, “About as much
as we can be.”

02:08:49.540 --> 02:08:55.650
He told us that we’d be safe as long as
we stuck with Him, and after that display,

02:08:55.650 --> 02:08:57.770
we had every reason to believe Him.

02:08:57.770 --> 02:09:00.530
We followed the stranger down the long, dark
road.

02:09:00.530 --> 02:09:04.349
He always walked in the middle, fearless,
making no attempt to hide.

02:09:04.349 --> 02:09:09.440
When we asked Him His name, He told us that
He goes by many names, but for the sake of

02:09:09.440 --> 02:09:11.250
simplicity, we could call Him Matthew.

02:09:11.250 --> 02:09:16.699
We thanked Matthew for saving us, and He gave
a sad sort of smile, and told us that He only

02:09:16.699 --> 02:09:18.360
wished He could have done more.

02:09:18.360 --> 02:09:23.790
There was something so strange about Matthew,
even beyond the fact He apparently had superpowers.

02:09:23.790 --> 02:09:28.330
I’d never met the man before and I’d be
willing to bet my right hand on that, and

02:09:28.330 --> 02:09:31.190
yet, it felt like I’d known Him my entire
life.

02:09:31.190 --> 02:09:35.120
He was so different, and yet, so incredibly
familiar.

02:09:35.120 --> 02:09:40.170
We told Him we were on our way to a nearby
SCP Foundation facility, where we were told

02:09:40.170 --> 02:09:41.630
we’d find safe haven.

02:09:41.630 --> 02:09:43.790
We asked him if he knew where to find it.

02:09:43.790 --> 02:09:49.260
Matthew told us that, in fact, He’d lived
in that very site for decades, a visitor,

02:09:49.260 --> 02:09:50.260
just dropping in.

02:09:50.260 --> 02:09:55.120
He’d had a very stressful job before, and
felt like taking a sabbatical while things

02:09:55.120 --> 02:09:57.000
ran themselves for once.

02:09:57.000 --> 02:10:02.170
“Evidently, my help was more necessary than
I imagined,” He said.

02:10:02.170 --> 02:10:06.630
Occasionally, as we walked, we’d see blobs
watching us from crevices and dark alleys

02:10:06.630 --> 02:10:08.281
on the side of the road.

02:10:08.281 --> 02:10:11.050
They seemed to watch, but, for some reason,
didn’t approach.

02:10:11.050 --> 02:10:13.700
It was the most remarkable thing.

02:10:13.700 --> 02:10:15.880
“Don’t worry,” He told us.

02:10:15.880 --> 02:10:18.070
“I’m putting up invisible shields.

02:10:18.070 --> 02:10:22.880
None of them can approach us as long as I
maintain my focus.”

02:10:22.880 --> 02:10:27.750
Of course, we’d all heard stories of remarkable
and terrifying things wandering the wasteland

02:10:27.750 --> 02:10:29.460
we used to call planet earth.

02:10:29.460 --> 02:10:33.560
You couldn’t run into other survivors and
groups without hearing whispers about the

02:10:33.560 --> 02:10:34.860
things lurking out there.

02:10:34.860 --> 02:10:40.270
Some had told of a giant, monstrous reptile
that had destroyed an entire survivor settlement

02:10:40.270 --> 02:10:42.330
in a mall out in Nevada.

02:10:42.330 --> 02:10:45.750
Others told that one of those SCP Sites was
haunted.

02:10:45.750 --> 02:10:49.940
People spoke about a ghostly man who looked
like a rotten corpse, who could walk through

02:10:49.940 --> 02:10:51.829
walls and drag people to Hell.

02:10:51.829 --> 02:10:56.290
But the things Matthew was capable of seemed
to be a whole other level.

02:10:56.290 --> 02:11:01.330
I asked Him what He was, and He told me, “Just
a humble craftsman, my son.

02:11:01.330 --> 02:11:08.140
I enjoy creating, though admittedly, my creations
seem to have gotten away from me these days.”

02:11:08.140 --> 02:11:11.190
His evasion was less funny than He seemed
to think it was.

02:11:11.190 --> 02:11:14.710
I pressed on, asking Him what exactly he’s
capable of.

02:11:14.710 --> 02:11:18.829
He shrugged, and answered that he could do
almost anything if he really put his mind

02:11:18.829 --> 02:11:19.829
to it.

02:11:19.829 --> 02:11:21.560
I asked, “So...

02:11:21.560 --> 02:11:22.790
Ultimate power?”

02:11:22.790 --> 02:11:25.250
This gave Him a chuckle.

02:11:25.250 --> 02:11:28.300
He shook His head, and said, “Let me tell
you a story.

02:11:28.300 --> 02:11:32.909
A man comes upon a maze cut into a corn field,
and decides he wants to try his luck.

02:11:32.909 --> 02:11:41.270
He spends hours getting to the center of the
maze, and there, he finds the Devil waiting

02:11:41.270 --> 02:11:42.270
for him.

02:11:42.270 --> 02:11:44.739
The Devil says, ‘Welcome to my domain.

02:11:44.739 --> 02:11:52.840
Your soul is now forfeit, unless you can complete
my challenge and win it back.’

02:11:52.840 --> 02:11:57.000
Of course, the man agreed.

02:11:57.000 --> 02:12:00.840
The Devil said, ‘I can see everything, do
everything, and be everything.

02:12:00.840 --> 02:12:04.710
I know every inch of the universe and can
produce anything from thin air.

02:12:04.710 --> 02:12:10.860
If you want to keep your soul, name one thing
I can’t do.”

02:12:10.860 --> 02:12:12.780
Curious, I asked, “What did the man say?”

02:12:12.780 --> 02:12:16.190
Matthew smiled and said, “Get lost.”

02:12:16.190 --> 02:12:21.580
And for the first time in those long, dark
months, I actually laughed, and it was at

02:12:21.580 --> 02:12:22.960
such a stupid, corny dad joke.

02:12:22.960 --> 02:12:25.670
It’s a strange world we live in.

02:12:25.670 --> 02:12:27.730
“Point is,” Matthew continued.

02:12:27.730 --> 02:12:29.210
“There is no ‘Ultimate Power.’

02:12:29.210 --> 02:12:35.520
Some things are denied even to God, especially
when he chooses to walk as a man on the Earth

02:12:35.520 --> 02:12:37.599
he created.”

02:12:37.599 --> 02:12:40.969
We kept walking for hours.

02:12:40.969 --> 02:12:45.290
Matthew assured us that we would get there
in time, as the rest of us got ever more anxious

02:12:45.290 --> 02:12:47.040
about the thought of the rising sun.

02:12:47.040 --> 02:12:51.780
He said he’d seen so many sunrises now that
he could time them to the second.

02:12:51.780 --> 02:12:55.260
In the meantime, we should enjoy getting to
stretch our legs a little.

02:12:55.260 --> 02:12:57.980
Even now, the city could be beautiful at night.

02:12:57.980 --> 02:13:01.710
When He led us all the way to what seemed
like an abandoned chemical plant, I could

02:13:01.710 --> 02:13:03.280
feel my heart sink.

02:13:03.280 --> 02:13:09.750
All this time, all this work, to find more
people, to find safety, only to see that this

02:13:09.750 --> 02:13:11.420
place was abandoned, too.

02:13:11.420 --> 02:13:14.900
Matthew smiled, and said, “That’s just
what they want you to think.”

02:13:14.900 --> 02:13:19.610
He snapped his fingers and the ground around
us began to rumble.

02:13:19.610 --> 02:13:23.790
The concrete shifted seamlessly and an entrance
opened up below.

02:13:23.790 --> 02:13:28.330
Heavy bulkheads shifted, revealing a sleek,
chrome hallway down into the ground.

02:13:28.330 --> 02:13:29.570
We were astonished.

02:13:29.570 --> 02:13:32.530
Matthew gestured down into the hall and we
descended.

02:13:32.530 --> 02:13:35.260
Matthew followed us, the entrance closing
behind him.

02:13:35.260 --> 02:13:41.500
“I’m just warning you,” He said, “This
may come as a bit of a shock.”

02:13:41.500 --> 02:13:45.949
We ventured deeper, passing through different
automated security checkpoints as cameras

02:13:45.949 --> 02:13:47.610
gazed down from above.

02:13:47.610 --> 02:13:51.330
Eventually, we found ourselves in what seemed
to be a central chamber.

02:13:51.330 --> 02:13:53.230
It was a hive of activity.

02:13:53.230 --> 02:13:55.199
People in normal civilians clothes.

02:13:55.199 --> 02:13:56.880
Guards in tactical gear.

02:13:56.880 --> 02:13:58.280
Scientists in lab coats.

02:13:58.280 --> 02:14:02.270
Tears filled my eyes, it was the most people
I’d seen in one place in months.

02:14:02.270 --> 02:14:05.369
A man in a lab coat wearing an extravagant
medallion approached.

02:14:05.369 --> 02:14:06.909
He was making notes on a clipboard.

02:14:06.909 --> 02:14:08.420
“Another batch of survivors.

02:14:08.420 --> 02:14:10.770
Good work, 343,” the man said.

02:14:10.770 --> 02:14:12.170
Matthew smiled and nodded.

02:14:12.170 --> 02:14:13.900
“No problem, Jack.

02:14:13.900 --> 02:14:16.199
Always happy to help.”

02:14:16.199 --> 02:14:19.290
The man with the medallion - Jack, presumably
- turned to me.

02:14:19.290 --> 02:14:22.380
“I imagine you’ve come a long way,”
he said.

02:14:22.380 --> 02:14:23.380
I nodded.

02:14:23.380 --> 02:14:25.980
“You have no idea.”

02:14:25.980 --> 02:14:27.250
Reality warpers.

02:14:27.250 --> 02:14:29.040
Real pieces of work, aren’t they?

02:14:29.040 --> 02:14:34.710
It’s one thing when an anomaly is all claws
and fangs, like SCP-682, or if their attack

02:14:34.710 --> 02:14:41.020
of choice is snapping necks like SCP-173,
but it’s an entirely different story if

02:14:41.020 --> 02:14:46.679
an anomaly can turn the air you breathe into
chocolate pudding or shove you into a pocket

02:14:46.679 --> 02:14:51.219
dimension that looks almost like our own reality,
except everyone is just a walking, talking

02:14:51.219 --> 02:14:52.420
pile of spiders.

02:14:52.420 --> 02:14:54.140
See what I mean?

02:14:54.140 --> 02:14:56.030
Reality warpers, real handfuls.

02:14:56.030 --> 02:15:00.420
Though, of course, not all reality warpers
are created equal.

02:15:00.420 --> 02:15:06.110
Some are relatively weak, only affecting the
world around them in a mild, ambient fashion.

02:15:06.110 --> 02:15:09.020
Others can rattle whole dimensions with their
tremendous power.

02:15:09.020 --> 02:15:11.960
The same also goes for morality.

02:15:11.960 --> 02:15:18.329
Some reality warpers are loving and benevolent,
such as SCP-343, the kindly, old all-powerful

02:15:18.329 --> 02:15:21.170
being known to some as God.

02:15:21.170 --> 02:15:25.560
And some are pure evil beings who want nothing
more than to use their immense power to sow

02:15:25.560 --> 02:15:28.580
chaos and misery among everyone else.

02:15:28.580 --> 02:15:33.860
And personally, we can’t think of a better
example of the latter than Bill Cipher from

02:15:33.860 --> 02:15:35.460
Gravity Falls.

02:15:35.460 --> 02:15:40.270
This Demonic Dorito wants nothing more than
to take over our dimension and rebuild it

02:15:40.270 --> 02:15:43.910
in his image of absolute insanity.

02:15:43.910 --> 02:15:50.330
So naturally, we started wondering: If these
two reality-warping titans, SCP-343 and Bill

02:15:50.330 --> 02:15:53.559
Cipher, ever came to blows, who would win?

02:15:53.559 --> 02:15:58.110
We were so curious, In fact, that we fired
up the Anom-O-Tron 6000, our state-of-the-art

02:15:58.110 --> 02:16:03.559
simulation supercomputer, to see how exactly
the two might meet and how their epic battle

02:16:03.559 --> 02:16:04.559
would play out.

02:16:04.559 --> 02:16:07.330
Who do you think would take the coveted W
on this one?

02:16:07.330 --> 02:16:12.750
Let us know down in the comments, along with
any other out of universe What If situations

02:16:12.750 --> 02:16:14.230
you’d love to see.

02:16:14.230 --> 02:16:17.020
But in the meantime, let’s fire up the machine.

02:16:17.020 --> 02:16:20.239
Be warned, folks: It’s gonna get weird.

02:16:20.239 --> 02:16:23.810
The date was July 12th, 2013.

02:16:23.810 --> 02:16:27.380
For SCP-343, it had started out as a relatively
normal day.

02:16:27.380 --> 02:16:31.580
He’d spent the night playing solitaire on
the astral plane, before warping back into

02:16:31.580 --> 02:16:36.319
his humanoid containment cell by morning,
leaving the Foundation none the wiser.

02:16:36.319 --> 02:16:39.149
After all, he was really here voluntarily.

02:16:39.149 --> 02:16:43.240
If the Foundation had truly wanted to try
to confine him here, they were welcome to

02:16:43.240 --> 02:16:47.940
give it a go, but it would be about as effective
as trying to catch a whisper in a butterfly

02:16:47.940 --> 02:16:48.940
net.

02:16:48.940 --> 02:16:53.350
While God had come to this place to experience
the joyful illusion of giving up control,

02:16:53.350 --> 02:16:56.469
it truly was little more than an illusion
to him.

02:16:56.469 --> 02:17:01.519
If he wanted to, he could exterminate the
SCP Foundation in less than an afternoon,

02:17:01.519 --> 02:17:04.019
then retire to Burger King for a Whopper.

02:17:04.019 --> 02:17:09.120
So really, they’re all just lucky he’s
a benevolent being, more interested in hanging

02:17:09.120 --> 02:17:13.340
out than dispensing wrath on those he perceived
as insolent.

02:17:13.340 --> 02:17:14.960
That was the Old Testament him.

02:17:14.960 --> 02:17:18.200
He’d done a lot of soul searching and growth
since then.

02:17:18.200 --> 02:17:22.679
It’d been at least a millennium since he’d
smote anyone, for that matter, and the last

02:17:22.679 --> 02:17:24.769
guy really had it coming.

02:17:24.769 --> 02:17:27.769
However, today was going to be a little different.

02:17:27.769 --> 02:17:30.780
God knew that something was going to happen
today.

02:17:30.780 --> 02:17:33.900
He sensed a great source of energy emerging.

02:17:33.900 --> 02:17:35.630
Something dark and malevolent.

02:17:35.630 --> 02:17:39.620
He sighed and closed his eyes for a moment,
focusing himself.

02:17:39.620 --> 02:17:44.110
He knew, whatever the nature of this threat,
it would fall upon him to face and destroy

02:17:44.110 --> 02:17:45.110
it.

02:17:45.110 --> 02:17:46.110
How irritating.

02:17:46.110 --> 02:17:49.200
He was hoping to finally binge Stranger Things
Season 4 today...

02:17:49.200 --> 02:17:52.689
Elsewhere in Site 19, things seemed to be
inordinately peaceful.

02:17:52.689 --> 02:17:57.429
There hadn’t been any containment breaches
or new anomalies brought in.

02:17:57.429 --> 02:18:00.559
There hadn’t been any attacks from rival
Groups of Interest.

02:18:00.559 --> 02:18:04.950
Dr. Bright hadn’t even done anything stupid
or started any fires.

02:18:04.950 --> 02:18:08.240
To borrow an old cliché, it was quiet.

02:18:08.240 --> 02:18:09.870
Too quiet.

02:18:09.870 --> 02:18:14.160
Perhaps the only person who wasn’t having
a relatively mellow day was Security Officer

02:18:14.160 --> 02:18:19.330
Frederick Simmons, a mid-level guard who’d
been stationed at Site 19 for four years now.

02:18:19.330 --> 02:18:22.540
He just wasn’t feeling himself today...

02:18:22.540 --> 02:18:25.950
The work didn’t bother Simmons - emotionally,
at least.

02:18:25.950 --> 02:18:30.189
Typically, even after seeing rather traumatic
things or being in near-death situations while

02:18:30.189 --> 02:18:34.050
in containment breaches, it hadn’t left
any lingering effects.

02:18:34.050 --> 02:18:37.910
But lately, he’d been having the strangest
dreams...

02:18:37.910 --> 02:18:39.950
It always played out the same way.

02:18:39.950 --> 02:18:44.769
Shortly after going to sleep, he’d open
his eyes in a strange, multi-colored void,

02:18:44.769 --> 02:18:49.190
surrounded by bizarre, seemingly random floating
objects, none of which seemed to have any

02:18:49.190 --> 02:18:52.189
real relevance to him or his life.

02:18:52.189 --> 02:18:56.780
And just when he’d begin to question it,
the other recurring element of the dream would

02:18:56.780 --> 02:18:57.780
occur.

02:18:57.780 --> 02:19:02.660
Out of the shimmering, oil-slick rainbow of
mind-boggling colors, a strange being would

02:19:02.660 --> 02:19:03.660
suddenly emerge.

02:19:03.660 --> 02:19:12.030
A glowing golden triangle, almost like a drawing
of a pyramid, with a stove pipe hat, a little

02:19:12.030 --> 02:19:18.769
bow tie, thin black arms and legs, and most
notable of all, a single large eye with a

02:19:18.769 --> 02:19:21.790
slit pupil staring out from the center.

02:19:21.790 --> 02:19:25.559
The eye almost seemed to have a strange, hypnotic
quality to it.

02:19:25.559 --> 02:19:28.250
Simmons felt bewitched whenever he looked
into it.

02:19:28.250 --> 02:19:29.269
He wasn’t afraid.

02:19:29.269 --> 02:19:31.090
Quite the opposite, actually.

02:19:31.090 --> 02:19:35.620
For reasons he couldn’t understand, this
strange creature from the world of dreams

02:19:35.620 --> 02:19:38.359
seemed like a good friend of his.

02:19:38.359 --> 02:19:47.139
He said, “Well, well, well, well, if it
isn’t my number one guy, the Fredmeister,

02:19:47.139 --> 02:19:48.139
in the house!

02:19:48.139 --> 02:19:49.139
I’ve missed you.

02:19:49.139 --> 02:19:50.139
Have you missed me?

02:19:50.139 --> 02:19:51.139
Put her there, good buddy!”

02:19:51.139 --> 02:19:52.139
The entity extended his hand, and Simmons
shook it.

02:19:52.139 --> 02:19:56.210
The Foundation guard could feel a strange
tingling sensation jolting down his arm.

02:19:56.210 --> 02:20:01.910
The first time Simmons had encountered the
entity, he’d told him his name: Bill Cipher,

02:20:01.910 --> 02:20:05.960
and he’d told him how incredibly important
it was that Simmons kept their little nighttime

02:20:05.960 --> 02:20:07.580
meetings a secret.

02:20:07.580 --> 02:20:10.610
In exchange, Bill was here to listen.

02:20:10.610 --> 02:20:15.010
Simmons would spend his time in the mindscape
pouring out his worries and frustrations with

02:20:15.010 --> 02:20:18.660
his daily work, as Bill paid impeccable attention.

02:20:18.660 --> 02:20:23.740
The strange little dream entity seemed fascinated
by the work Simmons did - All the peculiar

02:20:23.740 --> 02:20:26.770
and wondrous anomalies he guarded at Site
19.

02:20:26.770 --> 02:20:30.210
But to Simmons, it was all just boring work.

02:20:30.210 --> 02:20:34.399
Zombie-creating supernatural plague doctors
and immortal men with metal limbs lose their

02:20:34.399 --> 02:20:38.890
shine after you see them day in, day out,
for years on end.

02:20:38.890 --> 02:20:44.060
Frankly, Simmons needed a day off, but he’d
already used up all his PTO when he’d gotten

02:20:44.060 --> 02:20:46.010
the flu earlier that year.

02:20:46.010 --> 02:20:48.399
He just didn’t know what to do.

02:20:48.399 --> 02:20:50.780
Luckily for him, Bill had a solution.

02:20:50.780 --> 02:20:56.060
Bill, as it turned out, had a fancy little
ability: He could occupy the body of a human

02:20:56.060 --> 02:20:58.720
being, and operate it for them.

02:20:58.720 --> 02:21:02.620
Bill could take the wheel while Simmons took
a load off in the mindscape.

02:21:02.620 --> 02:21:06.990
How hard could standing around, pretending
to look busy at the SCP Foundation really

02:21:06.990 --> 02:21:07.990
be?

02:21:07.990 --> 02:21:12.090
As Bill explained the offer to him, Simmons
couldn’t see any flaws in his reasoning

02:21:12.090 --> 02:21:14.850
- After all, Bill was a friend.

02:21:14.850 --> 02:21:17.260
Why would he have any ill will towards him?

02:21:17.260 --> 02:21:22.149
With that, he shook hands with the bizarre
supernatural triangle, and felt the sudden,

02:21:22.149 --> 02:21:26.720
rough sensation of having his consciousness
ripped free from his body, only for Bill to

02:21:26.720 --> 02:21:29.010
slither in and take his place.

02:21:29.010 --> 02:21:35.290
This new Simmons - The Bill-occupied Simmons
- opened up his demonic, yellow eyes, and

02:21:35.290 --> 02:21:36.290
grinned.

02:21:36.290 --> 02:21:40.780
He gave a demented laugh to Simmons’ floated,
disembodied soul.

02:21:40.780 --> 02:21:47.600
“Oh man,” he said, wiping away a tear
of laughter with Simmons’ finger.

02:21:47.600 --> 02:21:48.600
“That was too easy!

02:21:48.600 --> 02:21:53.620
With your body, I can use the SCP Foundation’s
technology to take over the multiverse!

02:21:53.620 --> 02:21:54.859
See ya, sucker!”

02:21:54.859 --> 02:22:00.561
And with one last demented chuckle, Bill left
for work at the SCP Foundation, with Simmons

02:22:00.561 --> 02:22:04.270
being the latest in his long line of meat
puppets.

02:22:04.270 --> 02:22:09.000
After arriving at Site 19, he sneaked through
the facility, knowing exactly where he needed

02:22:09.000 --> 02:22:10.000
to be.

02:22:10.000 --> 02:22:15.560
You see, Bill is a native entity of the second
dimension - the world of flat shapes - but

02:22:15.560 --> 02:22:19.770
he’s able to access the minds of beings
in the third dimension, like us, through the

02:22:19.770 --> 02:22:23.520
medium of the mindscape, rather than the physical
realm.

02:22:23.520 --> 02:22:28.540
Bill’s life goal has always been to find
a way to permeate and take over the third

02:22:28.540 --> 02:22:31.979
dimension, turning it into his personal playground.

02:22:31.979 --> 02:22:36.560
All he needed was the right anomaly to bring
him forth into our world.

02:22:36.560 --> 02:22:43.440
In this case, a little anomalous device favored
by Dr. Kain Pathos Crow: SCP-158, also known

02:22:43.440 --> 02:22:45.050
as The Soul Extractor.

02:22:45.050 --> 02:22:50.310
While Dr. Crow left to the courtyard for his
evening walkies, the being that most people

02:22:50.310 --> 02:22:55.899
assumed was Fred Simmons secreted himself
into SCP-158’s containment chamber and locked

02:22:55.899 --> 02:22:57.520
the door behind him.

02:22:57.520 --> 02:23:02.640
He didn’t have much time; he’d need to
do this perfectly if he wanted a real chance

02:23:02.640 --> 02:23:04.750
at taking over the universe.

02:23:04.750 --> 02:23:07.350
He was amused by the irony, at least.

02:23:07.350 --> 02:23:11.360
The fact that, in order to take over, he’d
need to sneak into the midst of the people

02:23:11.360 --> 02:23:13.170
most likely to destroy him.

02:23:13.170 --> 02:23:16.500
Still, where’s the fun in a life with no
risk?

02:23:16.500 --> 02:23:22.319
At SCP-158’s control console, he inputted
the data to soul extraction and set a timer.

02:23:22.319 --> 02:23:26.729
However, there was one difference between
this and the usual procedures performed with

02:23:26.729 --> 02:23:31.360
the Soul Extractor: There was no containment
receptacle on the other end.

02:23:31.360 --> 02:23:35.020
Whatever was extracted would just be released
into the world.

02:23:35.020 --> 02:23:38.200
And this was exactly what Bill was counting
on.

02:23:38.200 --> 02:23:43.050
He laid Simmons’ body down on the gurney
and watched with glee as the robotic arm lowered

02:23:43.050 --> 02:23:44.050
towards him.

02:23:44.050 --> 02:23:50.330
It reached into his chest and pulled out the
essence of one three-sided threat to reality:

02:23:50.330 --> 02:23:52.010
Bill Cipher.

02:23:52.010 --> 02:23:55.819
One quick journey through the bowels of the
machine later, the nightmare scenario had

02:23:55.819 --> 02:24:01.340
come to pass - Bill floated around the room,
dragged into physical reality.

02:24:01.340 --> 02:24:06.490
He let out a long, conceited cackle and spun
his cane around.

02:24:06.490 --> 02:24:08.510
This was going to be fun!

02:24:08.510 --> 02:24:12.640
Elsewhere in the facility, alarms were going
off, and guards were deploying.

02:24:12.640 --> 02:24:17.290
Nobody was meant to be in containment chamber
158, so how was the soul extractor currently

02:24:17.290 --> 02:24:18.290
operating?

02:24:18.290 --> 02:24:20.439
This couldn’t possibly end well...

02:24:20.439 --> 02:24:23.660
Bill, on the other hand, was having a wonderful
time.

02:24:23.660 --> 02:24:27.700
He was pondering all the different ways he
could make the drab, clinical corridors of

02:24:27.700 --> 02:24:32.029
the SCP Foundation into his vision of perfect
weirdness.

02:24:32.029 --> 02:24:36.650
Maybe he’d turn all the researchers into
mice and turn Site 19 into a giant maze to

02:24:36.650 --> 02:24:38.130
run them through.

02:24:38.130 --> 02:24:43.479
Maybe he’d turn the air into farts and release
winged beasts from the hell dimension to ravage

02:24:43.479 --> 02:24:44.479
humanity.

02:24:44.479 --> 02:24:47.540
Maybe he’d go out to the parking lot and
key everyone’s cars.

02:24:47.540 --> 02:24:51.450
Oh, the diabolical possibilities were endless!

02:24:51.450 --> 02:24:56.470
As he floated out into the hall, his fantasizing
was interrupted by a group of Foundation Security

02:24:56.470 --> 02:24:58.880
Operatives wielding assault rifles.

02:24:58.880 --> 02:25:03.570
They entered an attack formation and trained
their rifles on him, before opening fire.

02:25:03.570 --> 02:25:07.200
Bill just found himself laughing again - The
gunfire just tickled!

02:25:07.200 --> 02:25:09.750
“Wow, you guys are hilarious!”

02:25:09.750 --> 02:25:11.710
Bill said between peals of laughter.

02:25:11.710 --> 02:25:16.771
“But wait, I can think of a way to make
you even funnier!”

02:25:16.771 --> 02:25:19.979
He snapped his fingers, and suddenly, the
guards were transformed.

02:25:19.979 --> 02:25:24.970
Instead of the serious first line of defense
for the SCP Foundation, they were now a gang

02:25:24.970 --> 02:25:29.810
of literal clowns straight from the circus,
holding balloon animals molded into the shapes

02:25:29.810 --> 02:25:30.810
of assault rifles.

02:25:30.810 --> 02:25:33.500
They giggled and threw pies at each other.

02:25:33.500 --> 02:25:36.870
Bill was right; this did make them even funnier.

02:25:36.870 --> 02:25:42.689
And he was just getting started, turning this
Foundation snoozefest into a party of cosmic

02:25:42.689 --> 02:25:43.689
proportions!

02:25:43.689 --> 02:25:47.740
Bill began running a rampage of weirdness
across the site.

02:25:47.740 --> 02:25:51.550
Essentially being the ultimate cosmic troll,
he decided he’d simply bother every single

02:25:51.550 --> 02:25:54.359
anomaly he could with his demonic antics.

02:25:54.359 --> 02:26:01.069
First, he appeared in SCP-096’s chamber
and pulled a brown paper bag over his head,

02:26:01.069 --> 02:26:04.479
with the words “UGLINESS LIES WITHIN”
written on the front.

02:26:04.479 --> 02:26:09.430
And just for fun, he then teleported the temperamental
beast to a nearby Amish community.

02:26:09.430 --> 02:26:14.260
It quickly became enraged when a gust of wind
blew the bag off its head, and a man named

02:26:14.260 --> 02:26:16.110
Jedediah saw its face.

02:26:16.110 --> 02:26:20.390
It then killed several others, also named
Jedediah, during the rampage.

02:26:20.390 --> 02:26:22.840
Bill thought it was hilarious.

02:26:22.840 --> 02:26:29.000
He then released SCP-682 into Site 19 and,
just to annoy the creature into further violence,

02:26:29.000 --> 02:26:33.010
he stuck an indestructible party hat on the
monster’s head.

02:26:33.010 --> 02:26:37.689
No matter how hard 682 tried, it couldn’t
remove the party hat.

02:26:37.689 --> 02:26:42.300
This caused it great frustration, which it
took out on any Foundation staff it happened

02:26:42.300 --> 02:26:43.960
to find in the area.

02:26:43.960 --> 02:26:48.979
It had fulfilled Bill’s expectations wonderfully,
but his quest for amusing carnage didn’t

02:26:48.979 --> 02:26:49.979
end there.

02:26:49.979 --> 02:26:55.540
Next, he went to bother SCP-049, the Plague
Doctor, who was in the process of doing surgery

02:26:55.540 --> 02:26:58.060
on a Foundation-provided dead goat.

02:26:58.060 --> 02:27:01.770
With a snap of his fingers, Bill transformed
the Plague Doctor’s surgical tools into

02:27:01.770 --> 02:27:04.280
colorful Play-Doh cutting tools.

02:27:04.280 --> 02:27:07.840
Needless to say, the supernatural surgeon
was less than pleased.

02:27:07.840 --> 02:27:12.740
He was about as annoyed as Dr. Clef was when
Bill turned his favorite shotgun into a bouquet

02:27:12.740 --> 02:27:18.490
of flowers, then sealed his feet into the
floor, or how vexed Dr. Gears was when Bill

02:27:18.490 --> 02:27:24.300
turned his plain beige necktie into a considerably
more loud and colorful tie.

02:27:24.300 --> 02:27:27.681
People there at the time reported hearing
Dr. Gears say, “I just don’t think that

02:27:27.681 --> 02:27:28.681
was necessary.”

02:27:28.681 --> 02:27:33.700
Oh, and he also did some more minor acts of
malice: He filled the break room with an army

02:27:33.700 --> 02:27:38.210
of flesh-eating zombies, he made a moat filled
with molten lava around the site that prevented

02:27:38.210 --> 02:27:43.490
anyone from escaping from his reign of terror,
and he even covered all the walls in cognitohazardous

02:27:43.490 --> 02:27:48.200
doodles that instantly drove any weak-minded
human who saw them into complete, gibbering

02:27:48.200 --> 02:27:49.200
madness.

02:27:49.200 --> 02:27:53.870
It was clear this reality-warping nightmare
needed to be stopped before he got bored of

02:27:53.870 --> 02:28:00.350
playing with his new Foundation toys and decided
to go remodel the universe in his own image.

02:28:00.350 --> 02:28:05.040
Thankfully, there was one anomaly on site
who was up to the task.

02:28:05.040 --> 02:28:09.790
Bill was treating himself to another evil
laugh in the Site 19 canteen when something

02:28:09.790 --> 02:28:11.100
peculiar happened.

02:28:11.100 --> 02:28:16.420
He looked down to see a man in what looked
like a tunic with greying hair and a beard.

02:28:16.420 --> 02:28:20.260
He walked with a peculiar kind of calmness,
his face blank.

02:28:20.260 --> 02:28:22.750
Why wasn’t this guy panicking?

02:28:22.750 --> 02:28:23.960
Was he stupid?

02:28:23.960 --> 02:28:27.210
Bill would seemingly need to teach this guy
a thing or two about fear...

02:28:27.210 --> 02:28:31.490
“Hey, gramps, don’t know if it’s escaped
your attention, but I’ve been giving this

02:28:31.490 --> 02:28:32.819
place an extreme makeover!”

02:28:32.819 --> 02:28:33.819
Bill yelled.

02:28:33.819 --> 02:28:37.580
“Did you forget to put on your glasses this
morning, or are you just that senile?”

02:28:37.580 --> 02:28:39.790
The stranger remained calm as could be.

02:28:39.790 --> 02:28:44.880
He replied with a voice that was measured
as it was deep, “Now, Bill, let’s not

02:28:44.880 --> 02:28:46.870
resort to name calling.

02:28:46.870 --> 02:28:49.850
That’s just childish, don’t you think?”

02:28:49.850 --> 02:28:51.750
Bill’s single eye widened at this.

02:28:51.750 --> 02:28:53.140
“Wait, Wait, hold up.

02:28:53.140 --> 02:28:55.229
How do you know my name?”

02:28:55.229 --> 02:28:56.229
Bill asked, irritated.

02:28:56.229 --> 02:28:59.351
“Are you a friend of the Time Baby or something?”

02:28:59.351 --> 02:29:03.660
He floated over and began circling the stranger,
hoping to intimidate him.

02:29:03.660 --> 02:29:06.460
Much to Bill’s frustration, it didn’t
appear to be working.

02:29:06.460 --> 02:29:12.710
“I know lots of things, Bill, lots of things,”
the stranger replied.

02:29:12.710 --> 02:29:14.720
“That’s my line!”

02:29:14.720 --> 02:29:16.400
Bill screeched, turning red.

02:29:16.400 --> 02:29:18.439
“Who do you think you are?”

02:29:18.439 --> 02:29:21.979
The stranger gave a quiet, reserved chuckle
that infuriated Bill.

02:29:21.979 --> 02:29:27.700
“Oh, personally, I just like to think of
myself as a humble craftsman, watching his

02:29:27.700 --> 02:29:30.150
beautiful creation play out,” he said.

02:29:30.150 --> 02:29:35.710
“But I suppose some of the people around
here like to call me God.”

02:29:35.710 --> 02:29:37.620
Bill didn’t like this.

02:29:37.620 --> 02:29:42.021
This whole universe was going to be his, and
he certainly didn’t appreciate some insolent

02:29:42.021 --> 02:29:45.420
old man acting like he ran the roost around
here.

02:29:45.420 --> 02:29:50.210
Bill would give him an education in who was
really holding the reins - and it would be

02:29:50.210 --> 02:29:55.010
the kind of education that left scars, if
it left anything at all.

02:29:55.010 --> 02:29:59.229
He extended his spindly black arms and released
bolts of lightning against the stranger, who

02:29:59.229 --> 02:30:04.830
simply continued to smile as the electricity
rippled around him, seemingly causing no effect.

02:30:04.830 --> 02:30:06.470
“Are you done?”

02:30:06.470 --> 02:30:07.960
the stranger asked.

02:30:07.960 --> 02:30:10.560
Bill laughed, hoping to hide his irritation.

02:30:10.560 --> 02:30:12.950
“I’m just getting started!”

02:30:12.950 --> 02:30:13.950
He bellowed.

02:30:13.950 --> 02:30:19.080
With a thunderous roar that shook the very
foundations of Site 19, Bill began to grow

02:30:19.080 --> 02:30:20.420
and shift.

02:30:20.420 --> 02:30:26.330
No longer a silly little triangle, he became
a huge, red pyramid of pure nightmares, covered

02:30:26.330 --> 02:30:31.850
in glowing golden arms and teeth, with long,
black tongues drooping out of each level.

02:30:31.850 --> 02:30:37.149
It was the most terrifying and demonic form
in his entire arsenal, and yet, he was astonished

02:30:37.149 --> 02:30:41.729
to find that the stranger still didn’t seem
to show any kind of fear.

02:30:41.729 --> 02:30:45.700
“Very impressive, Bill,” the stranger
said, sounding almost bored.

02:30:45.700 --> 02:30:50.359
“But I think you might be trying a little
too hard.”

02:30:50.359 --> 02:30:54.390
Oh, that does it; Bill would simply have to
destroy him.

02:30:54.390 --> 02:30:56.479
It was a matter of pride now.

02:30:56.479 --> 02:31:01.180
He raised several of his huge, golden fists
and began pounding down on the comparatively

02:31:01.180 --> 02:31:02.810
tiny, humanoid stranger.

02:31:02.810 --> 02:31:06.810
It was an assault so powerful that the ground
began cracking around their feet.

02:31:06.810 --> 02:31:12.210
And yet, it seemed that with almost no effort,
the stranger was able to intercept and block

02:31:12.210 --> 02:31:13.720
every single blow.

02:31:13.720 --> 02:31:15.399
Naturally, Bill was infuriated.

02:31:15.399 --> 02:31:21.229
It was time to finally unleash the full breadth
of his power on this beardy wise guy.

02:31:21.229 --> 02:31:26.561
He launched thunderbolts, fireballs, legions
of giant, mutant wasps, hailstorms, maelstroms,

02:31:26.561 --> 02:31:31.859
bubbles of pure madness, snakes made of barbed
wire, and even incredible coarse language.

02:31:31.859 --> 02:31:37.700
But despite it all, this man - the one who
claimed people call him God - was utterly

02:31:37.700 --> 02:31:38.700
unfazed.

02:31:38.700 --> 02:31:40.910
“You can dish it out,” he said.

02:31:40.910 --> 02:31:44.569
“But let’s see if you can take it.”

02:31:44.569 --> 02:31:45.750
Bill began to laugh.

02:31:45.750 --> 02:31:47.810
“What the heck is that supposed to mean?

02:31:47.810 --> 02:31:48.810
You can’t—“

02:31:48.810 --> 02:31:51.310
God snapped his fingers, and Bill was gone.

02:31:51.310 --> 02:31:52.310
Vanished.

02:31:52.310 --> 02:31:56.270
And with a flick of his wrist, all the damage
and transformations that Bill had performed

02:31:56.270 --> 02:31:57.270
had disappeared.

02:31:57.270 --> 02:32:01.690
It was as though the demonic triangle had
never even been there in the first place.

02:32:01.690 --> 02:32:06.270
Though Dr. Bright, who was acting Site Director
at the time, had some Scranton Reality Anchors

02:32:06.270 --> 02:32:09.430
turned on around the perimeter, just to be
safe.

02:32:09.430 --> 02:32:13.490
You can never be too careful with reality-warping
demons, after all.

02:32:13.490 --> 02:32:17.110
Later that day, Dr. Bright approached God,
and asked him what he’d actually done with

02:32:17.110 --> 02:32:18.110
Bill.

02:32:18.110 --> 02:32:23.189
God chuckled and replied, “For a being of
such immense power, he really had a rather

02:32:23.189 --> 02:32:27.931
childish mindset, so I sealed him away inside
a children’s cartoon, where he couldn’t

02:32:27.931 --> 02:32:29.700
do any further damage.”

02:32:29.700 --> 02:32:31.080
“What was the cartoon?”

02:32:31.080 --> 02:32:32.600
Dr. Bright asked.

02:32:32.600 --> 02:32:37.490
“A charming little Disney show called Gravity
Falls,” God replied.

02:32:37.490 --> 02:32:38.490
Addiction.

02:32:38.490 --> 02:32:44.240
It takes many forms and wears many faces,
like a demon walking among us.

02:32:44.240 --> 02:32:49.990
It takes over your life - crawling in and
changing you from the inside out.

02:32:49.990 --> 02:32:55.380
Breaking an addiction is hard, but oftentimes
not giving it up is much harder.

02:32:55.380 --> 02:33:01.100
That was a difficult lesson to learn for three
people: Joey Walker, Dolly McGregor, and Paul

02:33:01.100 --> 02:33:02.479
Ables.

02:33:02.479 --> 02:33:07.800
These three had never met one another, and
now, they never will, but each of them had

02:33:07.800 --> 02:33:10.170
two things in common.

02:33:10.170 --> 02:33:14.350
First was that they each had an addiction
they felt like they couldn’t shake, and

02:33:14.350 --> 02:33:19.030
the second was that they each had a run-in
with SCP-666.

02:33:19.030 --> 02:33:22.359
Joey Walker was at the end of his rope when
he encountered it.

02:33:22.359 --> 02:33:27.700
Everyone has bad days, but for Joey, every
day for the last fifteen years has been a

02:33:27.700 --> 02:33:28.800
bad day.

02:33:28.800 --> 02:33:34.109
He was pushing 40 with nothing to show for
it, except credit card debt, a scraggly beard,

02:33:34.109 --> 02:33:35.880
and a beat-up old Mustang.

02:33:35.880 --> 02:33:38.270
But booze had always been there for him.

02:33:38.270 --> 02:33:43.470
No matter how bad things got, he could always
count on a glass full of comfort at the end

02:33:43.470 --> 02:33:44.560
of the day.

02:33:44.560 --> 02:33:49.979
But to paraphrase a quote by Stephen King,
“Sometimes, when a man takes a drink, the

02:33:49.979 --> 02:33:51.569
drink takes the man.”

02:33:51.569 --> 02:33:54.859
And Joey Walker had been long since taken.

02:33:54.859 --> 02:34:00.200
He was a transient worker, doing jobs wherever
jobs needed doing, but he never expected that

02:34:00.200 --> 02:34:04.140
he would end up all the way to Tibet working
construction.

02:34:04.140 --> 02:34:08.271
Not that he was complaining - Sure, it was
cold, but there was plenty of Tibetan Chang

02:34:08.271 --> 02:34:09.490
to enjoy.

02:34:09.490 --> 02:34:15.370
It was a drink so good that legends even say
that Yetis would raid villages in the mountains

02:34:15.370 --> 02:34:17.439
to get a little taste.

02:34:17.439 --> 02:34:21.940
Joey had taken a liking to the Chang, and
it was what he had been drinking when he crashed

02:34:21.940 --> 02:34:25.500
his car up in the mountains, leaving him stranded
in the snow.

02:34:25.500 --> 02:34:31.069
Joey had survived the crash itself, but he
knew he wouldn’t last long in the cold.

02:34:31.069 --> 02:34:32.069
He needed shelter.

02:34:32.069 --> 02:34:35.979
That’s why he felt like he could hardly
believe his luck when he first saw the Yurt

02:34:35.979 --> 02:34:40.439
- a kind of traditional, Tibetan tent made
from animal skins.

02:34:40.439 --> 02:34:45.270
Joey had never seen anything quite like it,
but any refuge from the storm would do.

02:34:45.270 --> 02:34:48.609
He pushed forward through the snow and climbed
inside.

02:34:48.609 --> 02:34:51.720
But the inside of the Yurt was nothing like
the outside.

02:34:51.720 --> 02:34:57.250
In fact, it seemed like an exact replica of
his favorite sports bar back in Atlantic City.

02:34:57.250 --> 02:35:02.460
It was warm, there was all the old memorabilia
on the walls, and every screen was showing

02:35:02.460 --> 02:35:07.000
the Saints wiping the floor with the Colts
in the 2010 Superbowl.

02:35:07.000 --> 02:35:08.590
Joey didn’t even question it.

02:35:08.590 --> 02:35:10.930
He just smiled, and approached the bar.

02:35:10.930 --> 02:35:15.721
He even recognized the bartender - Malcolm,
a good old friend of his.

02:35:15.721 --> 02:35:20.570
Malcolm smiled back at him, but there was
something oddly menacing in his grin.

02:35:20.570 --> 02:35:21.840
“Welcome back,” he said.

02:35:21.840 --> 02:35:25.010
“I thought you’d hauled your sorry keister
off to Tibet.

02:35:25.010 --> 02:35:28.710
Guess you gave up on that too, just like everything
else.

02:35:28.710 --> 02:35:30.870
Well, except…”

02:35:30.870 --> 02:35:34.851
Malcolm pushed a glass of beer towards him
across the bar, and glared.

02:35:34.851 --> 02:35:39.860
Joey didn’t understand why Malcolm was being
so aggressive, but he didn’t question that,

02:35:39.860 --> 02:35:40.860
either.

02:35:40.860 --> 02:35:44.771
He grabbed the glass and drank up, guzzling
it down before slamming the empty glass down

02:35:44.771 --> 02:35:45.790
on the bar.

02:35:45.790 --> 02:35:50.040
Malcolm kept the drinks coming, round after
round after round, and Joey kept knocking

02:35:50.040 --> 02:35:51.109
them back.

02:35:51.109 --> 02:35:53.800
He didn’t notice when the TV screens turned
to static.

02:35:53.800 --> 02:35:58.561
He didn’t notice when the other patrons
at the bar began to jitter and twitch, turning,

02:35:58.561 --> 02:36:01.510
little by little, into something less than
human.

02:36:01.510 --> 02:36:06.630
He didn’t even notice when Malcolm’s face
started melting off his skull, as long as

02:36:06.630 --> 02:36:08.130
he kept pouring.

02:36:08.130 --> 02:36:13.109
Before he could even really understand what
was happening to him, Joey Walker was dead.

02:36:13.109 --> 02:36:15.460
His liver and kidneys had given out on him.

02:36:15.460 --> 02:36:20.180
His corpse would later be found, frozen on
the Tibetan mountainside, just thirty feet

02:36:20.180 --> 02:36:22.200
away from his crashed car.

02:36:22.200 --> 02:36:25.770
The coroner’s report would list his cause
of death as, “Accidental.”

02:36:25.770 --> 02:36:27.490
But this was no accident.

02:36:27.490 --> 02:36:34.560
He’d fallen victim to SCP-666, an anomalous
Yurt known to some as the Spirit House.

02:36:34.560 --> 02:36:41.029
The being he’d called Malcolm is known to
the Foundation as SCP-666-1, and Malcolm had

02:36:41.029 --> 02:36:43.100
failed its challenge.

02:36:43.100 --> 02:36:48.540
Sadly for our inebriated friend, the penalty
for failure is death.

02:36:48.540 --> 02:36:54.319
Next on our list of human tragedies comes
Dolly McGregor, a 62-year-old woman from Anaheim,

02:36:54.319 --> 02:36:55.319
California.

02:36:55.319 --> 02:37:00.970
Dolly was never averse to the drink, but she
knew how to enjoy her Mojitos in moderation.

02:37:00.970 --> 02:37:05.990
You rarely get to 62 if you don’t, and Dolly
could tell people with pride that she had

02:37:05.990 --> 02:37:11.229
two children, and six grandchildren, whom
she didn’t see nearly often enough for her

02:37:11.229 --> 02:37:12.229
liking.

02:37:12.229 --> 02:37:18.820
She also had over $100,000 in gambling debt
owed to a number of Casinos on the Vegas Strip.

02:37:18.820 --> 02:37:23.660
Ever since her husband, Albert, had passed
away several years prior, shooting craps,

02:37:23.660 --> 02:37:27.939
playing blackjack, and whiling away the hours
in front of the slot machines had been a welcome

02:37:27.939 --> 02:37:29.939
change from loneliness.

02:37:29.939 --> 02:37:36.060
But in Vegas, fortunes can change in an instant
- Dolly had gone from being on a hot winning

02:37:36.060 --> 02:37:38.230
streak to losing everything.

02:37:38.230 --> 02:37:42.630
The casinos extended her lines of credit until
she was gambling with money she’d never

02:37:42.630 --> 02:37:46.050
be able to pay back, but that didn’t stop
her.

02:37:46.050 --> 02:37:50.570
She’d been selling off everything, even
remortgaging the house that Albert had built

02:37:50.570 --> 02:37:54.649
with his own two hands to try and keep up
with her ballooning debts.

02:37:54.649 --> 02:37:58.351
Still, it wasn’t enough, but she couldn’t
stop, either.

02:37:58.351 --> 02:38:02.640
It wasn’t even that she felt good about
it anymore, it was just that she only ever

02:38:02.640 --> 02:38:07.980
felt normal among the flashing lights of slot
machines and the clatter of dice.

02:38:07.980 --> 02:38:11.830
She needed to get away; as far away as possible.

02:38:11.830 --> 02:38:16.050
She’d heard about people reaching spiritual
enlightenment in Tibet.

02:38:16.050 --> 02:38:21.870
They’d discovered God, or Gods, or sometimes
just a sense of inner peace.

02:38:21.870 --> 02:38:25.730
Whatever it was, she needed to find it and
to get this demon off her back.

02:38:25.730 --> 02:38:29.840
So she took the last of her savings and flew
off to Tibet to clear her head.

02:38:29.840 --> 02:38:34.020
She didn’t know if there were any casinos
in Lhasa, but if there were, her money would

02:38:34.020 --> 02:38:35.710
surely be no good there.

02:38:35.710 --> 02:38:38.520
It was exactly what she needed.

02:38:38.520 --> 02:38:41.560
But Tibet wasn’t the promised land she thought
it would be.

02:38:41.560 --> 02:38:46.970
Wherever Dolly went, there she was, with the
same vices and demons chasing her.

02:38:46.970 --> 02:38:51.649
The first night she spent in Lhasa, she used
the hotel wifi to download an online poker

02:38:51.649 --> 02:38:53.069
app on her phone.

02:38:53.069 --> 02:38:57.609
This culminated in another couple thousand
dollars lost, and a panic attack that caused

02:38:57.609 --> 02:39:02.640
Dolly to throw her phone into her toilet before
wandering off into the wilderness.

02:39:02.640 --> 02:39:04.800
She just needed to get away.

02:39:04.800 --> 02:39:09.760
But time and space got away from her, and
eventually, she was knee deep in the snow.

02:39:09.760 --> 02:39:11.229
Where had she come from?

02:39:11.229 --> 02:39:12.390
Where could she go?

02:39:12.390 --> 02:39:17.180
It quickly dawned on her that, if she didn’t
find some kind of shelter soon, she’d be

02:39:17.180 --> 02:39:18.180
done for.

02:39:18.180 --> 02:39:20.470
But all she could do was keep walking…

02:39:20.470 --> 02:39:24.351
That’s when she happened upon SCP-666.

02:39:24.351 --> 02:39:27.819
The Yurt was like an oasis on the barren mountainside.

02:39:27.819 --> 02:39:32.080
She didn’t expect comfort inside, but it
could at least provide her some shelter until

02:39:32.080 --> 02:39:34.891
the staff back at the hotel noticed she was
gone.

02:39:34.891 --> 02:39:37.670
Then they’d come and save her, right?

02:39:37.670 --> 02:39:38.670
Right?

02:39:38.670 --> 02:39:43.810
But when she passed through the yak-leather
flap into the Yurt, Dolly wasn’t in an ancient

02:39:43.810 --> 02:39:48.450
tent in the Tibetan wilderness, she was on
a casino floor.

02:39:48.450 --> 02:39:53.790
There was a big, beautiful roulette table
before her, attended to by a grinning, well-dressed

02:39:53.790 --> 02:39:54.790
croupier.

02:39:54.790 --> 02:39:59.490
They were flanked by an army of slot machines,
and all the pleasing, familiar sounds of cheerful

02:39:59.490 --> 02:40:01.601
gambling rang out through the air.

02:40:01.601 --> 02:40:05.890
She approached the table, and the croupier
shook his head in what seemed like disappointment.

02:40:05.890 --> 02:40:09.410
“Back again, eh, Dolly?” he said with
a sigh.

02:40:09.410 --> 02:40:11.740
“Of course, I should have expected it.

02:40:11.740 --> 02:40:16.029
After all, what else do you have in that empty
little life of yours, hmm?

02:40:16.029 --> 02:40:18.770
Without all this, you’d be nothing, right?

02:40:18.770 --> 02:40:19.950
Nothing at all.

02:40:19.950 --> 02:40:23.780
Since Albert died and the kids want nothing
to do with you, we’re all you’ve got.

02:40:23.780 --> 02:40:26.840
So, Dolly, what’ll it be - Red or black?

02:40:26.840 --> 02:40:29.000
Are you feeling lucky?”

02:40:29.000 --> 02:40:32.580
His words wounded Dolly, but that wouldn’t
stop her.

02:40:32.580 --> 02:40:35.670
She grabbed her chips, and put them all on
red.

02:40:35.670 --> 02:40:37.710
One last spin couldn’t hurt.

02:40:37.710 --> 02:40:39.710
What did she have to lose?

02:40:39.710 --> 02:40:42.990
She blinked, and she wasn’t sitting at the
table anymore.

02:40:42.990 --> 02:40:45.450
She was upright, but she wasn’t standing.

02:40:45.450 --> 02:40:52.210
Her wrists and ankles were bound to something
- to a wheel, a giant roulette wheel, like

02:40:52.210 --> 02:40:55.500
it was some medieval torture device.

02:40:55.500 --> 02:40:57.740
The croupier was standing across from her.

02:40:57.740 --> 02:41:00.729
Well, something that used to be a croupier.

02:41:00.729 --> 02:41:06.380
His face was flickering in and out; sometimes
it was human, sometimes it was a mess of eyes

02:41:06.380 --> 02:41:07.630
and teeth.

02:41:07.630 --> 02:41:12.359
More demons were sitting at all the slot machines
behind him, pulling levers made from human

02:41:12.359 --> 02:41:13.359
bones.

02:41:13.359 --> 02:41:16.470
“Good choice, Dolly,” the croupier said.

02:41:16.470 --> 02:41:17.580
“Red suits you.”

02:41:17.580 --> 02:41:19.750
He reached out and gave the wheel a spin.

02:41:19.750 --> 02:41:25.390
Dolly was lost in an overwhelming, pulsing
cascade of lights, colors, and sounds.

02:41:25.390 --> 02:41:30.359
The horrific, tinny noises of slot machines
and the laughter of the demonic croupier.

02:41:30.359 --> 02:41:36.130
She was lost in panic and terror as she just
kept spinning, and spinning, and spinning…

02:41:36.130 --> 02:41:41.569
When her body was eventually found, her muscles
were in the advanced stages of atrophy, as

02:41:41.569 --> 02:41:43.660
though she hadn’t been moving for years.

02:41:43.660 --> 02:41:49.010
Her brain was rotted, and the cause of death
was determined as sudden cardiac arrest after

02:41:49.010 --> 02:41:52.700
an extended period of sleep-deprivation and
malnutrition.

02:41:52.700 --> 02:41:57.470
Dolly’s family would never really know what
happened to her.

02:41:57.470 --> 02:42:03.550
The SCP Foundation had learned a lot about
SCP-666 after containing it in Site 73.

02:42:03.550 --> 02:42:09.060
Its anomalous effects namely, vivid, complex,
and potentially fatal hallucinatory experiences

02:42:09.060 --> 02:42:13.529
only affect those with some kind of addiction
or dependency.

02:42:13.529 --> 02:42:17.479
To anyone else entering the Yurt, it’s just
a normal tent.

02:42:17.479 --> 02:42:22.300
But any addicts who enter will fall under
its spell, and are generally transported back

02:42:22.300 --> 02:42:25.779
to the place they were when their addiction
was at its strongest.

02:42:25.779 --> 02:42:32.350
There, they’ll encounter SCP-666-1, an entity
that takes the form of a figure from the subject’s

02:42:32.350 --> 02:42:37.149
life - normally one heavily involved in facilitating
their addiction.

02:42:37.149 --> 02:42:43.430
Any kind of addiction seems to trigger it
- alcohol, drugs, gambling, pornography, food,

02:42:43.430 --> 02:42:46.979
self-destructive behavior, even video games.

02:42:46.979 --> 02:42:53.040
SCP-666 kills its victims with a twisted mockery
of the very thing they were dependent on in

02:42:53.040 --> 02:42:54.040
life.

02:42:54.040 --> 02:42:58.680
It was only with Paul Ables that the Foundation
started discovering the other side of the

02:42:58.680 --> 02:42:59.680
coin.

02:42:59.680 --> 02:43:04.040
By almost all accounts, Paul is a worse person
than anyone on this list.

02:43:04.040 --> 02:43:08.600
He got addicted to hard drugs early on in
life, and took up a life of violent crime

02:43:08.600 --> 02:43:10.109
to support his habit.

02:43:10.109 --> 02:43:14.800
He murdered two people during a liquor store
robbery, before being convicted and sentenced

02:43:14.800 --> 02:43:15.800
to death.

02:43:15.800 --> 02:43:20.600
He’d then been picked up as a D-Class by
the SCP Foundation, and selected as a test

02:43:20.600 --> 02:43:25.170
subject for SCP-666 due to his history of
drug abuse.

02:43:25.170 --> 02:43:29.740
The Foundation expected to be adding his body
to the incineration pile sometime soon.

02:43:29.740 --> 02:43:34.910
None of the researchers working on the case
predicted what actually ended up happening.

02:43:34.910 --> 02:43:37.340
Paul was forced to enter the Yurt.

02:43:37.340 --> 02:43:42.410
Not long after, he found himself standing
in a place he’d done everything to try to

02:43:42.410 --> 02:43:47.439
forget: The dark, graffiti-stained alley where
he’d been sold his first hit.

02:43:47.439 --> 02:43:48.950
This was the place.

02:43:48.950 --> 02:43:52.160
The place that destroyed his life.

02:43:52.160 --> 02:43:55.970
Every bad decision he’d ever made could
be traced back to here.

02:43:55.970 --> 02:43:59.020
And specifically to one man…

02:43:59.020 --> 02:44:00.020
Frank.

02:44:00.020 --> 02:44:06.510
Frank was his first dealer, and how here he
was, standing right across from him once more.

02:44:06.510 --> 02:44:08.090
Frank was grinning like a demon.

02:44:08.090 --> 02:44:09.880
“C’mon, Paulie,” he said.

02:44:09.880 --> 02:44:10.970
“You’re gutter trash.

02:44:10.970 --> 02:44:13.030
We both know what you’re going to do.

02:44:13.030 --> 02:44:14.150
Don’t you feel it?

02:44:14.150 --> 02:44:15.490
The itch?

02:44:15.490 --> 02:44:17.830
One more hit, Paulie, that’s all you need
to feel better.

02:44:17.830 --> 02:44:20.569
It’s time to take your medicine…”

02:44:20.569 --> 02:44:23.860
Frank - or this thing, pretending to be Frank
- was right.

02:44:23.860 --> 02:44:25.230
He did feel the itch.

02:44:25.230 --> 02:44:26.990
He did want it.

02:44:26.990 --> 02:44:28.590
Maybe he was no better than this.

02:44:28.590 --> 02:44:33.399
He began to reach out towards Frank, but then
he abruptly pulled his hand back.

02:44:33.399 --> 02:44:38.101
Frank’s eyes widened in genuine surprise,
as Paul replied, “I’m sorry.

02:44:38.101 --> 02:44:40.710
That’s not me anymore.”

02:44:40.710 --> 02:44:46.340
SCP-666-1 gave a smile, and said, “Maybe
it isn’t, Paulie, maybe it isn’t…”

02:44:46.340 --> 02:44:52.130
When Paul Ables was removed from the SCP-666
Yurt by one of the attending guards, the Foundation

02:44:52.130 --> 02:44:54.820
researchers discovered something amazing.

02:44:54.820 --> 02:45:00.850
Paul was very much alive, and more incredibly,
he didn’t feel the cravings anymore.

02:45:00.850 --> 02:45:03.140
His addiction was gone.

02:45:03.140 --> 02:45:07.580
And further tests showed that Paul wasn’t
a one-off event.In fact, anyone who denies

02:45:07.580 --> 02:45:14.529
the temptation of SCP-666 will see their addictions
miraculously disappear when they finally leave.

02:45:14.529 --> 02:45:19.440
After this it became clear to the Foundation
that SCP-666 isn’t just a way to punish

02:45:19.440 --> 02:45:22.440
addicts, it’s a kind of test.

02:45:22.440 --> 02:45:26.330
Those who want to change, who are willing
to truly confront their demons and resist

02:45:26.330 --> 02:45:31.820
the pull of temptation are rewarded with the
one thing they want most in life, freedom

02:45:31.820 --> 02:45:34.000
from their addiction.

02:45:34.000 --> 02:45:38.560
SCP-666 can be your doom or your salvation.

02:45:38.560 --> 02:45:43.060
And like most things in life, you get what
you give.

02:45:43.060 --> 02:45:47.729
One fine morning, your distant Aunt Carol
came to your family home in an almost frantic

02:45:47.729 --> 02:45:49.450
state of excitement.

02:45:49.450 --> 02:45:54.200
Carol had always been a bit eccentric, totally
harmless, of course, but what you’d describe

02:45:54.200 --> 02:45:57.140
as being on the more “zealous” side of
religious.

02:45:57.140 --> 02:46:01.290
Predictably, she wanted to ask you and your
family to come to church with her.

02:46:01.290 --> 02:46:05.020
Seeing as you don’t see Aunt Carol often,
you and your family decide that there’s

02:46:05.020 --> 02:46:06.500
no harm in indulging her.

02:46:06.500 --> 02:46:11.450
You’re not an atheist family by any means,
in fact you were all raised Catholic, but

02:46:11.450 --> 02:46:14.900
it felt like it’d been forever since you
last went to church.

02:46:14.900 --> 02:46:19.890
Aunt Carol wanted to show you and your family
the special celebrations that went on at her

02:46:19.890 --> 02:46:20.890
church.

02:46:20.890 --> 02:46:24.609
You remember her practically grabbing you
by the wrist and dragging you to the building,

02:46:24.609 --> 02:46:27.120
her eyes filled with a crazed enthusiasm.

02:46:27.120 --> 02:46:33.220
That’s when you saw something incredibly
strange, there were shadows moving behind

02:46:33.220 --> 02:46:35.790
the elaborate stained glass windows.

02:46:35.790 --> 02:46:38.830
Thousands of tiny shadows, darting around.

02:46:38.830 --> 02:46:42.390
And this low humming noise you faintly recognized.

02:46:42.390 --> 02:46:44.210
What was that noise?

02:46:44.210 --> 02:46:48.779
It was the cry of cicadas, but this was only
early spring.

02:46:48.779 --> 02:46:51.430
What were cicadas doing awake at this time
of year?

02:46:51.430 --> 02:46:54.150
You didn’t get much time to ponder this
question.

02:46:54.150 --> 02:46:59.230
In the next few seconds, you and the entire
church were surrounded by heavy duty tactical

02:46:59.230 --> 02:47:00.230
vehicles.

02:47:00.230 --> 02:47:04.189
What appeared to be a large and heavily-armed
SWAT team poured out of the vehicles.

02:47:04.189 --> 02:47:09.400
Unbeknownst to you, these were a Mobile Task
Force sent in by the SCP Foundation.

02:47:09.400 --> 02:47:16.360
Specifically, MTF Y-99, also known as the
Altar Boys, a specially trained group of Foundation

02:47:16.360 --> 02:47:18.830
agents used for anomalies of a religious nature.

02:47:18.830 --> 02:47:24.910
You, your Aunt, and the rest of your family
are rounded up to be debriefed and given amnestics.

02:47:24.910 --> 02:47:29.100
One of the last memories they took from you
was the sight of Foundation Agents dragging

02:47:29.100 --> 02:47:31.500
bloodied bodies out of the church.

02:47:31.500 --> 02:47:36.480
As the doors opened, thousands of cicadas
streamed out and dispersed into the skies.

02:47:36.480 --> 02:47:41.530
But these weren’t like any kind of cicada
you’d never seen, they were beautiful, their

02:47:41.530 --> 02:47:45.681
rainbow-colored wings reminding you of ornate
stained glass.

02:47:45.681 --> 02:47:50.080
Who could have guessed that these pretty little
bugs are tied to an entity very likely to

02:47:50.080 --> 02:47:54.560
bring about an XK-Class End of the World Scenario
some day in the future?

02:47:54.560 --> 02:47:59.399
The bugs, the bodies in the church, and even
your aunt’s incredibly strange behavior

02:47:59.399 --> 02:48:05.939
all fall under the umbrella of a Keter-Class
anomaly known as SCP-3004.

02:48:05.939 --> 02:48:10.880
But to truly understand this anomaly that
was once thought to be destroyed, and the

02:48:10.880 --> 02:48:17.149
implications of it still living today, we
need to go back 600 years, to Ireland in the

02:48:17.149 --> 02:48:18.729
15th Century.

02:48:18.729 --> 02:48:23.810
This era was believed to be the origin of
a Gaelic religious movement known as “Cétlaidí”,

02:48:23.810 --> 02:48:27.890
or the “The Singers” in English, a splinter
sect of Druidism.

02:48:27.890 --> 02:48:32.710
But this was no fringe cult, The Singers were
a mainstream religion in the British Isles

02:48:32.710 --> 02:48:35.000
for several hundred years.

02:48:35.000 --> 02:48:39.870
Its members included people of all social
classes, from lowly peasants to powerful and

02:48:39.870 --> 02:48:41.561
respected figures.

02:48:41.561 --> 02:48:46.010
They mingled heavily with Christians, mostly
Irish Catholics, and at some points in history

02:48:46.010 --> 02:48:50.540
came close to overtaking Christianity as the
dominant religion in Ireland.

02:48:50.540 --> 02:48:55.531
So, who were these people, if they’re supposedly
such a large part of recent history in the

02:48:55.531 --> 02:48:56.531
area?

02:48:56.531 --> 02:49:01.130
Like most Druids, their relationship with
nature was a key part of their belief system.

02:49:01.130 --> 02:49:07.280
In particular, they prized an extinct species
of Cicada known as Cicadetta luculenta, or

02:49:07.280 --> 02:49:10.000
the “stained glass cicada”, in English.

02:49:10.000 --> 02:49:14.529
The life cycle of birth and resurrection that
the cicadas underwent fascinated the Singers,

02:49:14.529 --> 02:49:17.960
and they performed a number of holy rituals
around it.

02:49:17.960 --> 02:49:22.239
One recorded ritual was the celebration of
children entering adulthood that was marked

02:49:22.239 --> 02:49:24.819
by them first losing their baby teeth.

02:49:24.819 --> 02:49:29.580
But the rituals of the Singers accidentally
opened some kind of door to a being from a

02:49:29.580 --> 02:49:35.300
different plane of reality, dubbed SCP-3004-1
by the Foundation.

02:49:35.300 --> 02:49:39.870
This being is an immensely powerful thought-form
that the Foundation believes to be a “Pistiphage”,

02:49:39.870 --> 02:49:41.460
or “Faith Eater.”

02:49:41.460 --> 02:49:46.560
It appears to have been attracted to our universe
by the rituals of the Singers, and so took

02:49:46.560 --> 02:49:52.930
a form relevant to their beliefs, namely,
a huge cicada, in order to feed on their faith.

02:49:52.930 --> 02:49:57.989
If things had stopped there then this would
be an almost innocent symbiotic relationship,

02:49:57.989 --> 02:50:04.649
but the interactions between SCP-3004-1 and
our world led to dangerous consequences due

02:50:04.649 --> 02:50:07.540
to its powerful reality-warping abilities.

02:50:07.540 --> 02:50:12.210
For example, during some rituals, huge numbers
of stained glass cicadas would burst from

02:50:12.210 --> 02:50:16.540
the mouths of those participating, often causing
them to choke to death.

02:50:16.540 --> 02:50:21.940
Other times 3004-1 would manifest physically
in the sky above its new worshippers, causing

02:50:21.940 --> 02:50:28.021
painful boils on whoever witnessed it, and
occasionally symptoms akin to radiation sickness.

02:50:28.021 --> 02:50:34.149
It appeared that 3004-1 was growing more powerful
over time, and its rise to power was intrinsically

02:50:34.149 --> 02:50:39.120
linked to the rituals of the Singers and the
existence of the stained glass cicadas.

02:50:39.120 --> 02:50:43.989
Two groups that pre-dated the Foundation,
the Vatican’s “Congregation for Otherworldly

02:50:43.989 --> 02:50:49.330
Acts” and the English Government’s “Royal
Society for the Imprisonment of Abnormalcy”,

02:50:49.330 --> 02:50:52.859
essentially performed an all-out religious
genocide on the Singers.

02:50:52.859 --> 02:50:56.841
No meaningful trace of the religion was left
when they were done, aside from their own

02:50:56.841 --> 02:50:57.910
records.

02:50:57.910 --> 02:51:02.689
While they were at it, they also exterminated
all the stained glass cicadas, leading to

02:51:02.689 --> 02:51:06.530
a complete stop of all SCP-3004 activity.

02:51:06.530 --> 02:51:12.689
It seemed like, despite the great human and
ecological cost, the anomaly had been neutralized.

02:51:12.689 --> 02:51:17.830
A few centuries later though, a series of
strange, cicada-related anomalous events started

02:51:17.830 --> 02:51:20.229
to occur across the United States.

02:51:20.229 --> 02:51:26.370
A strange man, seemingly made almost entirely
from cicada chitin, would appear at christenings,

02:51:26.370 --> 02:51:28.560
weddings, and funerals.

02:51:28.560 --> 02:51:33.020
Each time, his presence would cause the people
in attendance to do and experience horrific

02:51:33.020 --> 02:51:38.609
things and lead to legacies of hardship and
death that would linger for decades.

02:51:38.609 --> 02:51:44.230
This became known as SCP-2852, or “Cousin
Johnny” and it should have been the first

02:51:44.230 --> 02:51:48.770
clue that the nightmare of SCP-3004 was resurfacing.

02:51:48.770 --> 02:51:53.859
But since 3004 was already archived as “neutralized”,
nobody made the connection.

02:51:53.859 --> 02:52:02.170
Some time later, SCP-2852 incidents ceased,
and around that exact time, SCP-3004 instances

02:52:02.170 --> 02:52:03.649
started anew.

02:52:03.649 --> 02:52:08.729
It manifested in the form of strange, anomalous
activities taking place at Christian church

02:52:08.729 --> 02:52:15.521
services, specifically, those from Roman Catholic,
Eastern Catholic, Anglican, and Episcopalian

02:52:15.521 --> 02:52:16.600
communities.

02:52:16.600 --> 02:52:21.521
The only clues to outsiders would be an increase
in reported church attendance, and an increase

02:52:21.521 --> 02:52:24.970
in deaths from “natural causes” within
the community.

02:52:24.970 --> 02:52:29.670
These two stats were how the Foundation first
noticed something was amiss.

02:52:29.670 --> 02:52:36.170
Just as it had done with the Singers centuries
before, SCP-3004-1 had latched onto the beliefs

02:52:36.170 --> 02:52:42.650
and rituals of Christians, and was using this
new connection to harvest more faith for sustenance.

02:52:42.650 --> 02:52:44.210
The results were twofold.

02:52:44.210 --> 02:52:49.180
First, religious fervor and excitement to
attend church services saw a huge increase.

02:52:49.180 --> 02:52:54.180
Secondly, the actual content of these services
took a hard turn for the horrific.

02:52:54.180 --> 02:52:58.520
Much like Cousin Johnny infiltrations, this
really isn’t for the faint of heart by any

02:52:58.520 --> 02:52:59.560
definition.

02:52:59.560 --> 02:53:05.040
For example, young people with Christ-like
stigmata wounds being bitten to death by priests.

02:53:05.040 --> 02:53:09.750
Children removing the teeth of priests, before
they all start vomiting huge numbers of stained

02:53:09.750 --> 02:53:11.229
glass cicadas.

02:53:11.229 --> 02:53:16.010
There were extremely unpleasant rituals involving
castration and even a pregnant woman giving

02:53:16.010 --> 02:53:20.000
birth to even more swarms of stained glass
cicadas.

02:53:20.000 --> 02:53:23.330
We could go on, but you probably get the idea.

02:53:23.330 --> 02:53:29.970
Rituals inspired by SCP-3004-1 are horrific,
and all seem to involve the same extinct breed

02:53:29.970 --> 02:53:34.779
of stained glass cicadas worshipped by the
Singers before their annihilation.

02:53:34.779 --> 02:53:41.090
But how can these insects, which have been
dubbed SCP-3004-2, be here in the present

02:53:41.090 --> 02:53:45.390
if the Foundation forerunners made them extinct
so many centuries ago?

02:53:45.390 --> 02:53:47.750
The answer is simple, but strange.

02:53:47.750 --> 02:53:52.460
While they have all the hallmarks of being
alive, the stained glass cicadas present during

02:53:52.460 --> 02:53:57.000
modern iterations of SCP-3004 events aren’t
actually real.

02:53:57.000 --> 02:54:02.420
Genetic tests have shown that they’re actually
made from a mix of wood and real stained glass.

02:54:02.420 --> 02:54:06.689
These insects fly away from the scene after
the rituals are completed, traveling around

02:54:06.689 --> 02:54:10.750
six hundred miles from the site before disappearing
completely.

02:54:10.750 --> 02:54:16.189
The Foundation was growing concerned about
the nature of SCP-3004, especially given that

02:54:16.189 --> 02:54:20.340
instances were becoming more frequent and
harder to contain.

02:54:20.340 --> 02:54:25.230
Foundation scientists determined that the
creature known as 3004-1 likely existed within

02:54:25.230 --> 02:54:30.830
a layer of reality just above our own, and
if it ever managed to breach our reality,

02:54:30.830 --> 02:54:34.990
the worldwide level of violence and chaos
it could cause would likely lead to an XK-Class

02:54:34.990 --> 02:54:37.310
End of the World Scenario.

02:54:37.310 --> 02:54:41.810
Drastic actions would once again be needed
to prevent this, so they devised an emergency

02:54:41.810 --> 02:54:45.930
containment procedure that would only be used
as a last resort.

02:54:45.930 --> 02:54:51.270
The procedure, known as Protocol Damnatio
ad Bestias, would use a mixture of mass amnestic

02:54:51.270 --> 02:54:56.760
treatment and Thaumiel objects to completely
erase Christianity from not only the modern

02:54:56.760 --> 02:55:02.930
world, but all of history in the hopes of
cutting off 3004-1’s food supply to kill

02:55:02.930 --> 02:55:07.170
the entity or at least prevent it from entering
our world.

02:55:07.170 --> 02:55:11.649
The plan would center on placing a powerful
Roman-Catholic reality warper, who volunteered

02:55:11.649 --> 02:55:16.840
for the job of course, into an anomalous group
of machines known as “The Lions.”

02:55:16.840 --> 02:55:21.850
By submitting the reality warper to a lifetime
of suffering and essentially erasing him from

02:55:21.850 --> 02:55:27.100
existence, so too will it erase the world’s
full knowledge of Christianity, and hopefully

02:55:27.100 --> 02:55:28.739
save the world.

02:55:28.739 --> 02:55:32.800
This man will become the last martyr, dying
for all of humanity.

02:55:32.800 --> 02:55:38.359
He will become the last saint, St. Jude the
Damned, Bulwark Against Darkness

02:55:38.359 --> 02:55:40.870
You might ask: Are you sure this is necessary?

02:55:40.870 --> 02:55:42.890
There’s so much we don’t know about 3004-1.

02:55:42.890 --> 02:55:46.430
Do we know for a fact it’s this dangerous?

02:55:46.430 --> 02:55:51.750
Enter Agent Timothy Luttermann, a member of
Mobile Task Force Sigma-25, also known as

02:55:51.750 --> 02:55:53.390
“Ghostbusters.”

02:55:53.390 --> 02:55:58.420
Luttermann was part of a Foundation project
known as SIGHTSEE-LUX, using an astral projection

02:55:58.420 --> 02:56:03.070
technology that would free his consciousness
from his body, and allow it to travel freely

02:56:03.070 --> 02:56:05.160
between metaphysical planes.

02:56:05.160 --> 02:56:10.210
In plain English, they could use Luttermann’s
floating mind as a kind of spy, and insert

02:56:10.210 --> 02:56:13.300
it into 3004-1’s dimension.

02:56:13.300 --> 02:56:18.580
They achieved this by capturing one of 3004-1’s
false stained glass cicadas, and releasing

02:56:18.580 --> 02:56:22.989
it again, allowing Luttermann’s mind to
follow it home to its master.

02:56:22.989 --> 02:56:28.130
However, what was thought to be a simple intel
gathering mission turned into a complete nightmare.

02:56:28.130 --> 02:56:34.040
Luttermann found that 3004-1’s dimension
was entirely void, aside from the entity itself,

02:56:34.040 --> 02:56:37.610
and the millions of buzzing stained glass
cicadas.

02:56:37.610 --> 02:56:42.090
The entity was so huge and so complex that
it physically hurt to look at.

02:56:42.090 --> 02:56:47.370
Luttermann observed that its form kept shifting,
from a giant cicada, to an old man, to a cicada

02:56:47.370 --> 02:56:52.520
nailed to a wooden cross, to an infinite mess
of wood and stained glass.

02:56:52.520 --> 02:56:57.800
But even more terrifying than its physical
appearance were the contents of its mind.

02:56:57.800 --> 02:57:03.689
3004-1 forced itself into Agent Luttermann’s
brain, and in that moment, he finally understood

02:57:03.689 --> 02:57:04.689
it.

02:57:04.689 --> 02:57:10.439
The entity, which had no concept of metaphors,
allegory, or the divide between fact and fiction,

02:57:10.439 --> 02:57:15.100
truly believed that it was the Abrahamic God
depicted in the bible, and that all Christians

02:57:15.100 --> 02:57:17.080
are lovingly worshipping it.

02:57:17.080 --> 02:57:22.290
In its rituals, it was imposing some of the
bloodiest parts of the bible onto its flock,

02:57:22.290 --> 02:57:23.899
believing that’s what they wanted.

02:57:23.899 --> 02:57:28.710
All the while, it fed on their faith, growing
bigger and more powerful.

02:57:28.710 --> 02:57:32.820
Luttermann found that just being there with
the creature was hurting his soul.

02:57:32.820 --> 02:57:37.880
If it wasn’t a God yet, he believed it had
the power to become one in time and he advised

02:57:37.880 --> 02:57:41.450
that the Foundation shouldn’t send anyone
else to its dimension.

02:57:41.450 --> 02:57:44.340
It was too great a risk to all life on Earth.

02:57:44.340 --> 02:57:50.510
Perhaps, to prevent the horrible fate of us
all being destroyed by 3004-1, erasing Christianity

02:57:50.510 --> 02:57:52.739
would be a worthy sacrifice.

02:57:52.739 --> 02:57:54.880
That is, if it actually works.

02:57:54.880 --> 02:58:00.069
After all, they thought destroying the Singers
would neutralize 3004 once and for all, and

02:58:00.069 --> 02:58:02.029
yet here it is again.

02:58:02.029 --> 02:58:06.689
For all we know, we may just be prolonging
the inevitable...

02:58:06.689 --> 02:58:10.850
If you ever studied Ancient Egypt in your
history class, then you are probably familiar

02:58:10.850 --> 02:58:12.859
with the way they buried their pharaohs.

02:58:12.859 --> 02:58:18.380
When a king of Egypt died, their body would
be entombed in a huge sarcophagus, usually

02:58:18.380 --> 02:58:20.770
after being mummified.

02:58:20.770 --> 02:58:25.279
Mummification was the process that the Ancient
Egyptians used to preserve their dead, safeguarding

02:58:25.279 --> 02:58:30.480
a corpse with special chemicals and the application
of cloth, almost like bandages.

02:58:30.480 --> 02:58:34.739
This was done to keep cadavers from decaying,
usually because of the belief that this would

02:58:34.739 --> 02:58:36.910
carry over into the afterlife.

02:58:36.910 --> 02:58:41.739
And it wasn’t just the Egyptians that practiced
mummification either, mummies of human beings

02:58:41.739 --> 02:58:45.890
or animals have been found on almost every
continent in the world.

02:58:45.890 --> 02:58:51.260
Sometimes, a body can even be accidentally
mummified, through exposure to extreme cold,

02:58:51.260 --> 02:58:56.510
lack of oxygen or other environmental factors
that help keep the deceased preserved.

02:58:56.510 --> 02:59:02.100
Fun fact, the oldest recorded mummy isn’t
even one left behind by the Ancient Egyptians.

02:59:02.100 --> 02:59:07.330
It is actually a naturally mummified severed
head estimated to be 6000 years old.

02:59:07.330 --> 02:59:10.771
It was unearthed in South America in 1936.

02:59:10.771 --> 02:59:18.490
Yes, corpse preservation techniques can indeed
be strange, but none are stranger than SCP-1176,

02:59:18.490 --> 02:59:21.850
also known by the nickname “The Mellified
Man.”

02:59:21.850 --> 02:59:26.880
Now, as you may have already pieced together,
the Mellified Man is a mummified corpse, but

02:59:26.880 --> 02:59:31.160
not quite like the ones you would expect to
find buried in the Pyramids.

02:59:31.160 --> 02:59:35.770
Estimated by Foundation researchers to have
been a man in his mid-thirties when he died,

02:59:35.770 --> 02:59:41.590
SCP-1176 is a corpse that has degraded so
much over the centuries that it has made DNA

02:59:41.590 --> 02:59:43.640
examination impossible.

02:59:43.640 --> 02:59:50.040
According to some of the SCP Foundation’s
best minds, SCP-1176 is possibly of Arabian

02:59:50.040 --> 02:59:54.939
ancestry, and thought to have passed away
sometime during either the 10th or the 11th

02:59:54.939 --> 02:59:56.800
centuries AD.

02:59:56.800 --> 03:00:01.490
This is certainly not your ordinary mummy,
and it definitely isn’t like the kind you’d

03:00:01.490 --> 03:00:05.220
see in a cheesy black and white horror movie
or an old episode of Scooby-Doo.

03:00:05.220 --> 03:00:11.710
SCP-1176 is absolutely, undoubtedly dead by
all clinical definitions.

03:00:11.710 --> 03:00:16.310
It doesn’t show any signs of breathing,
and the processes of blood circulation or

03:00:16.310 --> 03:00:19.240
metabolism have long since stopped.

03:00:19.240 --> 03:00:24.850
However, despite the decay suffered by the
rest of the body, SCP-1176’s brain seems

03:00:24.850 --> 03:00:29.020
to have remained intact for almost ten whole
centuries.

03:00:29.020 --> 03:00:31.891
Not just intact, but active.

03:00:31.891 --> 03:00:36.380
The Foundation’s researchers have confirmed
that the brain has a constant level of electrical

03:00:36.380 --> 03:00:41.710
activity, consistent with people experiencing
stage 3 non-rapid eye movement sleep, known

03:00:41.710 --> 03:00:44.189
colloquially as “deep sleep.”

03:00:44.189 --> 03:00:47.649
So, a mummy with an active, albeit dormant
brain.

03:00:47.649 --> 03:00:51.529
How does an ancient culture manage to achieve
preservation like this?

03:00:51.529 --> 03:00:52.880
Alien technology?

03:00:52.880 --> 03:00:54.899
Cryogenic sleep chambers?

03:00:54.899 --> 03:00:56.400
Suspended animation?

03:00:56.400 --> 03:01:04.439
No, not quite, SCP-1176 exists in its current
state, in part, because the body has been

03:01:04.439 --> 03:01:05.439
mellified.

03:01:05.439 --> 03:01:10.910
Now, this was a process a lot like mummification,
but instead of wrapping them in cloth, a Mellified

03:01:10.910 --> 03:01:16.390
Man or a “human mummy confection” was
created by submerging a dead body in honey.

03:01:16.390 --> 03:01:20.609
According to historical records, elderly men
in Arabic countries would sometimes willingly

03:01:20.609 --> 03:01:23.370
volunteer themselves for this process.

03:01:23.370 --> 03:01:24.370
Why?

03:01:24.370 --> 03:01:27.990
Because the goal was to turn their bodies
into a healing confection.

03:01:27.990 --> 03:01:32.850
In other words, an elaborate sweet delicacy
created from a preserved corpse.

03:01:32.850 --> 03:01:37.890
That’s right, ancient cultures had candy
made from dead people.

03:01:37.890 --> 03:01:42.892
All the information the Foundation has gathered
about SCP-1176 seems to point to the body

03:01:42.892 --> 03:01:45.260
being one such mellified man.

03:01:45.260 --> 03:01:49.380
When extracting the remaining bodily fluids
from the corpse, instead of finding blood

03:01:49.380 --> 03:01:56.580
and other normal substances, Foundation researchers
discovered that SCP-1176 was full of a viscous,

03:01:56.580 --> 03:02:02.330
gold colored liquid that they designated as
SCP-1176-1.

03:02:02.330 --> 03:02:06.680
Further testing of this fluid revealed it
to be, you guessed it, honey.

03:02:06.680 --> 03:02:11.479
Specifically, it was a type known as clover
honey, made by a species called the Anatolian

03:02:11.479 --> 03:02:12.649
honey bee.

03:02:12.649 --> 03:02:19.440
This stuff was everywhere, filling SCP-1176
entirely, so much so that honey was even coming

03:02:19.440 --> 03:02:21.470
out of the body’s pores.

03:02:21.470 --> 03:02:24.180
This is due to the nature of the mellification
process.

03:02:24.180 --> 03:02:29.060
Typically, before death, a person who had
offered to sacrifice their own body would

03:02:29.060 --> 03:02:31.020
stop eating any food.

03:02:31.020 --> 03:02:35.359
Instead, their diet would consist solely of
honey, and nothing else.

03:02:35.359 --> 03:02:40.270
They would even bathe in it, submerging their
entire body in the substance inside and out

03:02:40.270 --> 03:02:44.470
until their sweat, and even their feces were
pure honey.

03:02:44.470 --> 03:02:48.610
This honey-only diet would eventually kill
the donor, and their corpse would be placed

03:02:48.610 --> 03:02:53.250
in a stone coffin, which was also filled up
with even more honey.

03:02:53.250 --> 03:02:58.250
After approximately one hundred years, what
would be left was human mummy confection,

03:02:58.250 --> 03:03:03.100
a honey based candy of sorts, that could then
be sold at street markets for a high value

03:03:03.100 --> 03:03:04.189
price.

03:03:04.189 --> 03:03:05.360
Why was it so expensive?

03:03:05.360 --> 03:03:09.960
Well, not just because it was literally made
from a dead person, but also because this

03:03:09.960 --> 03:03:14.811
confection was believed to possess rare and
powerful healing properties.

03:03:14.811 --> 03:03:19.090
Everything from the common cold to broken
bones was said to be cured by it.

03:03:19.090 --> 03:03:24.960
Despite it leaking out of SCP-1176, the honey
doesn’t seem to ever run out, even when

03:03:24.960 --> 03:03:27.450
tested under varying conditions.

03:03:27.450 --> 03:03:33.210
It seems like the Mellified Man actively produces
more of the sweet, golden substance, acting

03:03:33.210 --> 03:03:36.910
as the source rather than a container with
a finite amount.

03:03:36.910 --> 03:03:40.640
And yes, it’s still edible after several
centuries.

03:03:40.640 --> 03:03:44.900
In fact, it contains an abundance of essential
vitamins and nutrients.

03:03:44.900 --> 03:03:49.800
According to the Foundation’s testing, the
honey produced by SCP-1176 can suppress the

03:03:49.800 --> 03:03:54.689
feeling of hunger for up to eighteen whole
hours, and there are no long term side effects

03:03:54.689 --> 03:03:56.109
for most that eat it.

03:03:56.109 --> 03:03:58.850
However, this is not the case for everyone.

03:03:58.850 --> 03:04:03.740
The Foundation has learned that any person
without the blood type AB+ will have a severe

03:04:03.740 --> 03:04:07.150
allergic reaction should they consume any
of SCP-1176-1.

03:04:07.150 --> 03:04:14.380
The symptoms include acute hemolysis, which
means the red blood cells won’t break down

03:04:14.380 --> 03:04:18.811
properly, and renal failure, which is when
the kidneys stop functioning.

03:04:18.811 --> 03:04:26.130
This all results in death for most of the
subjects without AB+ blood who were fed SCP-1176-1.

03:04:26.130 --> 03:04:30.500
The symptoms for these unlucky people were
the same as receiving an incompatible blood

03:04:30.500 --> 03:04:33.030
type after a transfusion.

03:04:33.030 --> 03:04:39.210
In 1985, the SCP Foundation launched a raid
on a facility in Asmara, Eritrea, which at

03:04:39.210 --> 03:04:43.510
the time was owned by a group called the Manna
Charitable Foundation.

03:04:43.510 --> 03:04:47.729
Agents had been dispatched to this facility
after various rumors and reports that pointed

03:04:47.729 --> 03:04:52.070
to this location being the source of a strange
honey substance.

03:04:52.070 --> 03:04:56.450
This anomalous liquid was being shipped to
a number of areas in Ethiopia that had been

03:04:56.450 --> 03:04:57.970
stricken with famine.

03:04:57.970 --> 03:05:02.060
Pretty easy to guess where the Manna Charitable
Foundation got all that honey, right?

03:05:02.060 --> 03:05:09.360
The problem was, because SCP-1176-1 caused
adverse effects on people without AB+ blood,

03:05:09.360 --> 03:05:13.229
a considerable amount of civilians had died
from consuming it.

03:05:13.229 --> 03:05:16.550
Hence, the SCP Foundation was forced to step
in.

03:05:16.550 --> 03:05:22.760
When SCP-1176 was first uncovered, the body
had been stored inside a large stone sarcophagus,

03:05:22.760 --> 03:05:26.320
as was part of the ancient practice of creating
a mellified man.

03:05:26.320 --> 03:05:31.330
There was also a copper pipe and spigot, installed
by the Manna Charitable Foundation to extract

03:05:31.330 --> 03:05:32.939
the honey from within.

03:05:32.939 --> 03:05:38.040
The lid, sides and the inside of the sarcophagus
itself had a number of Egyptian hieroglyphics

03:05:38.040 --> 03:05:39.910
inscribed within.

03:05:39.910 --> 03:05:44.490
These were mostly spells and ceremonial texts,
written as a way to protect the individual

03:05:44.490 --> 03:05:47.040
that was to become the Mellified Man.

03:05:47.040 --> 03:05:51.130
There were also inscriptions written in a
dialect that was an early precursor to the

03:05:51.130 --> 03:05:56.120
Arabic language, however these sections had
been replaced with updated versions in Classical

03:05:56.120 --> 03:05:57.200
Arabic.

03:05:57.200 --> 03:06:02.580
One of these read:
“Abdallah ibn Salah ibn Ayyub ibn Nasir,

03:06:02.580 --> 03:06:07.080
fifteenth son of the great sheikh (illegible),
was put to the fast of honey on the first

03:06:07.080 --> 03:06:12.729
of Rajab in the year of the Hijra 3(illegible),
and died on the fifteenth of Ramadan.

03:06:12.729 --> 03:06:17.850
The great imam al-Yusuf has sealed him within
the ancient vessel, marked with the signs

03:06:17.850 --> 03:06:23.279
decreed by the ancients, to ferment in honey
for one hundred years and bring aid to the

03:06:23.279 --> 03:06:24.939
people in time of need.”

03:06:24.939 --> 03:06:29.920
Much like a headstone used to mark the grave
of someone who has passed, the sarcophagus

03:06:29.920 --> 03:06:36.670
that SCP-1176 was in featured a passage commemorating
a man who gave his life and body to heal others.

03:06:36.670 --> 03:06:38.640
Sounds nice, right?

03:06:38.640 --> 03:06:43.340
But there was another inscription, written
elsewhere on the stone sarcophagus, which

03:06:43.340 --> 03:06:47.790
translated to a dire warning:
“Beware, imam, for the mark of Iblis is

03:06:47.790 --> 03:06:49.500
upon this one!”

03:06:49.500 --> 03:06:55.190
According to the rest of the second inscription,
the tomb containing SCP-1176 had been opened

03:06:55.190 --> 03:06:56.190
before.

03:06:56.190 --> 03:07:02.319
During a time of great famine, imam Al-Malik
had ordered it to be opened so that the SCP-1176-1

03:07:02.319 --> 03:07:04.950
honey could be used to feed the starving people.

03:07:04.950 --> 03:07:09.760
Jars upon jars were filled with the anomalous
golden liquid and brought to the sheikh, the

03:07:09.760 --> 03:07:13.880
ruler of the land, as well as sent to the
people suffering from the lack of food.

03:07:13.880 --> 03:07:18.989
However, the very next day a number of these
people fell ill, stricken by a terrible fever

03:07:18.989 --> 03:07:21.689
that ultimately claimed their lives.

03:07:21.689 --> 03:07:26.910
Only the sheikh, his brothers and his sons,
who had all eaten the honey, survived.

03:07:26.910 --> 03:07:30.870
Any others who hadn’t been killed by the
fever accused the sheikh and his family of

03:07:30.870 --> 03:07:35.840
sorcery, and these surviving subjects attempted
to destroy the body that had produced this

03:07:35.840 --> 03:07:37.229
cursed nectar.

03:07:37.229 --> 03:07:41.751
But when the sheikh’s people found the Mellified
Man, they witnessed in horror as the body

03:07:41.751 --> 03:07:46.700
stood upright, dancing around as it screamed
and taunted the people.

03:07:46.700 --> 03:07:50.780
Al-Malik declared that the Devil himself sent
an evil spirit to corrupt SCP-1176.

03:07:50.780 --> 03:07:57.580
The honey confection was meant to be a means
of healing, but it had been corrupted.

03:07:57.580 --> 03:08:01.880
The sarcophagus was then sealed, and the inscription
on it finished with the following caution

03:08:01.880 --> 03:08:05.979
to any that found it:
“May God strike down any who would break

03:08:05.979 --> 03:08:07.649
these seals.”

03:08:07.649 --> 03:08:13.930
Countless centuries later, once the SCP Foundation
had recovered SCP-1176 and the sarcophagus

03:08:13.930 --> 03:08:17.960
containing it, they began testing with the
Mellified Man.

03:08:17.960 --> 03:08:23.510
Their goal was to determine how much of the
SCP-1176-1 honey the ancient corpse could

03:08:23.510 --> 03:08:27.840
produce, perhaps in the hopes of using this
substance as a form of hunger relieving field

03:08:27.840 --> 03:08:30.149
ration for their operatives.

03:08:30.149 --> 03:08:36.460
Removing the body from its sarcophagus, Foundation
researchers placed SCP-1176 on a metal grate,

03:08:36.460 --> 03:08:40.810
designed to drain the honey as it was produced
instead of allowing it to build up.

03:08:40.810 --> 03:08:45.250
Over the course of several hours, more and
more honey seemed to be produced, beginning

03:08:45.250 --> 03:08:50.130
at a rate of almost a liter per hour, to almost
56 liters every hour.

03:08:50.130 --> 03:08:55.670
But then, after ten and a half hours of producing
what seemed like an endless flow of honey,

03:08:55.670 --> 03:08:57.850
something unexpected happened.

03:08:57.850 --> 03:09:04.029
The deceased body of the Mellified Man, dead
for hundreds if not thousands of years, woke

03:09:04.029 --> 03:09:05.029
up.

03:09:05.029 --> 03:09:09.540
Foundation staff detected a spike in brain
activity, if you cast your mind back to earlier,

03:09:09.540 --> 03:09:15.040
you’ll remember that SCP-1176’s brain
had managed to survive and stay intact long

03:09:15.040 --> 03:09:16.830
after it should have decayed.

03:09:16.830 --> 03:09:21.960
The Mellified Man opened his eyes and immediately
started to wildly flail around.

03:09:21.960 --> 03:09:26.359
He made a number of distressed sounds, the
long dead body trying to crawl towards the

03:09:26.359 --> 03:09:28.430
outskirts of the testing chamber.

03:09:28.430 --> 03:09:34.040
Thanks to so many of its organs and muscles
having withered away over the years, SCP-1176

03:09:34.040 --> 03:09:37.220
was barely able to see or understand its surroundings.

03:09:37.220 --> 03:09:43.450
It couldn’t speak, not properly anyway,
given that its tongue had long since decayed.

03:09:43.450 --> 03:09:48.090
The Foundation’s personnel moved in to try
and restrain the ancient and now animated

03:09:48.090 --> 03:09:54.030
body, hoping to sedate it before SCP-1176
caused any lasting damage to itself.

03:09:54.030 --> 03:10:00.029
Eventually, staff were able to force SCP-1176
back into its sarcophagus, slamming the stone

03:10:00.029 --> 03:10:02.560
lid back in place and trapping it within.

03:10:02.560 --> 03:10:08.100
They could hear the once human creature screeching
and vocalizing from inside, bashing against

03:10:08.100 --> 03:10:11.930
the inside of the stone coffin with its head
and limbs.

03:10:11.930 --> 03:10:17.180
It took three whole hours of this for the
Mellified Man to return to its usual state,

03:10:17.180 --> 03:10:21.710
by which time its ancient bones were fractured
beyond repair.

03:10:21.710 --> 03:10:27.609
SCP-1176 is a sad tale of a man who had willingly
given his life to be a source of healing for

03:10:27.609 --> 03:10:28.840
people in need.

03:10:28.840 --> 03:10:33.900
He allowed himself to be mellified, turned
into a confection that could bring an end

03:10:33.900 --> 03:10:34.900
to famine.

03:10:34.900 --> 03:10:40.960
And yet, somehow, this was corrupted and turned
into something that spread fever and pestilence.

03:10:40.960 --> 03:10:46.540
For now, the Mellified Man sleeps, but his
brain is still alive inside.

03:10:46.540 --> 03:10:50.930
While he might be asleep, he may never be
able to rest.

03:10:50.930 --> 03:10:57.810
In 1961, the SCP Foundation discovered a town
that was completely devoid of all life.

03:10:57.810 --> 03:11:02.050
Not long before their arrival, Darrington,
North Carolina, had been a community with

03:11:02.050 --> 03:11:03.480
high aspirations.

03:11:03.480 --> 03:11:09.380
A deeply religious township of devout Christians,
many of whom were seeking greater prosperity

03:11:09.380 --> 03:11:10.380
from their lives.

03:11:10.380 --> 03:11:15.950
But now, their home was a ghost town, with
no sign of any prior Darrington resident to

03:11:15.950 --> 03:11:16.950
be found.

03:11:16.950 --> 03:11:19.250
Where the hell had they all gone?

03:11:19.250 --> 03:11:23.180
It hardly seemed likely that the population
of an entire town would all simultaneously

03:11:23.180 --> 03:11:26.270
decide to up sticks and leave to pastures
new.

03:11:26.270 --> 03:11:30.810
But then again, maybe the citizens of Darrington
hadn’t left at all.

03:11:30.810 --> 03:11:35.930
Perhaps they weren’t even really still human,
and had taken up residence somewhere much

03:11:35.930 --> 03:11:37.210
darker…

03:11:37.210 --> 03:11:38.950
like underground?

03:11:38.950 --> 03:11:44.030
This is the story of one of the earliest known
instances of a phenomena now known under the

03:11:44.030 --> 03:11:52.010
designation of SCP-3089, or to use its alternative
name: That Old Time Religion.

03:11:52.010 --> 03:11:57.380
When the SCP Foundation arrived in a desolate
Darrington to find the townsfolk had all vanished,

03:11:57.380 --> 03:12:03.130
they immediately began an investigation into
the exact ‘how’s and ‘why’s, the answers

03:12:03.130 --> 03:12:05.690
to what exactly had happened here.

03:12:05.690 --> 03:12:10.760
After all, while not a huge place, Darrington
was home to nearly a thousand residents, and

03:12:10.760 --> 03:12:13.380
that many people don’t just disappear.

03:12:13.380 --> 03:12:16.430
If they even had disappeared and weren’t
just… dormant.

03:12:16.430 --> 03:12:21.870
But what the Foundation uncovered was a gruesome
discovery, that led to them not only demolishing

03:12:21.870 --> 03:12:27.380
the entire North Carolinian town, but purchasing
all the land around it to keep the area under

03:12:27.380 --> 03:12:29.550
permanent observation.

03:12:29.550 --> 03:12:34.380
Prior to demolition, however, the Ministry
of Sevenfold Blessing had been one of the

03:12:34.380 --> 03:12:37.950
oldest buildings in Darrington, much like
most town churches.

03:12:37.950 --> 03:12:42.810
And it was while searching the offices of
this church that Foundation clean-up crews

03:12:42.810 --> 03:12:47.780
discovered their first piece of evidence,
the initial clue about what had happened to

03:12:47.780 --> 03:12:49.290
this deserted town.

03:12:49.290 --> 03:12:53.811
They recovered a series of cassette tapes,
each with a recording of sermons that had

03:12:53.811 --> 03:12:57.080
been given within the Ministry of Sevenfold
Blessing.

03:12:57.080 --> 03:13:02.100
These were all delivered by one Pastor Bartholomew
Jenner, the first having been recorded on

03:13:02.100 --> 03:13:05.939
August 17th of 1959, two years earlier.

03:13:05.939 --> 03:13:11.479
“My friends, I want to talk to you about
the Bible offers, tonight,” Pastor Jenner

03:13:11.479 --> 03:13:13.479
began in the first of these recordings.

03:13:13.479 --> 03:13:16.479
“I want to talk to you about what you are
owed.

03:13:16.479 --> 03:13:17.840
I want to talk to you about…

03:13:17.840 --> 03:13:21.750
I want to talk to those of you who are struggling,
right now.

03:13:21.750 --> 03:13:24.390
To those of you who have hardship and pain.

03:13:24.390 --> 03:13:29.270
Maybe you’ve heard that the Bible only nourishes
the spirit; that God provides only for our

03:13:29.270 --> 03:13:30.330
immortal souls.

03:13:30.330 --> 03:13:35.439
Well, my friends, I am here to tell you that
this is simply not true.”

03:13:35.439 --> 03:13:40.800
Pastor Bartholomew Jenner seemed to be focused
on the discussion of very real, relatable

03:13:40.800 --> 03:13:41.800
problems.

03:13:41.800 --> 03:13:46.290
After all, what person hasn’t felt unsatisfied
with their life at one point or another?

03:13:46.290 --> 03:13:49.490
And this was apparently no different for the
people of Darrington.

03:13:49.490 --> 03:13:53.720
“Many of you can think of places in your
lives where you have not yet risen.

03:13:53.720 --> 03:13:55.560
Where you are not yet victorious.

03:13:55.560 --> 03:13:56.560
Marriage.

03:13:56.560 --> 03:13:57.560
Finances.

03:13:57.560 --> 03:13:58.560
Health.

03:13:58.560 --> 03:14:00.529
But do not fret, my friends.

03:14:00.529 --> 03:14:02.050
God wants you to rise.

03:14:02.050 --> 03:14:04.370
He has cleared the path for you.

03:14:04.370 --> 03:14:08.729
It is one littered with His earthly treasures;
to claim them, you need only to shed your

03:14:08.729 --> 03:14:11.160
old selves and be reborn.”

03:14:11.160 --> 03:14:15.489
The pastor was merely using the shared faith
of the township to help reaffirm that their

03:14:15.489 --> 03:14:18.600
struggles were not the be all and end all
of their lives.

03:14:18.600 --> 03:14:21.649
Or at least, that’s how it first appeared.

03:14:21.649 --> 03:14:25.980
But the religious practices taking place in
this first recording would soon take a bizarre

03:14:25.980 --> 03:14:31.890
turn, making it clear there was something
far more sinister, even cult-like, going on

03:14:31.890 --> 03:14:34.271
in the Ministry of Sevenfold Blessing.

03:14:34.271 --> 03:14:36.070
“Now, if you would…

03:14:36.070 --> 03:14:39.939
some of the ladies from the mayor's office
were kind enough to collect these cicada shells.

03:14:39.939 --> 03:14:41.340
Pass them along.

03:14:41.340 --> 03:14:43.899
Each of you take one – yes, the children
too.

03:14:43.899 --> 03:14:44.920
Be careful.

03:14:44.920 --> 03:14:45.920
Very careful.

03:14:45.920 --> 03:14:47.270
They are fragile.

03:14:47.270 --> 03:14:49.820
Each of you, take one, and hold it in your
left hand.

03:14:49.820 --> 03:14:50.820
Yes.

03:14:50.820 --> 03:14:52.529
The left hand, not the right.

03:14:52.529 --> 03:14:53.529
Your left.”

03:14:53.529 --> 03:14:57.439
The shells of dead cicadas hardly seemed like
common fare for a sermon like this.

03:14:57.439 --> 03:15:02.250
Although, as the recording continued, it was
easy to understand that Pastor Jenner intended

03:15:02.250 --> 03:15:07.820
these discarded insect carapaces to be something
of a metaphor, even if they were pretty gross

03:15:07.820 --> 03:15:11.439
– especially to some of the younger members
of his congregation.

03:15:11.439 --> 03:15:16.170
He explained to the Darrington residents that
these cicada shells were meant to be symbolic

03:15:16.170 --> 03:15:20.750
of whatever hardship the citizens were currently
struggling with in their lives; whether it

03:15:20.750 --> 03:15:24.460
was work, a marriage, or an ill family member.

03:15:24.460 --> 03:15:29.050
Then came the next part of this unorthodox
practice; the pastor instructed everyone in

03:15:29.050 --> 03:15:33.729
the congregation to picture themselves holding
their biggest problem in their left hand…

03:15:33.729 --> 03:15:37.489
“Now, I want you to squeeze your left hand.

03:15:37.489 --> 03:15:38.939
Squeeze it into a fist.

03:15:38.939 --> 03:15:42.300
Feel that problem cracking; like old, dried
out paper.

03:15:42.300 --> 03:15:47.399
Feel it crumble to dust,” Jenner told them,
and the residents of Darrington did so, crushing

03:15:47.399 --> 03:15:49.640
their cicada shells until there was nothing
left.

03:15:49.640 --> 03:15:51.271
“Everyone, open your eyes.

03:15:51.271 --> 03:15:53.280
Don't you feel better?

03:15:53.280 --> 03:15:54.280
Stronger?

03:15:54.280 --> 03:15:56.069
This is what is offered.

03:15:56.069 --> 03:16:01.060
Our hardships are like the shell; we shall
cast them aside even as they crumble.

03:16:01.060 --> 03:16:03.440
God has cleared a path.”

03:16:03.440 --> 03:16:07.620
Needless to say, the Foundation agents that
recovered the tapes of Pastor Jenner’s odd

03:16:07.620 --> 03:16:10.220
sermons weren’t entirely sure what to make
of them.

03:16:10.220 --> 03:16:14.640
And as unusual as they were, the recordings
did little to indicate where the townspeople

03:16:14.640 --> 03:16:17.790
of Darrington, North Carolina, had disappeared
to.

03:16:17.790 --> 03:16:22.899
But as they listened further, what they found
was even more unsettling than an entire congregation

03:16:22.899 --> 03:16:25.420
of people crushing cicada shells.

03:16:25.420 --> 03:16:31.521
In the second recording, dated December 19th
of 1959, Pastor Jenner was once again presiding

03:16:31.521 --> 03:16:32.521
over his congregation.

03:16:32.521 --> 03:16:37.910
He had just finished quoting a passage from
Matthew, chapter twenty-five, verse thirty,

03:16:37.910 --> 03:16:42.020
which related to a Biblical tale known as
the Parable of the Talents.

03:16:42.020 --> 03:16:47.080
In this story, a master puts his servants
in charge of a differently sized portion of

03:16:47.080 --> 03:16:50.980
his wealth while he is away, then judges them
based on whether or not his servants make

03:16:50.980 --> 03:16:52.810
a profit using his money.

03:16:52.810 --> 03:16:57.170
The third servant, who had received the least
talents – meaning an amount of money – was

03:16:57.170 --> 03:17:02.560
punished for burying his share in the ground;
“cast into the outer darkness” to face

03:17:02.560 --> 03:17:04.819
“weeping and gnashing of teeth.”

03:17:04.819 --> 03:17:10.080
It was after making mention of this unprofitable
servant that Pastor Jenner went on to address

03:17:10.080 --> 03:17:16.200
even more of the bizarre, almost ritualistic,
practices he had been introducing to his sermons.

03:17:16.200 --> 03:17:20.370
“Now, some of you have expressed concerns
over the new sacraments.

03:17:20.370 --> 03:17:22.460
A few have even called them sacrilege.

03:17:22.460 --> 03:17:25.590
And yet, have we not prospered?

03:17:25.590 --> 03:17:31.380
Have these same nay-sayers, these same ‘Doubting
Thomases’ not profited from our good works?”

03:17:31.380 --> 03:17:32.380
the pastor declared.

03:17:32.380 --> 03:17:37.500
“I have shown you how to heal the sick with
the Lord’s Prayer and the blood of an unbaptized

03:17:37.500 --> 03:17:38.500
child.

03:17:38.500 --> 03:17:42.979
I have shown you how to see your future in
the steaming entrails of a quivering crow.

03:17:42.979 --> 03:17:45.830
I have shown you the path to glory.

03:17:45.830 --> 03:17:47.970
But I cannot make you follow this path.

03:17:47.970 --> 03:17:53.300
I can only show it to you; it is you and you
alone who must follow it – who must rise

03:17:53.300 --> 03:17:55.561
and shed your old self.”

03:17:55.561 --> 03:17:58.109
Shed your old self.

03:17:58.109 --> 03:18:02.600
The words immediately called to mind the image
of the cicadas, insects that discard their

03:18:02.600 --> 03:18:05.680
outer carapaces and emerge anew.

03:18:05.680 --> 03:18:10.300
Bugs that also burrow into the ground and
wait, lying dormant under the earth for years

03:18:10.300 --> 03:18:11.500
at a time.

03:18:11.500 --> 03:18:16.140
All before they emerge, rising up again…
so they can spread.

03:18:16.140 --> 03:18:20.380
It was becoming clear that Pastor Jenner was
certainly deviating further and further from

03:18:20.380 --> 03:18:22.979
the church’s normal religious practices.

03:18:22.979 --> 03:18:27.720
His bold and blatant descriptions of what
sounded like ritualistic sacrifices were shocking

03:18:27.720 --> 03:18:32.800
enough to hear; speaking of using blood and
entrails to bring the town the prosperity

03:18:32.800 --> 03:18:33.800
it sought.

03:18:33.800 --> 03:18:38.170
But if that wasn’t bad enough, the worst
was still yet to come… contained within

03:18:38.170 --> 03:18:40.279
the third and final recording.

03:18:40.279 --> 03:18:45.830
Unlike the previous cassettes, most of the
sermon from June 7th 1960 was almost completely

03:18:45.830 --> 03:18:47.311
unintelligible.

03:18:47.311 --> 03:18:51.550
And without any visual evidence to go with
it, it was hard for the Foundation to make

03:18:51.550 --> 03:18:53.910
out exactly what was going on.

03:18:53.910 --> 03:18:58.811
It began with another quote from Matthew,
this time chapter twenty-eight, verse six;

03:18:58.811 --> 03:19:03.060
which made mention of the resurrection of
Jesus, that he had risen, and that people

03:19:03.060 --> 03:19:05.380
should come and see where the Lord lay.

03:19:05.380 --> 03:19:10.260
“Not a metaphor, my friends,” Pastor Jenner
explained, before urging his congregation

03:19:10.260 --> 03:19:12.600
to join in some kind of formation.

03:19:12.600 --> 03:19:13.670
“Step forward.

03:19:13.670 --> 03:19:16.570
Mothers behind their daughters, fathers behind
their sons.

03:19:16.570 --> 03:19:17.570
Turn to face the…”

03:19:17.570 --> 03:19:22.460
The recording became unintelligible again
after that point, with only a few more words

03:19:22.460 --> 03:19:23.460
being audible.

03:19:23.460 --> 03:19:28.120
The pastor seemed to have gathered the townsfolk
of Darrington, presumably for some new form

03:19:28.120 --> 03:19:29.120
of ritual.

03:19:29.120 --> 03:19:33.280
He encouraged the town’s children to close
their eyes and pray, before reminding the

03:19:33.280 --> 03:19:38.400
congregation that God sacrificed the life
of his only son, Jesus.

03:19:38.400 --> 03:19:42.380
Frighteningly, it appeared that Pastor Jenner
was implying the adults of Darrington should

03:19:42.380 --> 03:19:43.770
do the same.

03:19:43.770 --> 03:19:46.680
One of the next fragments of his sermon that
could be deciphered declared:

03:19:46.680 --> 03:19:49.149
“…lamb is slaughtered to feed the lion.

03:19:49.149 --> 03:19:51.479
The Son is slaughtered to feed…”

03:19:51.479 --> 03:19:55.250
Between more and more noise interfering with
the recording, Pastor Jenner could be heard

03:19:55.250 --> 03:19:58.330
saying:
“The pact is complete.

03:19:58.330 --> 03:20:01.850
This world shall be our paradise.”

03:20:01.850 --> 03:20:07.710
Before encouraging his congregation – or
those who were left – to dig deep and wait.

03:20:07.710 --> 03:20:10.510
Then came perhaps the most horrific part of
the tape.

03:20:10.510 --> 03:20:14.790
The remainder of the recording lasted thirty
minutes, comprised of pure static.

03:20:14.790 --> 03:20:19.160
Or, the Foundation agents listening to it
assumed, at first, that it was just interference.

03:20:19.160 --> 03:20:23.640
But further audio analysis seemed to suggest
that the long, continuous mass of hissing

03:20:23.640 --> 03:20:28.180
wasn’t static at all; it was the chittering
sound of insects…

03:20:28.180 --> 03:20:31.070
like the noise made by cicadas.

03:20:31.070 --> 03:20:34.040
For a time, the incident at Darrington left
the Foundation baffled.

03:20:34.040 --> 03:20:37.590
There seemed to be no clear answer as to what
had happened.

03:20:37.590 --> 03:20:42.290
Not one of the town’s residents was anywhere
to be found, and on top of that, there were

03:20:42.290 --> 03:20:43.290
no bodies.

03:20:43.290 --> 03:20:48.470
No remains of any kind to speak of; if they
were dead, there would at least be some kind

03:20:48.470 --> 03:20:49.660
of trace.

03:20:49.660 --> 03:20:54.319
And then there were all the questions raised
by Pastor Bartholomew Jenner’s strange sermons;

03:20:54.319 --> 03:20:57.540
why did he seem so focused on enacting rituals?

03:20:57.540 --> 03:21:00.210
Did any of his methods really benefit the
town?

03:21:00.210 --> 03:21:05.760
And why did he place so much emphasis on…
cicadas, of all things?

03:21:05.760 --> 03:21:10.450
Answers were few and far between, although
almost six decades after the Foundation discovered

03:21:10.450 --> 03:21:15.220
the desolate town of Darrington, a new development
would come to light…

03:21:15.220 --> 03:21:18.470
To be more accurate, it was fifty-six years
later.

03:21:18.470 --> 03:21:24.460
On the 11th January 2017, a Foundation agent
named Daniel Mitchell was patrolling the area

03:21:24.460 --> 03:21:29.140
that had formerly been Darrington, North Carolina
– before the Foundation had demolished all

03:21:29.140 --> 03:21:30.560
traces of the town.

03:21:30.560 --> 03:21:35.180
By this point, the SCP Foundation had long
thought that they had figured out exactly

03:21:35.180 --> 03:21:40.560
what SCP-3089 was; they had even encountered
it emerging in a number of different forms

03:21:40.560 --> 03:21:43.150
in both 2007 and 2015.

03:21:43.150 --> 03:21:48.550
However, it was what Daniel Mitchell happened
across during the routine monthly patrol that

03:21:48.550 --> 03:21:51.130
revealed the horrifying truth.

03:21:51.130 --> 03:21:55.760
At the outskirts of the area where the town
had once been, a series of sinkholes had opened

03:21:55.760 --> 03:22:00.689
up, at some point between the previous monthly
check and this one in early 2017.

03:22:00.689 --> 03:22:05.080
And if you think that these sinkholes caused
a disturbance in the earth and uncovered all

03:22:05.080 --> 03:22:09.150
the bodies of the former residents or Darrington,
you’d be wrong.

03:22:09.150 --> 03:22:11.810
It was far, far stranger…

03:22:11.810 --> 03:22:16.489
The Foundation conducted a full-scale examination
of the sinkholes around the demolished North

03:22:16.489 --> 03:22:17.840
Carolinian town.

03:22:17.840 --> 03:22:21.780
And these weren’t just a few patches of
loose ground that had sunk through.

03:22:21.780 --> 03:22:25.949
The geological survey the Foundation carried
out quickly revealed that these sinkholes

03:22:25.949 --> 03:22:29.070
led to an extensive network of tunnels deep
underground.

03:22:29.070 --> 03:22:33.779
They extended several hundred kilometers outwards,
practically covering the entire underside

03:22:33.779 --> 03:22:35.771
of where Darrington had been.

03:22:35.771 --> 03:22:41.090
The tunnels seemed far too big than any other
created by any natural means, but the entire

03:22:41.090 --> 03:22:46.779
network also appeared too rudimentary, too
imperfect to have been carved using any modern

03:22:46.779 --> 03:22:49.370
excavation technology like a large drill.

03:22:49.370 --> 03:22:54.350
Plus, if equipment like that had been on site,
the Foundation would have noticed, as they

03:22:54.350 --> 03:22:55.800
kept the area monitored.

03:22:55.800 --> 03:23:00.330
It was almost like something had been burrowing
through the ground, only to eventually crawl

03:23:00.330 --> 03:23:03.640
back up to the surface, resulting in the sinkholes.

03:23:03.640 --> 03:23:08.090
What’s more, the Foundation’s geological
tests suggested that the network of tunnels

03:23:08.090 --> 03:23:10.220
was almost four whole decades old.

03:23:10.220 --> 03:23:15.090
That would have placed the date of their creation
about ten years after the disappearances of

03:23:15.090 --> 03:23:16.760
everyone in Darrington.

03:23:16.760 --> 03:23:21.920
Naturally, the Foundation immediately launched
a mission to explore more of the tunnels.

03:23:21.920 --> 03:23:26.100
Before even completing a full sweep of the
underground space in its entirety, they had

03:23:26.100 --> 03:23:28.680
made another discovery.

03:23:28.680 --> 03:23:33.620
Contained within the tunnels was over a whole
ton of organic material that had been mostly

03:23:33.620 --> 03:23:36.660
preserved without decomposing too much.

03:23:36.660 --> 03:23:40.920
The SCP Foundation began gathering samples
for testing, finding most of this material

03:23:40.920 --> 03:23:43.540
to be severely desiccated dermis tissue.

03:23:43.540 --> 03:23:49.439
That’s the dense layer of skin beneath the
epidermis, and it had all been entirely dried

03:23:49.439 --> 03:23:50.439
out.

03:23:50.439 --> 03:23:53.180
But that wasn’t all the testing uncovered.

03:23:53.180 --> 03:23:57.620
According to genetic analysis, the tissue
had two distinct types of DNA present.

03:23:57.620 --> 03:24:02.750
The first being easily identified as human
genetic material, which made sense.

03:24:02.750 --> 03:24:06.430
Despite the material lacking in moisture,
the dermis tissue didn’t match the skin

03:24:06.430 --> 03:24:07.970
of any other mammal.

03:24:07.970 --> 03:24:10.689
But then there was the other DNA present.

03:24:10.689 --> 03:24:15.390
Combined with the expected human DNA was the
presence of something else that the Foundation

03:24:15.390 --> 03:24:18.870
researchers had quite some difficulty finding
a match for.

03:24:18.870 --> 03:24:24.300
Eventually, they determined that this genetic
material entangled with human DNA belonged

03:24:24.300 --> 03:24:30.069
to the Cicadtta montana… better known as
the New Forest cicada.

03:24:30.069 --> 03:24:31.850
Cicadas again.

03:24:31.850 --> 03:24:37.560
Cicada DNA mixed with human DNA, discovered
in a large network of underground tunnels.

03:24:37.560 --> 03:24:42.160
All beneath the same town where a pastor had
his congregation crush cicada shells in their

03:24:42.160 --> 03:24:45.180
left hands during one of his sermons.

03:24:45.180 --> 03:24:49.720
Ten years before the sinkhole incident, the
Foundation was alerted to a particular YouTube

03:24:49.720 --> 03:24:53.620
channel by the name of ‘Kai Sanchez: Positively
Rich’.

03:24:53.620 --> 03:24:58.000
On the surface, Kai was one of many online
grifters, preaching about how easy it was

03:24:58.000 --> 03:25:03.000
to quickly achieve an obscene amount of wealth
by simply believing in yourself.

03:25:03.000 --> 03:25:07.859
Usually, if not always, these types of people
were trying to scam their audience of loyal

03:25:07.859 --> 03:25:13.240
subscribers into investing in some kind of
illicit moneymaking scheme or any number of

03:25:13.240 --> 03:25:17.650
other cons; promising their followers easy
money that never came.

03:25:17.650 --> 03:25:20.300
But Kai Sanchez’s channel was slightly different.

03:25:20.300 --> 03:25:24.760
So much so that the Foundation had to contain
his entire audience, deeming them to have

03:25:24.760 --> 03:25:28.000
been affected by SCP-3089.

03:25:28.000 --> 03:25:33.880
The video that caught the Foundation’s attention
was an hour-long upload from Kai titled ‘Seven

03:25:33.880 --> 03:25:35.960
Secrets to Ascend the Ladder of Prosperity’.

03:25:35.960 --> 03:25:42.000
There was that word again – prosperity – the
same thing Pastor Jenner had promised his

03:25:42.000 --> 03:25:44.141
congregation in Darrington.

03:25:44.141 --> 03:25:46.529
And the similarities didn’t end there.

03:25:46.529 --> 03:25:51.770
In his video, much like the pastor during
his sermons, Kai Sanchez encouraged his audience

03:25:51.770 --> 03:25:54.729
to visualize their success in order to achieve
it.

03:25:54.729 --> 03:25:59.210
He implied that the human consciousness could
impact reality; for example, if his viewers

03:25:59.210 --> 03:26:04.040
just imagined themselves having a bigger bank
account or looking more attractive, then these

03:26:04.040 --> 03:26:07.370
things would manifest themselves in the real
world.

03:26:07.370 --> 03:26:12.540
One of Kai’s ‘Secrets to Ascend the Ladder
of Prosperity’ was as follows: “Visualize

03:26:12.540 --> 03:26:13.540
your ascendance.

03:26:13.540 --> 03:26:17.330
Re-imagine yourself as someone who can reach
the top of that ladder.

03:26:17.330 --> 03:26:18.739
Shed your old identity.

03:26:18.739 --> 03:26:20.979
Tear it off and throw it aside – like dead
skin.

03:26:20.979 --> 03:26:22.199
You won't need it.

03:26:22.199 --> 03:26:23.380
Not where you're going.”

03:26:23.380 --> 03:26:26.570
The resemblance to Pastor Jenner’s sermons
was uncanny.

03:26:26.570 --> 03:26:31.790
Kai’s video even encouraged that his audience
leave scraps out to lure stray cats into their

03:26:31.790 --> 03:26:37.180
homes, and then, once they had one, to take
a knife and… well, you remember what happened

03:26:37.180 --> 03:26:38.180
in Darrington.

03:26:38.180 --> 03:26:43.810
But Kai Sanchez made sure to specify: “Remember
to hold the knife with your left hand…”

03:26:43.810 --> 03:26:47.500
Another online community was tagged by the
Foundation for similar teachings.

03:26:47.500 --> 03:26:51.970
This group of insular men were trying to apply
the same methodology primarily to attract

03:26:51.970 --> 03:26:52.970
women.

03:26:52.970 --> 03:26:56.740
However, they also reasoned it could be used
to improve their own financial status and

03:26:56.740 --> 03:27:01.899
physical stature; all done through visualizing
and believing that doing so would make these

03:27:01.899 --> 03:27:03.550
things improve.

03:27:03.550 --> 03:27:06.480
That having faith would grant them prosperity.

03:27:06.480 --> 03:27:11.330
This disturbed community even tried to use
bug-rattlers to emit frequencies to aid in

03:27:11.330 --> 03:27:12.979
attracting women.

03:27:12.979 --> 03:27:17.290
Contained within these rattlers were the preserved
remains of… cicadas.

03:27:17.290 --> 03:27:22.550
Male cicadas have tymbals, structures on their
outer shell that emit a loud hissing, chittering

03:27:22.550 --> 03:27:28.500
noise that they often use to find a mate,
after spending so much time dormant underground…

03:27:28.500 --> 03:27:30.390
before burrowing up to the surface.

03:27:30.390 --> 03:27:35.229
And if you’ve been paying attention, you
might be able to guess exactly where this

03:27:35.229 --> 03:27:36.771
is going…

03:27:36.771 --> 03:27:41.920
SCP-3089 is a phenomenon that occurs within
communities of people who are seeking some

03:27:41.920 --> 03:27:43.780
form of prosperity.

03:27:43.780 --> 03:27:48.330
Whether that community be a town, a group
of like-minded people online, or any other

03:27:48.330 --> 03:27:50.100
group of collected individuals.

03:27:50.100 --> 03:27:55.170
The particular type of prosperity these people
are all seeking can be anything; from spiritual

03:27:55.170 --> 03:27:58.080
enlightenment, to financial success.

03:27:58.080 --> 03:28:04.729
The SCP Foundation doesn’t yet quite understand
exactly how SCP-3089 starts, only that communities

03:28:04.729 --> 03:28:09.560
affected by it will attempt to achieve their
chosen material success through the application

03:28:09.560 --> 03:28:16.130
of rituals, like visualizing what they hope
to overcome and achieve, and practicing sacrifices.

03:28:16.130 --> 03:28:21.090
In short, these people have to believe these
acts will grant them what they want.

03:28:21.090 --> 03:28:25.430
They need to be willing to go far enough to
do unspeakable things.

03:28:25.430 --> 03:28:28.060
They need to have faith.

03:28:28.060 --> 03:28:33.400
Although what they don’t realize is, some
things can feed on that faith, they can harvest

03:28:33.400 --> 03:28:34.400
it…

03:28:34.400 --> 03:28:38.359
Before these communities realize the terrible
things that they have done – or who exactly

03:28:38.359 --> 03:28:42.689
has tricked them into performing these rituals
– they’ll begin to undergo a horrific

03:28:42.689 --> 03:28:50.449
transformation process; known as SCP-3089-B.
It begins in the chrysalis stage.

03:28:50.449 --> 03:28:55.109
Members of a community that has been affected
by SCP-3089 will experience a declined state

03:28:55.109 --> 03:28:56.189
of metabolism.

03:28:56.189 --> 03:29:02.520
Now classified as instances of SCP-3089-A,
their brain activity, heart rate, and body

03:29:02.520 --> 03:29:04.960
temperature will all begin to lower.

03:29:04.960 --> 03:29:09.390
Over a period of between three and six hours,
these people will then suffer a change to

03:29:09.390 --> 03:29:12.430
their epidermis – the outer layer of skin.

03:29:12.430 --> 03:29:16.660
It starts to harden, until it has formed a
dense, brittle substance…

03:29:16.660 --> 03:29:17.660
like a shell.

03:29:17.660 --> 03:29:22.649
Next comes the second stage of SCP-3089-B:
metamorphosis.

03:29:22.649 --> 03:29:29.580
Internally, SCP-3089-A individuals will develop
a number of teratomas – a type of germ cell

03:29:29.580 --> 03:29:35.199
tumor that can contain several different types
of tissue, such as hair, muscle, and bone.

03:29:35.199 --> 03:29:39.640
During the next two or three weeks, these
tumors will expand and dissolve the person’s

03:29:39.640 --> 03:29:41.060
soft tissue.

03:29:41.060 --> 03:29:43.710
Then there’s the final stage: emergence.

03:29:43.710 --> 03:29:50.640
An instance of SCP-3089-A will exit its dormant
state that began in the initial stage.

03:29:50.640 --> 03:29:56.149
Once they have awoken, then… something exits
the outer epidermal shell.

03:29:56.149 --> 03:29:58.109
It will not communicate.

03:29:58.109 --> 03:30:02.690
Some will retain remnants of internal organs
– such as eyes or lungs – however, these

03:30:02.690 --> 03:30:05.939
are vestigial, no longer serving any purpose.

03:30:05.939 --> 03:30:09.600
The brain functions deviate from any normal
human patterns.

03:30:09.600 --> 03:30:14.859
Having completed the process, this… thing
will attempt to burrow down into the soil

03:30:14.859 --> 03:30:17.060
via any means at its disposal.

03:30:17.060 --> 03:30:18.890
An outer shell.

03:30:18.890 --> 03:30:20.739
Digging into the soil.

03:30:20.739 --> 03:30:22.290
The tunnels underneath Darrington.

03:30:22.290 --> 03:30:24.810
The genetic material uncovered below.

03:30:24.810 --> 03:30:27.840
Dermis tissue with two types of DNA.

03:30:27.840 --> 03:30:30.660
A mix of human … and cicada.

03:30:30.660 --> 03:30:32.680
There is something out there.

03:30:32.680 --> 03:30:36.830
It is preying on people’s faith, their longing
for prosperity.

03:30:36.830 --> 03:30:41.239
Then, when these communities are presented
with someone who can take advantage of that

03:30:41.239 --> 03:30:47.310
faith – like Pastor Jenner or Kai Sanchez
– they find themselves encouraged to push

03:30:47.310 --> 03:30:49.560
their faith to its furthest limit.

03:30:49.560 --> 03:30:54.120
And then, they’re rewarded by becoming something
else…

03:30:54.120 --> 03:30:55.900
something nightmarish.

03:30:55.900 --> 03:31:00.520
The question is: when they wake up, and crawl
back out from their tunnels, leaving a sinkhole

03:31:00.520 --> 03:31:05.029
in their wake… where do these cicada creatures
go?

03:31:05.029 --> 03:31:09.970
The anomalous religions that the SCP Foundation
has cataloged and studied over the years are

03:31:09.970 --> 03:31:15.880
many in number and bottomless in depth, with
specialized para-theological researchers limiting

03:31:15.880 --> 03:31:21.540
themselves to just one or maybe two faiths,
diving fully into a religion of their choice

03:31:21.540 --> 03:31:24.010
and mastering its forbidden knowledge.

03:31:24.010 --> 03:31:28.760
But the Foundation is careful to make sure
that those researching these faiths don’t

03:31:28.760 --> 03:31:33.520
succumb to their beliefs, as many anomalous
religions are dangerous to the organization

03:31:33.520 --> 03:31:39.180
in practice, involving tasks such as making
blood pacts with ancient gods, or modifying

03:31:39.180 --> 03:31:41.390
one’s body to better suit a divine purpose.

03:31:41.390 --> 03:31:46.601
There’s some seriously nasty stuff involved
in the immaterial world, almost to the point

03:31:46.601 --> 03:31:50.979
where it makes you wonder why anyone would
be suckered into joining up with what appears

03:31:50.979 --> 03:31:55.000
to be from the outside, just another cult
of crazies.

03:31:55.000 --> 03:31:57.090
But let’s not generalize.

03:31:57.090 --> 03:32:02.150
Religions, even those that are non-anomalous,
are all strange from the outside, even if

03:32:02.150 --> 03:32:04.319
one may seem natural to you.

03:32:04.319 --> 03:32:09.470
But one anomalous religion stands out from
all the rest as having more active followers,

03:32:09.470 --> 03:32:14.870
more history, and more documented culture
than any other, and that is Sarkicism.

03:32:14.870 --> 03:32:20.149
Hold on to your flesh, because today on SCP
Explained, we’re going to be answering the

03:32:20.149 --> 03:32:26.310
question “What is Sarkicism?”, and hopefully
don’t get distracted and ritually sacrifice

03:32:26.310 --> 03:32:30.580
you, the viewer, in the name of the Grand
Karcist Ion along the way.

03:32:30.580 --> 03:32:33.590
Let’s get to it, meatbags.

03:32:33.590 --> 03:32:37.680
Before we begin, it’s important to note
that Sarkicism is an incredibly dense and

03:32:37.680 --> 03:32:42.050
deep religion, and that covering every last
detail of it in a short period of time would

03:32:42.050 --> 03:32:47.970
be a herculean, nigh-impossible task for even
the most well-read Sarkic lore-masters.

03:32:47.970 --> 03:32:49.930
So where would you even start?

03:32:49.930 --> 03:32:51.819
What is Sarkicism?

03:32:51.819 --> 03:32:55.540
To best understand that, we’re going to
bring you back all the way to the beginning

03:32:55.540 --> 03:33:01.090
of human history, to the ancient world of
the Eurasian continent, where sprawling empires

03:33:01.090 --> 03:33:05.109
ruled and war between them was an all-too-common
occurrence.

03:33:05.109 --> 03:33:09.620
In what is now south-central Siberia, the
Daevite Empire ruled with an iron fist.

03:33:09.620 --> 03:33:16.120
The Daeva were a warrior culture, with militarism,
conquest, gruesome human sacrifice, and thaumaturgic,

03:33:16.120 --> 03:33:21.090
magic rituals being universally consistent
in their culture, according to the few historical

03:33:21.090 --> 03:33:24.080
accounts available that make mention of the
empire.

03:33:24.080 --> 03:33:29.670
The Daevites practiced anomalous magic, arcane
rituals, and sacrifices that bolstered their

03:33:29.670 --> 03:33:33.449
power, longevity, and standing within their
society.

03:33:33.449 --> 03:33:38.440
The empire was ruled by a theocratic aristocracy
called the daeva, those who were especially

03:33:38.440 --> 03:33:43.670
attuned to the anomalous world, who practiced
cannibalism and thaumaturgy, and whose bodies

03:33:43.670 --> 03:33:48.550
were so warped and modified by decades of
magic alteration that Foundation historians

03:33:48.550 --> 03:33:53.380
would come to the conclusion that the Daeva
were so divergent from modern humans that

03:33:53.380 --> 03:33:57.290
they could be considered a separate species
altogether.

03:33:57.290 --> 03:34:00.760
But how the Daeva relate to Sarkicism remains
the question.

03:34:00.760 --> 03:34:04.390
And the answer is found in the Empire’s
slave-owning culture.

03:34:04.390 --> 03:34:07.520
The Daevites owned many, many slaves.

03:34:07.520 --> 03:34:12.449
People they had bought or taken from their
lands as a sign of pure Daevite power in the

03:34:12.449 --> 03:34:14.899
form of ownership over another human being.

03:34:14.899 --> 03:34:20.341
Daevite city states had massive, sprawling
slave populations, and among those, was a

03:34:20.341 --> 03:34:22.859
young boy by the name of Ion.

03:34:22.859 --> 03:34:27.939
Ion’s appearance would be depicted over
the years by Sarkic art and culture as inconclusive

03:34:27.939 --> 03:34:32.560
and varied, whether it was their gender, or
even the question of whether or not Ion resembled

03:34:32.560 --> 03:34:37.840
a human, the cult of personality that would
crop up around Ion would be a testament to

03:34:37.840 --> 03:34:42.649
Sarkicism’s eventual widespread culture,
but it was here, in ancient western Siberia,

03:34:42.649 --> 03:34:46.120
where those seeds of Sarkicism originated.

03:34:46.120 --> 03:34:51.790
According to the most prominent Sarkic texts,
Ion was a slave, like many others in the Daevite

03:34:51.790 --> 03:34:52.790
empire.

03:34:52.790 --> 03:34:57.790
Born into slavery by a Daevite mother and
a concubine father, the circumstances of Ion’s

03:34:57.790 --> 03:35:01.110
birth indicate that he was destined to be
a slave from the onset.

03:35:01.110 --> 03:35:03.170
But there was something remarkable about them.

03:35:03.170 --> 03:35:07.540
Ion, in the eyes of his masters, was different
from other slaves.

03:35:07.540 --> 03:35:12.470
He was intelligent, and so much so that the
decision was made for Ion to serve under a

03:35:12.470 --> 03:35:16.840
Daevite priestess, where he could hone his
skills to serve the empire in ways unlike

03:35:16.840 --> 03:35:22.580
the other slaves, who toiled away constructing
massive public works or died in foreign lands

03:35:22.580 --> 03:35:24.109
on the field of battle.

03:35:24.109 --> 03:35:29.050
Ion did not understand what differentiated
him from others, and why he deserved such

03:35:29.050 --> 03:35:33.450
special treatment, but it was the realization
that the only thing separating him from his

03:35:33.450 --> 03:35:39.240
masters was the possession of power that would
serve as the basis for Sarkicisms founding

03:35:39.240 --> 03:35:40.240
doctrines.

03:35:40.240 --> 03:35:45.450
Ion watched in horror as those they knew succumbed
to the backbreaking work that the empire forced

03:35:45.450 --> 03:35:51.100
upon its slaves, and how prevalent death and
destruction were among its people.

03:35:51.100 --> 03:35:56.340
Inside Ion grew a great rage for the Daevites,
who flaunted their power over others in the

03:35:56.340 --> 03:35:57.500
form of slavery.

03:35:57.500 --> 03:36:02.580
He wished to transcend the physical limitations
that kept him and his fellow slaves in bondage

03:36:02.580 --> 03:36:04.920
and service to the Daevites.

03:36:04.920 --> 03:36:10.210
Ion knew that their masters practiced thaumaturgy,
a form of magic that granted great power to

03:36:10.210 --> 03:36:16.279
its users, and in a brutal world where power
is what defines who is master and who is slave,

03:36:16.279 --> 03:36:20.990
the prospects of achieving it became more
important to Ion than anything else.

03:36:20.990 --> 03:36:25.970
If he could harness such power for himself,
Ion could break free from the chains of slavery

03:36:25.970 --> 03:36:29.229
that kept him subservient to those Daevite
masters.

03:36:29.229 --> 03:36:34.590
He would achieve apotheosis, the belief that
an individual could ascend to godhood through

03:36:34.590 --> 03:36:36.930
raw power and unbridled will.

03:36:36.930 --> 03:36:42.260
Over time, Ion's hatred of the so-called “living
gods” of the Daeva grew so strong that he

03:36:42.260 --> 03:36:44.319
actively began plotting their downfall.

03:36:44.319 --> 03:36:49.949
Around 1800 BCE, Ion’s influence among the
lowest ranks of the empire was inescapable.

03:36:49.949 --> 03:36:56.400
He was charismatic, he was a slave, he was
powerful, and he spoke of violence.

03:36:56.400 --> 03:37:01.609
Of seizing Daevite magic for himself and using
it to elevate himself into power.

03:37:01.609 --> 03:37:06.640
Ion’s tenets and beliefs appealed to the
slave population, who also grew hungry for

03:37:06.640 --> 03:37:07.640
freedom.

03:37:07.640 --> 03:37:12.180
Ion’s creed spread like wildfire, and would
form the basis for all Sarkic belief in the

03:37:12.180 --> 03:37:13.270
centuries that came.

03:37:13.270 --> 03:37:18.319
First, there was apotheosis, which Ion was
striving to achieve, and the path to doing

03:37:18.319 --> 03:37:20.370
so was the will to power.

03:37:20.370 --> 03:37:23.229
The next belief covered that concept in depth.

03:37:23.229 --> 03:37:28.270
Ion believed that the will to power was the
primary driving force of man, as an individual

03:37:28.270 --> 03:37:34.239
seeks to master all things within its domain,
they exert that power onto others, and others

03:37:34.239 --> 03:37:37.310
have the ability to exert it back in opposition.

03:37:37.310 --> 03:37:42.840
Desire is the measure of power, and those
with a stronger will always triumph over the

03:37:42.840 --> 03:37:43.840
weak.

03:37:43.840 --> 03:37:48.160
The next belief was the act of Theophagy,
a hypothetical tenant that Ion was toying

03:37:48.160 --> 03:37:51.300
with after observing the Daevite religion
for years.

03:37:51.300 --> 03:37:56.340
Theophagy referred to the act of sacrificial
consumption of a god, and upon eating them

03:37:56.340 --> 03:38:01.410
achieving thaumaturgical, reality-bending,
and all-powerful abilities.

03:38:01.410 --> 03:38:06.510
There were many gods in the universe, and
this Ion knew, but none of them were fit for

03:38:06.510 --> 03:38:07.720
him to worship.

03:38:07.720 --> 03:38:10.300
Instead, he would crave their power.

03:38:10.300 --> 03:38:15.960
As a metaphorical example of theophagy, Ion
wanted nothing more than to consume the Daevite

03:38:15.960 --> 03:38:19.029
empire whole, taking its power for his own.

03:38:19.029 --> 03:38:21.399
Next, there was the idea of sacrifice.

03:38:21.399 --> 03:38:26.640
Whether it was for the sacrifice of the self
for the benefit of many, or sacrifice of many

03:38:26.640 --> 03:38:32.399
for the benefit of the individual, Ion believed,
much like his masters, that ritual sacrifice

03:38:32.399 --> 03:38:37.380
was a powerful tool that could be used as
a means to achieve an end.

03:38:37.380 --> 03:38:41.380
Those who commanded the sacrifice were showing
their power, bringing them that much closer

03:38:41.380 --> 03:38:43.199
to apotheosis.

03:38:43.199 --> 03:38:47.420
Those who were sacrificed were experiencing
strife, which would only make them stronger

03:38:47.420 --> 03:38:48.840
than before.

03:38:48.840 --> 03:38:51.720
Muscles suffer damage, but eventually heal.

03:38:51.720 --> 03:38:55.620
The mind develops toleration against hardship,
such as slavery.

03:38:55.620 --> 03:39:00.529
This cycle of destruction and regeneration
in strife was, according to Ion, one of the

03:39:00.529 --> 03:39:02.840
greatest tutors in the natural world.

03:39:02.840 --> 03:39:07.030
Ion’s final core belief would become the
most prominent, outward facing indicator of

03:39:07.030 --> 03:39:11.030
Sarkicism, and that was the idea of “shepherding
the flesh”.

03:39:11.030 --> 03:39:15.819
Ion believed that all living things descended
from a single progenitor, an all-powerful

03:39:15.819 --> 03:39:20.939
god known as Yaldabaoth, who the Sarkics would
later regard as the principal power in the

03:39:20.939 --> 03:39:21.939
universe.

03:39:21.939 --> 03:39:26.640
Yaldabaoth’s relationship with Sarkicism
is tenuous at best, with modern Sarkic cults

03:39:26.640 --> 03:39:29.350
either admiring or fearing the enemy.

03:39:29.350 --> 03:39:34.120
One thing is certain though, Yaldabaoth remains
present in all Sarkic culture, even if the

03:39:34.120 --> 03:39:36.790
religion doesn’t exactly worship the god
itself.

03:39:36.790 --> 03:39:43.270
Yaldabaoth was a destroyer, who fed upon gods,
worlds, and stars, who incidentally created

03:39:43.270 --> 03:39:48.490
the entire universe and life itself as a result
of its power-hungry actions.

03:39:48.490 --> 03:39:54.069
The creation stories talk of Yaldabaoth as
a blind entity, driven solely by instinct,

03:39:54.069 --> 03:39:56.890
fueled by the forces of primordial chaos.

03:39:56.890 --> 03:40:03.120
As life was created as a result of Yaldabaoth’s
existence, it was ultimately unguided by intelligence,

03:40:03.120 --> 03:40:07.490
and its spread throughout the universe was
similar to that of a germ than anything grand

03:40:07.490 --> 03:40:08.670
or divine.

03:40:08.670 --> 03:40:12.910
Ion, upon learning of these myths, came to
the conclusion that the multiverse itself

03:40:12.910 --> 03:40:18.290
was only an altar that held life’s existence,
which was brought into reality for the ultimate

03:40:18.290 --> 03:40:20.750
sacrifice at the hands of Yaldabaoth.

03:40:20.750 --> 03:40:25.670
The entity would one day reclaim all of existence
for itself, harvesting what it created and

03:40:25.670 --> 03:40:30.790
consuming it whole, as this was Yaldabaoth’s
nature and purpose as the ultimate being of

03:40:30.790 --> 03:40:31.840
the cosmos.

03:40:31.840 --> 03:40:36.560
Ion saw this shared ancestry among life as
the key to genetic modification.

03:40:36.560 --> 03:40:41.560
As all life was derived from Yaldabaoth, it
held a similar genetic code, and it would

03:40:41.560 --> 03:40:46.410
become the Sarkic right to guide and cultivate
organic matter, stealing the genes of other

03:40:46.410 --> 03:40:49.100
lifeforms or creating entirely new ones.

03:40:49.100 --> 03:40:54.540
Through this perversion of life, Ion felt
he could ascend from something ordinary to

03:40:54.540 --> 03:41:00.000
a living god, fueled by the unending cycle
of sacrifice and creation.

03:41:00.000 --> 03:41:04.310
With his radical, power-hungry beliefs rapidly
spreading throughout the Daevite empire, mostly

03:41:04.310 --> 03:41:08.710
among its slaves, the leading Daeva became
fearful of Ion.

03:41:08.710 --> 03:41:12.800
Attempts to assassinate him or usurp Ion’s
influence were met with failure, and only

03:41:12.800 --> 03:41:18.160
fueled the mission of his followers, furthering
the belief that if they were to achieve godhood,

03:41:18.160 --> 03:41:23.199
they had to overthrow the Daevites, who were
the most present, all-powerful beings in their

03:41:23.199 --> 03:41:24.229
lives.

03:41:24.229 --> 03:41:28.920
This all came to a head when Ion launched
his final act against the Daevite empire.

03:41:28.920 --> 03:41:33.520
After years of sowing the seeds of disharmony
and hate among the slave population, Ion rallied

03:41:33.520 --> 03:41:37.790
his followers and swept them up into a full-scale
rebellion.

03:41:37.790 --> 03:41:43.970
In a short time, Ion overthrew the province
he grew up in, fueled by the rage of his followers,

03:41:43.970 --> 03:41:48.270
who mercilessly razed the city and slaughtered
the Daevites like animals.

03:41:48.270 --> 03:41:52.710
Those who were present could see the inspiration
Ion brought to his followers, how he commanded

03:41:52.710 --> 03:41:54.680
them as if he were a living god.

03:41:54.680 --> 03:41:59.580
How he used the reality-bending magic of the
Daeva and turned it against them, with his

03:41:59.580 --> 03:42:04.050
followers utilizing anomalous warfare in a
horrific, gruesome way.

03:42:04.050 --> 03:42:09.140
Flesh was turned into a weapon, living beings
were contorted and transformed into monstrosities

03:42:09.140 --> 03:42:12.540
and abominations that fueled the Sarkic war
machine.

03:42:12.540 --> 03:42:17.570
Daeva thaumaturgy simply could not compete
against the permeating, powerful, and unrestricted

03:42:17.570 --> 03:42:20.170
abilities of Ion’s followers.

03:42:20.170 --> 03:42:25.700
Before long, the city fell before the being
who had, in that moment of bloodlust and fury,

03:42:25.700 --> 03:42:27.520
achieved apotheosis.

03:42:27.520 --> 03:42:32.380
The being who was now known as the Grand Karcist
Ion.

03:42:32.380 --> 03:42:36.870
The Grand Karcist and his followers rampaged
throughout the ancient world, felling cities

03:42:36.870 --> 03:42:41.670
and entire empires to serve as stepping stones
in their path to godhood.

03:42:41.670 --> 03:42:46.270
Their weapons and armor were unlike anything
else at the time, and their utilization of

03:42:46.270 --> 03:42:50.180
powerful, flesh-bending magic made them unstoppable
on the field of battle.

03:42:50.180 --> 03:42:56.380
The city of Adytum was established as the
Sarkic holy city, where Ion ruled as the Sorcerer-King

03:42:56.380 --> 03:42:57.989
as a living deity.

03:42:57.989 --> 03:43:02.140
Texts from this period suggest that Ion had
somehow usurped control of Yaldabaoth the

03:43:02.140 --> 03:43:08.109
Devourer itself, wearing the flesh of the
Old God as a sort of armor, and crafting a

03:43:08.109 --> 03:43:09.810
kingdom from its body.

03:43:09.810 --> 03:43:14.310
While this depiction is most likely only a
metaphor for how much Ion resembled Yaldabaoth

03:43:14.310 --> 03:43:19.189
in philosophy and pure power, the image of
a living god devouring and succeeding the

03:43:19.189 --> 03:43:24.460
old one is a striking visual that surely empowered
many Sarkics at the time.

03:43:24.460 --> 03:43:29.240
Another story from Sarkic mythology during
this period is “The Six Ordeals of Ion”,

03:43:29.240 --> 03:43:34.920
a parable that told of six challenges that
were issued to Ion by the Archons, the servants

03:43:34.920 --> 03:43:38.760
of Yaldabaoth, who challenged the newly crowned
king of Adytum.

03:43:38.760 --> 03:43:43.540
By enduring their trials, Ion mastered the
rituals, practices, and beliefs ubiquitous

03:43:43.540 --> 03:43:48.409
to Sarkicism and broke free from the bondage
of mortal limitations.

03:43:48.409 --> 03:43:52.729
But the authenticity of this myth is debated,
and the nature of the ordeals and Ion’s

03:43:52.729 --> 03:43:55.520
further relationship with Yaldabaoth remains
unknown.

03:43:55.520 --> 03:44:00.930
But why did the Grand Karcist Ion, with his
flowing red robes and wielding his all-powerful

03:44:00.930 --> 03:44:06.510
staff, who twisted flesh and drew blood when
he so much as drew breath, fall into such

03:44:06.510 --> 03:44:12.029
obscurity that his religion remains a mysterious
and obscure footnote in the Foundation’s

03:44:12.029 --> 03:44:13.029
archives?

03:44:13.029 --> 03:44:17.770
If the Sarkics were as powerful as these early
texts state, where are they today?

03:44:17.770 --> 03:44:22.600
Why did the horrific city of Adytum, built
of living, organic material that stood monument

03:44:22.600 --> 03:44:25.279
to Ion’s indomitable will, fall?

03:44:25.279 --> 03:44:31.850
In Sarkicism’s golden age, from 1600 and
1200 BCE, the religion’s permeation was

03:44:31.850 --> 03:44:33.040
inescapable.

03:44:33.040 --> 03:44:38.319
Like the diseases they wielded in their wars,
Sarkicism spread like a contagion across the

03:44:38.319 --> 03:44:39.319
world.

03:44:39.319 --> 03:44:43.659
Everywhere they went, they assimilated tribes
and villages into their ranks, fighting under

03:44:43.659 --> 03:44:46.590
the banner of Adytum and the Sarkic faith.

03:44:46.590 --> 03:44:52.210
This expanded empire would be referred to
as Kalmaktama, or the “Deathless”.

03:44:52.210 --> 03:44:57.470
Many tried to defeat these brutal invaders,
including the king of the Hittite empire himself,

03:44:57.470 --> 03:44:58.840
but all fell before them.

03:44:58.840 --> 03:45:04.040
As the Kalmaktama Empire attempted to establish
a foothold in the Mediterranean, invading

03:45:04.040 --> 03:45:09.620
and colonizing the islands of Cyprus, Crete,
and Gyaros, for the first time in Sarkic history,

03:45:09.620 --> 03:45:13.010
the tides of war began to turn against the
religion.

03:45:13.010 --> 03:45:18.510
A coalition of kingdoms was formed in response
to the Sarkic threat, created by the Egyptians,

03:45:18.510 --> 03:45:24.620
Greeks, Minoans, Canaanites, Assyrians, and
most importantly, the Mekhanites, who were

03:45:24.620 --> 03:45:27.340
the followers of the Church of the Broken
God.

03:45:27.340 --> 03:45:31.570
The cult of Mekhane, the Broken God, had urged
these kingdoms to unite against the Sarkic

03:45:31.570 --> 03:45:37.670
threat, and now united, outfitted their allies
with superior, Mekhanite technology that anomalously

03:45:37.670 --> 03:45:43.330
enhanced the empires’ war capabilities,
putting them on-par with the Sarkic death-sorcerers.

03:45:43.330 --> 03:45:48.580
And so, a great war was waged between the
Kalmaktama Empire and the Coalition of Kingdoms.

03:45:48.580 --> 03:45:52.819
The details of such are largely lost to time,
but the war itself was fought with the full

03:45:52.819 --> 03:45:57.609
power of the Sarkics and the Mekhanites clashing
with one another, and its consequences left

03:45:57.609 --> 03:45:59.390
an imprint on the earth itself.

03:45:59.390 --> 03:46:05.530
A death toll that estimates place at 20 to
30 million, mass graves, anomalous weapons,

03:46:05.530 --> 03:46:09.830
and even the deployment of giant, mechanical
beings created by the Mekhanites known as

03:46:09.830 --> 03:46:14.180
“Colossi” that rampaged through Sarkic
settlements and cities.

03:46:14.180 --> 03:46:19.540
Though the battle was costly on both sides,
the Kalmaktama Empire fell to the Coalition,

03:46:19.540 --> 03:46:24.090
and the once impenetrable city of Adytum was
destroyed, forever.

03:46:24.090 --> 03:46:28.279
Sarkicism would fall into obscurity, and the
empire would be forgotten, possibly because

03:46:28.279 --> 03:46:32.800
it was much easier than remembering the horrors
Ion subjected the world to.

03:46:32.800 --> 03:46:36.990
The Grand Karcist himself disappeared, his
whereabouts unknown shortly after the fall

03:46:36.990 --> 03:46:38.120
of Adytum.

03:46:38.120 --> 03:46:42.359
Some said he had ascended into godhood, leaving
the world behind.

03:46:42.359 --> 03:46:46.510
Others said he was slain in battle, nothing
more than a man who believed he would never

03:46:46.510 --> 03:46:47.510
die.

03:46:47.510 --> 03:46:51.330
The Sarkic religion was effectively extinguished
from the world, never to be seen again.

03:46:51.330 --> 03:46:55.330
Or so, that’s what the coalition was led
to believe.

03:46:55.330 --> 03:47:01.029
Though the empire and Adytum fell, and Ion
disappeared, an idea as tantalizing and powerful

03:47:01.029 --> 03:47:03.800
as Sarkicism is difficult to snuff out entirely.

03:47:03.800 --> 03:47:09.569
In reality, Sarkicism would continue in secret,
in both its homeland in the Urals and among

03:47:09.569 --> 03:47:13.020
the offshoot tribes that had fought under
Adytum’s banner.

03:47:13.020 --> 03:47:18.220
These sects of Sarkicism would practice their
beliefs in their war-ravaged homeland, which

03:47:18.220 --> 03:47:23.720
suffered a great collapse, resulting in the
fall of kingdoms, a crisis of refugees, and

03:47:23.720 --> 03:47:28.040
a decline of art, literature, science, and
technology.

03:47:28.040 --> 03:47:32.670
Lingering disease and famine from Sarkic biological
weapons spread even to the kingdoms of the

03:47:32.670 --> 03:47:37.370
coalition, resulting in an event historians
refer to as the Late Bronze Age Collapse.

03:47:37.370 --> 03:47:42.080
The empire that was once Deathless had now
fallen, but its followers remained, practicing

03:47:42.080 --> 03:47:46.040
their power-craving rituals in secret and
without centralization.

03:47:46.040 --> 03:47:51.170
This led to a Sarkic diaspora, where various
sects and Sarkic cults, each with culturally

03:47:51.170 --> 03:47:54.500
distinct beliefs, would crop up throughout
the Eurasian continent.

03:47:54.500 --> 03:47:59.659
While the Foundation is unsure of the specifics
of these cults’ activities and beliefs,

03:47:59.659 --> 03:48:04.720
elements of Sarkicism would soon begin to
permeate the upper echelon of society.

03:48:04.720 --> 03:48:09.300
Infiltrating Carpathian cults or sought out
by nobles themselves, who ignored the rumors

03:48:09.300 --> 03:48:13.580
of devil worship and witchcraft to seek out
Sarkic power for their courts.

03:48:13.580 --> 03:48:17.899
The tempting power that Sarkicism granted
made it a popular choice to be practiced in

03:48:17.899 --> 03:48:22.811
secret by upper-ranking royals and even entire
noble families.

03:48:22.811 --> 03:48:27.199
From their position of power, where they had
access to knowledge, influence, and a fresh

03:48:27.199 --> 03:48:31.199
supply of sacrifices, Sarkicism endured.

03:48:31.199 --> 03:48:35.450
Over time, this would result in the formation
of Sarkic “Great Houses”, where families

03:48:35.450 --> 03:48:41.149
practiced their own interpretation of Sarkicism,
the religion that was now mutated into hundreds

03:48:41.149 --> 03:48:44.900
upon hundreds of variations and subcultures.

03:48:44.900 --> 03:48:49.529
These great houses would focus on individualism,
and applying their powers to fulfill their

03:48:49.529 --> 03:48:51.040
self-serving needs.

03:48:51.040 --> 03:48:55.930
Sarkicism, now decentralized completely, would
spread throughout Europe via marriage, as

03:48:55.930 --> 03:49:00.520
a high society of cults and magicians whose
true motives for ruling their kingdoms and

03:49:00.520 --> 03:49:05.880
provinces were kept hidden behind their meaty,
flesh-curtain of absolute secrecy.

03:49:05.880 --> 03:49:10.880
Today, the Sarkic cults persist, and their
anomalies are frequently uncovered by the

03:49:10.880 --> 03:49:11.880
Foundation.

03:49:11.880 --> 03:49:15.920
Understanding them and their religion, however,
is another ordeal entirely, and the majority

03:49:15.920 --> 03:49:19.810
of Sarkic history, culture, and practices
are unknown to the organization.

03:49:19.810 --> 03:49:21.359
But they’re still out there.

03:49:21.359 --> 03:49:26.570
In the highest ranks of urban society, in
the most remote villages of the world.

03:49:26.570 --> 03:49:29.870
There will always be those who crave to wield
flesh.

03:49:29.870 --> 03:49:36.710
The followers of Ion who hope to achieve Apotheosis,
however they may believe they can do so.

03:49:36.710 --> 03:49:40.620
Though the details remain unclear, there is
one thing the Foundation has realized over

03:49:40.620 --> 03:49:49.970
its years of studying the religion: Sarkicism
has, and always will, remain.

